{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | sed -n '103,160p;448,552p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-LOG.md | sed -n '119,220p'\"","aggregated_output":"   103\t## Future evidence scoring (D372)\n   104\t\n   105\tAlex decided future gold scoring should measure helpful versus not helpful evidence without requiring separate scores for core and supporting. Use frozen golden-v5 as-is: combine core and supporting as helpful, treat not-kept as unhelpful, and keep optional entries neutral. A counting report has not yet been implemented. Historical scores retain their original definitions. D373 removes the stop caused by a separate concern about three question-gold entries: keep the gold unchanged, continue scoring and disclose the concern; see `../hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-parallel-refinement/ruler-conflict-2026-11-05.zh.md`.\n   106\t\n   107\t## Latest decision (D369)\n   108\t\n   109\tAlex decided in D369 to capture core and supporting evidence without a strict boundary and in D370 to remove the 22 preset starting questions and separate earnings-report import. The replay entry now defaults to `poc-v118` (D374), refuses old seeded ledgers and baseline configurations, and continues to read existing non-seeded questions; earnings releases remain normal source items. This change has local contract tests but has not passed end-to-end product acceptance. The frozen historical rulers and results remain unchanged.\n   110\t\n   111\tThe small 2026-11-05 study used three archived NVDA articles and an 8/28 historical 68-question snapshot: without versus with an appended report, independent AI review found 14/27 versus 13/27 complete matters. This measured appended extraction context, not the distinct former coverage-start step; D370 removes both by Alex's decision. Full traces and limitations are in the separate `hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review` worktree under `docs/research/2026-11-05-real-input-evidence/existing-library-results-2026-11-05.md`.\n   112\t\n   113\t\n   114\t**One-day smoke completed (2026-11-05 UTC):** Alex requested a quick 1–2 day end-to-end test. One day, 2026-08-29, ran in `/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/poc/data/v117-one-day-smoke-2026-11-05/`: config v117, an 8/28 historical library, 40 extraction calls, 93 evidence records written, four new questions, 54 judged and zero terminal failures. Two judgement attempts were refused and corrected. A Microsoft revenue forecast of $391.1bn was assigned to a rung whose upper bound excludes $391.1bn; the same article's actual quarterly revenue and next-quarter guidance were dropped with no home. Some source dates and bodies are not verified, and an independent 14-article sample review was incomplete due to truncated text. This is not semantic or production acceptance. Findings and scope: `docs/research/2026-11-05-real-input-evidence/one-day-v117-smoke-2026-11-05.zh.md` in that worktree. The clean source-text comparison and its condition-hidden review are complete; council discussion of next steps is ongoing.\n   115\t\n   116\t**D371, in progress:** Alex directed that present and forward-looking revenue and financial information should be tracked. Diagnose the same-day extraction and filing losses before designing a general change. No new financial tracking implementation has been accepted yet. The old frozen standard and gold are unchanged. The original prompt-only pilot failed design review. The user approved an exact prompt addition for an experiment; it is not a production implementation. Four paired real-article diagnostic calls per arm completed for the exact approved sentence: v74i versus experimental role-d371-pilot. Microsoft next-quarter guidance and NVIDIA FY2028 guidance still dropped in the treatment; a single draw is not acceptance or proof of causation. Details: docs/research/2026-11-05-real-input-evidence/d371-prompt-pilot-results.zh.md (isolated worktree). The requested full prompt audit and restructure were drafted experimentally; five real-article paired diagnostic requests per arm completed. Microsoft revenue guidance was missed in both arms, and the draft produced unsupported original dates, a quote refusal and suspect links. No production prompt change or acceptance; see restructure-pilot-results.zh.md in the isolated worktree.\n   117\t\n   118\t**Clean Step 1 coverage council (2026-11-06):** Codex and Claude Code independently reviewed the existing attempts and completed three discussion rounds. The proposed next research candidate moves the existing evidence-reading block ahead of the thesis-opening block while preserving the article, open-thesis state and paired output. It is a hypothesis, not an implemented or validated fix. A complete prompt/contract audit and independent review precede any controlled Luna comparison. Historical paragraph-based and source-first experiments, their noise and attribution problems, and the rejected overlap-based merge are recorded in [the council review](../clean-arch/STEP1-COVERAGE-COUNCIL.md). No new Luna experiment was run in the council.\n   119\t\n   120\t**Clean Step 1 coverage order result (2026-11-07):** The isolated 54-call clean comparison completed and all answers were reviewed blind. Moving the evidence-reading block recovered a known Kyber report and denial in one of three candidate answers against none in three controls, with attribution blur; it also produced unsupported gaming-to-AI links in two candidate answers and no controls. It is not adopted. A separate exact-quote example misattributes an executive's prediction in the standalone summary. [Results and replay](../clean-arch/STEP1-COVERAGE-ORDER-RESULTS.md) record all selected cases, uncertainties and source-fidelity work; no production ledger was written.\n   121\t\n   122\t**Clean Step 1 fidelity council (2026-11-07):** Codex and Claude Code completed five rounds on source attribution, conditions, dates and meaning. No tested fix or root cause is established. The agreed source-to-record review of 49 articles / 160 evidence items and the subsequent isolated field-order comparison are complete; the later 54-answer / 217-record repeated sample remains separate. Prior source-first, quote-first and follow-up-review experiments and their limits are recorded in [the fidelity council](../clean-arch/STEP1-FIDELITY-COUNCIL.md). No Luna experiment or production change was made in this council.\n   123\t\n   124\t**Clean Step 1 fidelity review (2026-11-07):** All 49 saved source packets and 160 original evidence items have received a source-and-record review; focused independent cross-checks cover the findings and selected controls. The [review and article replay](../clean-arch/STEP1-FIDELITY-REVIEW.md) distinguish source contamination and missing source material from model meaning, citation, date and link issues. The [isolated schema property-order diagnostic](../clean-arch/STEP1-CITATION-ORDER-RESULTS.md) completed all 66 calls and condition-blinded article reviews. Several omissions and semantic errors persisted; it did not establish a fix and is not adopted. It used saved articles and before-states without changing production.\n   125\t\n   126\t**Clean Step 1 source handoff council (2026-11-07):** The ongoing [council and offline checks](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-HANDOFF-COUNCIL.md) reconstructed 16 matching article-34 controls, all omitting a Kyber report and denial; the cause remains unknown. The 20-article saved source-role overlap review distinguished previously cited AI-generated summary lines and an unrelated recommendation from authored body. The clean runner does not send the saved source-role labels; the council chose to first compare original and previously selected source text on ten known articles. The isolated 60-call source-text comparison and condition-hidden review are complete; [results](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-TEXT-RESULTS.md) show specific contamination reductions alongside persistent omissions and changed meaning. It did not advance state or write production. The isolated six-article low-versus-medium source-fidelity diagnostic completed 36/36 calls and condition-hidden review. [Results](../clean-arch/STEP1-REASONING-FIDELITY-RESULTS.md) show partial improvements alongside persistent source-qualification and attribution concerns; no production setting is changed. The [prompt audit](../clean-arch/STEP1-FIDELITY-PROMPT-AUDIT.md) maps the observed failures to the full request and signed standard. The six-article isolated schema-description comparison completed 36/36 calls and condition-hidden review; the candidate did not preserve the repeated example qualification and is not adopted. [Results](../clean-arch/STEP1-SUMMARY-FIDELITY-RESULTS.md). A further six-article 36-call low-versus-medium comparison used corpus-cleaned sources outside the original 49-item clean replay and a fixed exploratory context; results were mixed, including unsupported links and incorrect attribution/date fields. [Results and replay](../clean-arch/STEP1-ADDITIONAL-SOURCES-RESULTS.md). The structured-claims candidate was not sent after review revealed scope and complexity concerns. Council review of the next action is ongoing. The date-text schema-description diagnostic completed 48/48 calls on eight known cases, with mixed results; the candidate is not adopted. A selected-run census found twelve literal \"null\" strings in date-text fields, but no production writer impact is established. [Results and replay](../clean-arch/STEP1-DATE-DESCRIPTION-RESULTS.md). A further preregistered eight-source date comparison completed 48/48 calls; the candidate lost a supported company-article statement date in all three draws on one source and is not adopted. [Results and replay](../clean-arch/STEP1-DATE-NEW-SOURCES-RESULTS.md). A bounded corpus census confirmed 163 source pages across three explicit generated-summary structures whose labels were removed while some summary text was retained; two NVIDIA cases were reproduced through the cleaner. [Source provenance investigation](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-PROVENANCE-CENSUS.md). A read-only source-lineage replay reproduced 363/363 cleaned pages with current inputs, preserved ambiguous original-line locations, and surfaced the generated-summary label loss for review. [Source investigation and lineage replay](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-PROVENANCE-CENSUS.md). An offline neighboring-context observation exposed only 144 or 149 of 163 known labels and introduced many other page lines; it is not adopted as a general source fix. [Observations and viewer](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-CONTEXT-OBSERVATIONS.md). A new [saved-quote integrity investigation](../clean-arch/STEP1-QUOTE-INTEGRITY-CENSUS.md) reconstructed 360 saved answers across eight overlapping cohorts, including 78 prepared-source calls. Five saved unverified passage instances were complete matches under the existing normalization; an in-memory candidate recovered their original slices, while ten others remained unverified. The normalized source-slice lookup is now installed only in the isolated clean Step 1 runner; saved-answer and entry-point checks are recorded there. Page provenance, Unicode completeness, production resource budgets and writer integration remain open. The existing writer stores only one quote, whereas 63 of 160 evidence items in the 49-article exploratory trace have multiple passages. A [source-first 49-article coverage review](../clean-arch/STEP1-COVERAGE-CENSUS.md) separates material missing from the model input from source-visible omissions in the saved answers, with uncertain matter boundaries labeled. (Superseded: the next investigation then was why supplied material is missed; the current next task is under \"One next task\".) The canonical prompt and production configuration remain unchanged. Adding fallible role annotations remains a separate untested candidate. Council streams and handoffs are in `poc/data/clean-step1-ongoing-council-2026-11-07/`.\n   127\t\n   128\t## What runs\n   129\t\n   130\t- **Nothing is live.** The two-week run of D563 finished on 2026-11-16 at 01:23 local (`poc/data/clean-carried-run-2026-11-16/`, draw\n   131\t  complete, ledger $3.476 of $6.00); its readings are recorded (D564, [result](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/carried-run/RESULT.md));\n   132\t  the six contested last answers are being traced at $0 (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/contested-six/`).\n   133\t- **Pipeline (replay default `poc/config/poc-v118.json`, D370, D374).** Every item reads the relevant open questions from the library at the start of its day, then extraction v74i on `gpt-6-luna` proposes evidence and questions; Jev matching with the collision judge matches them; code writes the records; judging-v7 judges changes once a day; pull mode closes due questions. There is no separate seed or coverage-start report import, and reports as source items remain eligible. This default has not completed end-to-end acceptance. The [pipeline guide](poc/pipeline-plan.md) maps stages to code.\n   134\t- **Measured:** one company (NVDA) over one 14-day window (2026-07-01 to 07-14), the judgement scored at the window end on the frozen ruler (AGENTS §7.1). Three draws of `poc-v116` against three of `poc-v108` run in the same hours: 53 against 45 agreements of 57; operating margin and capex agree in 3 of 3 draws, never judged without the coverage-start reading ([acceptance](research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/acceptance-design.md)).\n   135\t- **Served data:** the service, the MCP server and the standalone page serve the sealed three-month ledger `served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828` (68 theses, 34 groups; D358), built by the earlier `poc-v34` pipeline, not by the replay default. HTTP `/library`, MCP `thesis_library` and the standalone page share the dated bundle writer.\n   136\t- **Idea API:** `poc-v118-idea` (D290, D335, D374): two discovery calls and one adoption and weighting assessment; only adopted theses with positive weights appear, and nonempty plans total 100%. The [Idea contract](poc/idea-card.md) owns its fields and the limits of its scores.\n   137\t- **Interface:** the Thesis Library and Explore Ideas workspaces, with the confidence Trigger and an Action preview (no wallet connection or order execution). The [UI specification](poc/thesis-ui.md) and the [integration guide](../poc/ui/README.md) own its behaviour.\n   138\t- **Repository:** `main` holds the product, the frozen ruler and the research records; run databases, logs and model archives stay on disk (D353), located by the [data manifest](research/2026-10-25-english/data-manifest.md). Worktrees: `/Users/lchingen/hivemind` is the main checkout, where slice branches are cut from `main`; `/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28` (the extraction branch, merged on 2026-11-03) keeps in its ignored folders the stored end-to-end runs of `poc-v91` to `poc-v95` that later comparisons read (D359); `/Users/lchingen/hivemind-run-v109-2026-11-04` is the finished judging-v8 run's worktree. Older branches stay in Git without worktrees (D359); none is merged work in progress. The clean source-text comparison and its condition-hidden review are complete; council discussion of next steps is ongoing.\n   139\t\n   140\t## Open defects\n   141\t\n   142\t1. **Competitor and customer news is filed under the company's revenue questions** instead of the share, capital-spending or custom-chip question it informs (D355; filing is otherwise about 85% right). Share facts are often not written at all, an extraction recall miss. The total-revenue question holds about a quarter of all links (D354).\n   143\t2. **One bet opened twice** about one encounter in five: the collision judge splits a seed question from an identical candidate on a fine detail (D354).\n   144\t3. **A question the standard rules out** (the lidar legislation) was proposed by the extraction and opened in one draw of three (D354).\n   145\t4. **A thesis opened from an article gets no dependency of its own**: the default Jev matching asks for none (`views/jev_matching.py`), although D51 has the matching call choose them; themes still reach every company thesis through the theme block (D191, D195). Found in the 2026-11-05 consolidation; building it is decided (D368).\n   146\t5. **Historical coverage-start reading, retired by D370** (D364–D366): the capital-spending line is missed in about one read in six (the question is then left as it was); a labelled guidance figure is written with the fact tier; later reports reach the questions only through the daily stream; `scripts/preflight.py` does not replay the reading's check.\n   147\t6. **Measured on one company and one 14-day window**, the judgement scored at the window end only; no version of the current pipeline has completed a longer window (a 60-day run of `poc-v108` was stopped at Alex's word after 2026-07-15, [log row 8](research/2026-11-04-argument-record/log.md)). The China-share question (v17) swings between draws (0 of 3 in the acceptance, 2 of 3 in its control, 1 of 3 in the frozen draws): two readers found the starting figures did not cause the acceptance's drop, and the byte-identical extraction request kept a \"share fell to zero\" sentence in two candidate draws and dropped it in two control draws. One acceptance draw judged nothing on v16; its cause is not established.\n   148\t7. **What a judgement reads grows with the window** (D358). Argument records (D201) were measured as the remedy on 2026-11-04 and not built: judging-v8 agreed 12 of 17 against 15 of 17, judging-v9's card added little at about half again the judging cost; their code was removed at Alex's request ([log rows 4–11](research/2026-11-04-argument-record/log.md)).\n   149\t8. **Seen once, not traced.** A judgement named a shown theme as a dependency and the check refused it twice, stopping a draw for a day (2026-11-02, D266). The sealed run's review recorded that a succession's opening evidence is not linked to the new question (D358), not yet checked against today's code.\n   150\t9. **Earlier defects, unchanged.** Matching (build log row 49): another document's copy of a figure can be treated as new evidence; one matter can occupy several groups; same-answer candidate references caused seven chain or duplication decisions of the generative matcher; empty `original_who` values can count as the same party; different names for one population cause two of nine Jev merge misses. Nine 2026 aggregate-spending theses under `ai-capex` each have a different population; whether to combine them is a product choice. Extraction's instructions remain narrower than the PRD's important-question rule and omit the personal-memo exception, and extraction can change a quantity's meaning before matching (a guarantee amount against financing provided). Classification keeps its [recorded simulation defects](research/2026-10-25-english/classification-existing-defects.txt). The corpus audit recorded 97 official notices with 56 body and file-name collisions, to re-fetch before relying on a rebuilt corpus. An older intermittent search-test failure is untraced. Fresh Idea allocations vary while saved weights do not; the confidence chart applies the current plan to past states and is not a calibrated probability; broad analyst-prose quality and fresh Idea stability remain unaccepted (the [Idea contract](poc/idea-card.md) lists its limits); generative matching dependencies await `matching-v4`. The readers' doubts about the frozen standard, listed in the [extraction branch's state page](research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/current-state-extraction-branch-2026-11-03.md), remain for Alex.\n   151\t\n   152\tUpstream supply and the human review pool's output remain deferred.\n   153\t\n   154\t10. **A new-system store being written serves its first day in progress** (D573, D574; `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/page-contract/LIVE-READ-DESIGN.md`, B):\n   155\t   before any day completes, the service's default date falls back to the latest judgement's day. Not built: a correct guard needs one\n   156\t   snapshot for the check and the read, MCP's start and the streamed Idea response handled; 0 of 143 stores are in that state and no\n   157\t   new-system store is served live today.\n   158\t\n   159\t## One next task\n   160\t\n   448\t**The one next task: none open (D689, D690, 2026-11-20).** poc-v118 is the product (Alex chose A, D690), and the research line\n   449\trests until his new direction. The hybrid's release line is paused, and the judge and c8 lines are closed for now. A line reopens only\n   450\ton its condition below. No paid send is open, and D439 has $0 available without Alex's word.\n   451\t- **D689 (Alex chose option 1; council N closed both lines; record:\n   452\t  [council-n-codex.md](research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-n-codex.md), [council-n2-codex.md](research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-n2-codex.md)).**\n   453\t  - **Judge.** The carried previous conclusion holds rejected forecasts: on full evidence, 0 of 13 move with it and 8 of 13 without it,\n   454\t    with 0 of 8 controls moving.\n   455\t    - The readers jointly support 4 net repairs against the 5 required, including M14 in two of three old draws.\n   456\t    - The frozen gold reads 44.3 against 45.0, with China share regressed.\n   457\t    - It reopens on eight eligible failures on fresh questions, which the design never read and are counted once across draws, with\n   458\t      matched controls and a source-checked summary of the omitted facts (D198 option 2). Then the D198 choice and its price go to\n   459\t      Alex.\n   460\t  - **c8.** It showed no improvement in the final answers tested, and adds about $24 to old's about $9 over 82 days. It reopens on a\n   461\t    traced decisive fact that old missed, c8 delivers, and that could change a named final answer.\n   462\t  - **Spend (an error of mine).** \"Inside D439's $40\" was written in D679, D682 and D684 with no tally. D439 stands at about $39.65 or\n   463\t    $44.42 under the two readings. Phase 1's ledger is $2.64, not $2.4.\n   464\t- **History of this line (D681–D688)** follows. Alex opened the hybrid's build and\n   465\ttest, and asked that problems not be found only at the end (his words are in the D681 record). Plan: [PLAN.md](research/2026-11-20-hybrid/PLAN.md). Design:\n   466\t[DESIGN-J2.md](research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md).\n   467\t- **Where old loses on the 32 matters:**\n   468\t  - it never opens 17;\n   469\t  - it opened M08 and M14 in 3/3 draws, but the judge reasoned wrongly: amounts that overlap were added, and a figure of another scope\n   470\t    was taken as the answer.\n   471\t- **Census:** 24 answers rejected by both readers ([CENSUS.md](research/2026-11-20-hybrid/census/CENSUS.md)).\n   472\t- **Found at $0:** the judge writes the rung first and its reference and derivation last (`schema_for` appends the stance fields to\n   473\t  the end of `properties`).\n   474\t- **Arms:**\n   475\t  - J2a, the schema order only;\n   476\t  - J2b, J2a plus an overlap and scope check.\n   477\t- **The probe and its rule** are written before any J2 send. Its regression guard is the frozen judgement gold: the stored v7 requests\n   478\t  give 15/17, 15/17 and 16/17, and are rebuilt byte for byte.\n   479\t- **Status (D685):**\n   480\t  - **The judge line is paused within D198.** Four angles have failed:\n   481\t    - J2a and J2b fail the locked blind reading;\n   482\t    - removing the previous conclusion misses its screen by one, and the frozen gold reads 44.3 against 45.0;\n   483\t    - H1, the heading only, gives 0 net repairs against 2 in council J's blind diagnostic.\n   484\t  - The carried derivation holds the rejected rungs. Every remaining lever changes D198.\n   485\t  - **No fresh test exists on this corpus.** The judge's errors sit in about ten numeric bets the design has read; 27 fresh bets gave\n   486\t    1 target against 8 needed.\n   487\t- **Opening census (D686):** [OPENING-CENSUS.md](research/2026-11-20-hybrid/OPENING-CENSUS.md). Of the 16 matters old never opens:\n   488\t  - 6 are merged into a held question, because the scoring list is finer than D197 and D248;\n   489\t  - 5 fall outside the library's NVIDIA-only subject;\n   490\t  - 5, plus M05, are never proposed, though D248 allows them; a fix needs a new extraction version (D274).\n   491\t- **D382 answered (D687; his words are in the record):** in the hybrid, a company's own material figure keeps its own question, as\n   492\t  old's opening does.\n   493\t- **Attainable check (D688, council M):** [OPENING-CENSUS.md](research/2026-11-20-hybrid/OPENING-CENSUS.md), last two sections.\n   494\t  - The census found no credible path to a D665 lead through opening changes alone.\n   495\t  - The concrete misses within Alex's rules are M20 (a $125B unsigned obligation, D388) and M05. M09, M30 and M25 are coin flips.\n   496\t  - Noise costs about 1.4.\n   497\t  - What binds: the list counts finer than D248/D388 on 9 matters, the NVIDIA-only subject on 5, and D198 on 2.\n   498\t  - No opening test is sent.\n   499\t- **D688's recommendation, answered by D689:** keep poc-v118 as production and pause the hybrid's release line. Questions on other\n   500\t  research-list companies' key figures are offered only for their own value. Spend: phase 1 $2.64 of $3 (ledger); `phase1b` $0.36 of\n   501\t  $2.\n   502\t\n   503\t**Earlier next task, closed by D676 and D677 (D665–D675): read the release comparison's six draws when they finish, with the council-reviewed tools**\n   504\t(`docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v12.md` §1.4–§1.6; `DESIGN-1.6.md` v7; D675).\n   505\t\n   506\t- **Done:**\n   507\t  - stage 0 and slice 2;\n   508\t  - the full run, six draws, launched together at 22:36 on 2026-11-17 under `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/`;\n   509\t  - every reading instrument built and passed by the council before any output was read: reading tools in round 5, the §1.6 tools in\n   510\t    round 10; the scorer hardened through Codex rounds 11–21 (D675); 101 stage0 tests, 75 mutants on the reading tools.\n   511\t- **Result, 2026-11-19 (diagnostic, 5 draws; Alex stopped new-1).** The new system loses on the release comparison.\n   512\t  - Of 32 key matters, the new system serves 2–3 and the old one 10 (a = 0, b = 7–8). The controls pass.\n   513\t  - Even a perfect new-1 could not reverse it.\n   514\t  - The new libraries miss the core revenue, margin and capex matters.\n   515\t  - Details: `docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-LOG.md`, `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/`.\n   516\t  - **Diagnosed (D676, council):** D382's figure exclusion plus the Step 1→ladder bundled-question loss (D432). Even repaired, the new system ties at best. The old system stays; no further comparison run.\n   517\t  - **The goal loop is closed (D677, council).** The old system stays and no paid work continues. It reopens only if Alex reverses D505\n   518\t    or funds a full run, with a written path to passing first.\n   519\t  - **The one-outcome probe failed its line 1** (`docs/research/2026-11-19-one-outcome-probe/RESULT.md`): it fixes the period bundles\n   520\t    but not the deal bundles.\n   521\t  - **What a pass would take** ($0 arithmetic on the frozen list; pass = a − b ≥ 5 and a ≥ 2b):\n   522\t    - **Under D382:** the old system keeps 4 figure matters the new one can never take, so b ≥ 4. The new system would need at least 9\n   523\t      matters only it serves, out of the 14 its rules allow that the old system misses: 6 shared quantities, 5 obligations and 3\n   524\t      policy steps. Today it serves 0–1 of them.\n   525\t    - **With D382 reversed:** at least 5 of 17, the 14 plus 3 figures the old system misses, provided it also matches the old system on\n   526\t      the rest.\n   527\t    - **Either way:** passing needs much broader opening, not a wording fix.\n   528\t- **(Superseded) When all six draws end, in this order:**\n   529\t  1. `eligibility.py`: six complete draws, launched within 1 h, sends within 72 h.\n   530\t  2. `mapping.py export`, then `read`, `third`, `result`.\n   531\t  3. `mark_cards.py deck`, then `mark`, `debate 1`, `debate 2`, `readings`.\n   532\t  4. `score_comparison.py <run root> <mapping out> <marks folder>`: rebuilds every derived file from the primary data (refuses any that\n   533\t     differs, the readings record included) and gives the verdict and the printed-beside quantities on the rebuilt snapshot.\n   534\t  5. `d400_code_check.py` and `step2_lines.py`: the hard checks and the release status.\n   535\t  6. `d400_reader_lines.py` and `d431_reading.py`: printed beside.\n   536\t  7. A council loop on the result, and a row in `TRIES.md`.\n   537\t- **If a draw stops:** no release verdict; a diagnostic export (plan §1.4 item 10).\n   538\t- **If the verdict is not a practical lead:** the council-loop skill on the traces, and the next try from another angle (D674).\n   539\t- **Monitored** in `RUN-LOG.md`. Out-of-scope findings go to `FINDINGS.md`.\n   540\t- **Held** (D662): answer-choice changes, model trials, and live-store, planner and integration work. D658 waits (D664).\n   541\t- **Open:** D661 (past Codex readers ran with memories on); D656's listing omission; the 589 uncommitted paths (his call).\n   542\t\n   543\t**After D638:** the stop hook rejected the hold, so the council opened D612's fourth condition with a new candidate, astra with arm A2\n   544\t(D436's second-side sentences; D639).\n   545\t- **Two readings,** both VOID by their planted listing controls (D640, D641).\n   546\t- **Descriptive only:**\n   547\t  - A2 wrote H20 2 of 2 where the frozen arm declined 2 of 2, unflagged by both product reviewers;\n   548\t  - memory is disputed;\n   549\t  - agreed hard-line failures frozen 2 against A2 0;\n   550\t  - the listing harm is unmeasured.\n   551\t- **Its status:** astra with A2 stays provisional and unadopted, and the route stops.\n   552\t\n   119\t    - It was spliced into a copy, `new-1/step1-patched/trace.sqlite`, which now has 1884 of 1884 rows complete. The originals are kept.\n   120\t    - Backups were made of `run.json` and the ledger (`*.bak-20261119-before-single-item`).\n   121\t    - The ledger stop was cleared, Step 1 marked completed in `step1-patched`, and new-1 relaunched normally at 12:40. Step 2 started.\n   122\t    - **This departs from D449's whole-component redo, on Alex's instruction.**\n   123\t  - **The release chain** (`reading-chain.sh`) was restarted and waits for new-1. Before its deck it sets the diagnostic deck key aside.\n   124\t- 2026-11-19 ~13:40: **DIAGNOSTIC result on the five finished draws** (`reading-diagnostic/diagnostic-count.json`; not a release verdict).\n   125\t  - **Controls:** all pass. 6/6 plants caught, 4/4 supported controls supported, 3/3 repeats the same.\n   126\t  - **Served matters (N = 32, margin 5):**\n   127\t    | | new | old | a (new only) | b (old only) |\n   128\t    |---|---|---|---|---|\n   129\t    | Counting 1 | 3 | 10 | 0 | 7 |\n   130\t    | Counting 2 | 2 | 10 | 0 | 8 |\n   131\t  - **Best case for the new system if new-1 served every matter served in new-2 or new-3:** new 4–5, old 10, a = 1, b = 6–7. That is\n   132\t    still no lead for the new system, and b − a ≥ 5.\n   133\t  - **What the old system serves and the new one misses:** M04 hyperscaler capex, M06 FY27 data-center revenue, M10 and M11 FY28 margin\n   134\t    and revenue, M17 the Anthropic anchor investment, M18 the FY27 gross margin.\n   135\t  - **What the new system serves:** M13, M15, M31, plus M19 and M32 in one draw only.\n   136\t- 2026-11-19 12:55: **Alex chose \"Stop it now\"**: new-1 cannot change the conclusion.\n   137\t  - new-1's launcher was stopped by SIGTERM in Step 2. Its record shows `crashed`, at $45.29.\n   138\t  - The release chain was stopped too. No process is left.\n   139\t  - **Final paid spend:** about $145 in all.\n   140\t    - Old system: $27.26 for its three draws.\n   141\t    - New system: new-2 $34.66, new-3 $37.64, new-1 $45.29, plus the $0.12 single-item send.\n   142\t  - **The answer stands as the 5-draw diagnostic:** the new system loses (served: new 2–3, old 10).\n   143\t- 2026-11-19 ~13:30: **Why the new system loses.** This is the D674 round's diagnosis, $0, from stored traces and libraries.\n   144\t  - **The new libraries hold no question on the company's own figures.** Of their 33–41 questions, none is on revenue, data-center\n   145\t    revenue, gross margin or hyperscaler capex. They are deals, investments, shipments and regulators. The old libraries open FY27\n   146\t    revenue, FY28 revenue, FY27 data-center revenue, FY27 gross margin and hyperscaler capex from 07-02 to 07-08.\n   147\t  - **The new system extracts the evidence but files no question for it.** new-2's Step 1 extracted 642 evidence items on\n   148\t    revenue, margin or capex; 336 were linked elsewhere and 306 kept unlinked.\n   149\t  - **The cause is the prompt's rule, by decision:**\n   150\t    - D382 (Alex: \"我觉得财务类型不应该是thesis，而更多的是条件…\"): \"a company's own figures are conditions, not questions\".\n   151\t    - D384: \"opens only the big matters\", with class A, the main-driver quantity, left out under D382.\n   152\t    - The week acceptance (2026-09-22..28) already found the same thing: the clean path lacked FY27 and FY28 revenue and the FY28\n   153\t      margin, and its stored reasoning named this do-not-open sentence.\n   154\t  - **Size of the class.** 7 of the 32 matters are company figures (M06, M07, M09, M10, M11, M18, M30). The old system serves 5–6 of\n   155\t    them and the new system 0. That is 4 of the old system's 7–8 old-only matters.\n   156\t  - **Outside the company figures** the new system still trails: old serves 6 and new 3. It misses M04, hyperscaler capex (a shared\n   157\t    quantity, which D384 allows), M17, the Anthropic anchor investment (an obligation), and M19 in 2 of its draws.\n   158\t- 2026-11-19 ~14:00: **The goal's loop stops, on its limits.**\n   159\t  - **A pass needs much broader opening.** At least 9 of 14 rule-allowed matters under D382, against 0–1 today, or D382 reversed. The $0\n   160\t    census found three loss points, and none yields to a wording fix.\n   161\t  - **Confirming any candidate needs a full comparison,** about $110. That is above D439's $40 ceiling, so it starts only on Alex's word.\n   162\t  - **Probe spend this round:** about $3 by the ledgers.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba poc/config/poc-v118.json; nl -ba poc/config/poc-v118-idea.json; nl -ba docs/poc/pipeline-plan.md; rg -n 'D370|D374|poc-v118' docs -g '*.md' -g '\"'!**/*review*'\"' -g '\"'!**/CURRENT_STATE.md'\"' -g '\"'!**/DECISIONS*'\"' | rg '0\\\\.5|0\\\\.6|gold|minutes|acceptance|243|refus' | cut -c1-330 | head -65\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
