allenge-2.md:20:   - Hashed before the first send: the article list, the versions (poc-v118, and astra-frozen with v5.5 excluded), the reader instructions, the\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v11.md:299:**Old system, per draw:** poc-v118's own $0.53 to $0.66 for 243 articles, scaled up, is about $5. But cost per article rises as the library\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-3/cold-challenge-4.md:18:- It was never given a decision number (a search of `docs/DECISIONS.md` for it finds nothing; D370's record says only \"confirmed\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-3/cold-codex-2.md:15:- **Empty starts:** the July comparison and fresh-week test started empty. D370 removes the artificial preset questions but retains existing research as context; it does not decide that every real deployment starts empty. This is a plausible reason the tests\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-3/cold-codex-2.md:25:Neither of our earlier questions should be put as the next choice yet. Mine jumped to a treatment for one class. Yours bundles three separate choices: starting with real prior research, asking a person to approve new questions, and requiring a fixed form. D3\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-3/own-reflection.md:64:the 22 \"artificial\" preset questions (D370) and said extraction should read the existing research library; D466 put the\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-3/cold-challenge-1.md:58:   an analyst's list to start from). His decisions that bear on it: D370 (the 22 artificial preset questions removed;\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-channel/CHANNEL-ASSESSMENT.md:55:  dependency (D370, D368), so for article-opened questions the channel has nothing to read until the matching step chooses\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-3/handoff-cold.md:19:- The two systems in one paragraph: the old one is production (`poc/config/poc-v118.json`); the new one is `clean-arch/`: a\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-3/handoff-cold.md:29:  owner decided about the question list: \"## D370\", \"## D382\", \"## D384\", \"## D397\", \"## D436\"). The index `docs/DECISIONS.md` has one\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-3/cold-challenge-3.md:27:  `poc/data/sealed-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite`, read immutable); D370's own diagnostic used \"the same\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-3/cold-challenge-3.md:63:   earlier-dated library by both families. The product Alex described keeps its library (D370: extraction reads the existing\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/ACCEPTANCE-DESIGN.md:16:- **Systems:** production as it now runs (poc-v118) and the clean path as frozen (Step 1 c8, Step 2, the ladder step, the frozen judge). No\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-4/claude-measurement.md:13:| 3 | Judgement key (reader B) + `score_judgement.py` | At the window end 2026-07-14, does the chosen answer band overlap reader B's range | 23 questions, 20 with a view, 17–19 judged per draw | Code against one model reader's answers (D262) | Scoring \ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-4/claude-measurement.md:35:| Keys 1–3 before D370; D392 | NVDA, 2026-07-01..14, also the tuning set (\"the articles tuned c8\", D392) | 22 hand-written preset questions | 3, same-day control |\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-4/claude-measurement.md:40:**The design says otherwise.** The product is a continuous stream against a standing library that each article reads (`docs/prd/00-system.md`, Purpose; D375, not built). The rebuild is to be evaluated \"against a known initial library\", with Alex review\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-4/handoff-history.md:17:called production (`poc/config/poc-v118.json`, code under `src/hivemind/`, design in `docs/system-design.html` with data in\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/NEW-SYSTEM-FRAME.md:12:- **Reference system:** the old system as it runs (`poc/config/poc-v118.json`), kept as the default and as the comparison.\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-4/handoff-measurement.md:17:called production (`poc/config/poc-v118.json`, code under `src/hivemind/`, design in `docs/system-design.html` with data in\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-4/common.md:15:called production (`poc/config/poc-v118.json`, code under `src/hivemind/`, design in `docs/system-design.html` with data in\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/SEPARATION-DESIGN.md:126:Today's default holds no seed edge (D370), so only `reads` edges written when a question is created (D51) are in play. For each\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/SEPARATION-DESIGN.md:190:| writers: `seeding.seed_views` (retired from the default by D370; each stored seeded draw holds 17 such rows); `writing.write` from the matching answer (`jev_matching` returns `'dependencies': []` today) | write the row without a kind | each w\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/SEPARATION-DESIGN.md:225:| D354, D370, D427 | judging, matching and the reading prompt are frozen as they run; preset questions are retired from the default | nothing here changes a frozen piece; a build is a new version the council or Alex opens |\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/DECISION-PAGE-2026-11-15.md:23:- **The old system** is today's default configuration (`poc-v118`, kept unchanged for comparison). Its last full measurement was on\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:16:- **Reference systems:** production as it runs (poc-v118) and the clean path as frozen (c8, Step 2 D427, ladder step D426, frozen judge).\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:176:  step (presets, D370; four or five sends cannot show safety); both converge on the kept figures as a record.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-LOG.md | sed -n '30,42p;84,96p;123,182p'; rg --files docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison | rg '(RESULT|SCORE|score|verdict|cost|run-time|old-|FINDINGS|REPORT)' | rg -v 'stage0/census' | tail -95; rg -n 'v118' docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/DECISION-PAGE-2026-11-15.md; rg -n 'golden-v5|243|q1|q2|q3' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | cut -c1-240\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-LOG.md | sed -n '30,42p;84,96p;123,182p'; rg --files docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison | rg '(RESULT|SCORE|score|verdict|cost|run-time|old-|FINDINGS|REPORT)' | rg -v 'stage0/census' | tail -95; rg -n 'v118' docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/DECISION-PAGE-2026-11-15.md; rg -n 'golden-v5|243|q1|q2|q3' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | cut -c1-240\"","aggregated_output":"    30\t| 22:05 | slice | s-old complete ($0.22). s-new stopped at the ladder: the shared ledger refused a $1.33 astra reservation against the slice's $10 guard (spent $2.86; 8 concurrent worst-case reservations ≈ $10.7). Diagnosis: guard sizing, a launcher parameter (plan §2: fix the launcher only, rerun). Before the stop: Step 1 98 articles ≈ 40 s and $0.011 each; Step 2 and cases complete (9 cases); 5 astra ladder sends answered, no wrapper refusal. Full-run guard $65 leaves room (≈ $23 spent + ≈ $11 reservations at that point) | rerun as slice-2, 07-01..07-03, guards $25 / $3 |\n    31\t| 2026-11-17 22:35 | slice-2 | Both draws complete (new \\$0.93, old \\$0.05). Checks: 1–4 PASS at once; 5 and 6 failed first by the checks' own error. Old's 3 extra items are copies merged into their originals (not extracted), and day-end judgements carry `day:<date>`. Corrected and rerun: **all six PASS** (39 articles, 42.1 s and \\$0.0084 each, every ladder pass astra, same 39 items in order, a day state reads back) | stage0/slice-2-checks.txt |\n    32\t| 2026-11-17 22:36 | run | **Full run launched:** new-1..3 (clean, astra-frozen, guard \\$65 each) and old-1..3 (poc-v118, guard \\$25 each), 07-01..09-20, on the shared items DB, all six within one minute (D667 timing), at commit 4c66408f | monitor armed (stops, crashes, component changes, progress every 100 attempts / 7 days) |\n    33\t| 22:41 | reading tools | mapping.py (3 tests), mark_cards.py (4 tests), build_cards.py type field; card form check (D673): round 1 named two rung annotations (removed) and a truncation artefact of the check itself; round 2 named only the systems' own structure (rung counts, library sizes), disclosed | stage0/blinding-check-codex*.md |\n    34\t| 23:03 | check | six draws running; spend new 0.43–0.45, old 0.91–1.08; my own mistake: a status check tried to count rows in a live Step 1 trace (AGENTS §9: never open a live run's databases); refused by the classifier, not repeated; status is read from run.json and the ledgers only | run/ |\n    35\t| 23:24 | card form check (D673), rounds 3–4 on the new card (request context, own opening place, numbered answers) | round 3 named one form element: the answer step's third annotation form ('the amount last reported when the question opened'); the annotation filter is now the closed set of ladder_step's three suffixes (484 stored conditions, 0 left annotated). Round 4 named only content (rung counts, theme counts, library size): closed, disclosed with the result | stage0/blinding-check-codex-3.md, -4.md |\n    36\t| 23:37 | reading-tools council, rounds 2–4 | round 2–3 both readers not ready (eligibility, mapping validation, publishers, debate, plants, split readings, card context); round 4: Claude ready to read, Codex 3 more (key-verified card flags, reconciled attempt log, theme rungs), fixed; 47 tests, 39 mutants + 5 controls as predicted; §1.6 design v2 sent with round 5 | D675; tools-review-codex-2..4.md; DESIGN-1.6.md |\n    37\t| 00:06 | §1.6 design rounds 5–7 → v6; reading tools committed (c3704776, 802f2b08) | both readers: design faithful after v6's small fixes; built eligibility inputs, D400 code check, printed-beside quantities, diagnostic export (54 tests, 43 mutants + 6 controls); three builders started in parallel for D400 reader lines, Step 2 lines, D431 at 07-14 (new files only, fake readers) | DESIGN-1.6.md v6; D675 |\n    38\t| 00:29 | three §1.6 tools built (D400 reader lines 7 tests, Step 2 lines 10, D431 6; each with mutants on scratch copies) | finding: Step 2 line 3 as v6 defines it is predetermined (group_text drops later reports' tier/stated day/period/speaker; v6 counts them; c1: 78/79 groups) while the product's judge reads each member's full record (PRD §6; 741 and 1,127 same-claim notes in c1/p1 requests); sent to the council as round 8 with the tools | tools-review-brief-8.md |\n    39\t| 01:02 | §1.6 tools pass the council (round 10, Codex READY; Claude round 9 points fixed) | every instrument D672 requires is built and reviewed before any output: reading tools (round 5) and §1.6 tools (round 10); 92 stage0 tests; CURRENT_STATE next task = the reading order once the six draws end | f2cbfcfa |\n    40\t| 01:20 | old-1, old-2 complete | old-1 $9.83, old-2 $8.60, no stop; old-3 near the end; the new draws still in Step 1 (about $2.8 each) | run/ |\n    41\t| 01:21 | old-3 complete | $8.83, no stop; the three old draws total $27.26 against $25 guards each (not a budget); the new draws are in Step 1 | run/ |\n    42\t| 13:11 | reading chain dry run end to end on the slice ($0, fake reader) | every step joins; verdict 'too small' as ordered; gap fixed: printed-beside quantities now computed for invalid and too-small verdicts too | stage0/chain_dry_run.py |\n    84\t- 2026-11-18 21:02: Mac unplugged at 100%. Alex was notified to keep it on power overnight; new-1's redo needs about 18 h.\n    85\t- 2026-11-18 22:57: **new-3 complete**, at $37.64 in all.\n    86\t  - Step 1 $21.3; Step 2 and the cases about $6.4; the ladder about $6.9; the judge about $3.0.\n    87\t  - Five of the six draws are complete. new-1's Step 1 redo, launched at 19:05, is still running.\n    88\t  - Eligibility and the reading wait for all six draws, so nothing is read before then.\n    89\t- 2026-11-19 00:54: AC power back at 39% and charging, after about 4 h on battery. No draw was lost; new-1's Step 1 redo continues ($27.8).\n    90\t- 2026-11-19 10:55: **Alex:** \"i think you are really wasting my time and money with my reruns, just get it done and tell me the results\".\n    91\t  - Asked whether to wait for new-1 (about 4 h, about $17) or stop it and score the five finished draws. **He chose: \"Let it finish, then score\".**\n    92\t  - No new reruns.\n    93\t  - `reading-chain.sh` started detached (pid in `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-chain.pid`). It waits for new-1 to complete, then\n    94\t    runs the CURRENT_STATE order: eligibility, then mapping, then cards, then the verdict, then the release checks. Outputs go to\n    95\t    `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading/`.\n    96\t\n   123\t  - **The release chain** (`reading-chain.sh`) was restarted and waits for new-1. Before its deck it sets the diagnostic deck key aside.\n   124\t- 2026-11-19 ~13:40: **DIAGNOSTIC result on the five finished draws** (`reading-diagnostic/diagnostic-count.json`; not a release verdict).\n   125\t  - **Controls:** all pass. 6/6 plants caught, 4/4 supported controls supported, 3/3 repeats the same.\n   126\t  - **Served matters (N = 32, margin 5):**\n   127\t    | | new | old | a (new only) | b (old only) |\n   128\t    |---|---|---|---|---|\n   129\t    | Counting 1 | 3 | 10 | 0 | 7 |\n   130\t    | Counting 2 | 2 | 10 | 0 | 8 |\n   131\t  - **Best case for the new system if new-1 served every matter served in new-2 or new-3:** new 4–5, old 10, a = 1, b = 6–7. That is\n   132\t    still no lead for the new system, and b − a ≥ 5.\n   133\t  - **What the old system serves and the new one misses:** M04 hyperscaler capex, M06 FY27 data-center revenue, M10 and M11 FY28 margin\n   134\t    and revenue, M17 the Anthropic anchor investment, M18 the FY27 gross margin.\n   135\t  - **What the new system serves:** M13, M15, M31, plus M19 and M32 in one draw only.\n   136\t- 2026-11-19 12:55: **Alex chose \"Stop it now\"**: new-1 cannot change the conclusion.\n   137\t  - new-1's launcher was stopped by SIGTERM in Step 2. Its record shows `crashed`, at $45.29.\n   138\t  - The release chain was stopped too. No process is left.\n   139\t  - **Final paid spend:** about $145 in all.\n   140\t    - Old system: $27.26 for its three draws.\n   141\t    - New system: new-2 $34.66, new-3 $37.64, new-1 $45.29, plus the $0.12 single-item send.\n   142\t  - **The answer stands as the 5-draw diagnostic:** the new system loses (served: new 2–3, old 10).\n   143\t- 2026-11-19 ~13:30: **Why the new system loses.** This is the D674 round's diagnosis, $0, from stored traces and libraries.\n   144\t  - **The new libraries hold no question on the company's own figures.** Of their 33–41 questions, none is on revenue, data-center\n   145\t    revenue, gross margin or hyperscaler capex. They are deals, investments, shipments and regulators. The old libraries open FY27\n   146\t    revenue, FY28 revenue, FY27 data-center revenue, FY27 gross margin and hyperscaler capex from 07-02 to 07-08.\n   147\t  - **The new system extracts the evidence but files no question for it.** new-2's Step 1 extracted 642 evidence items on\n   148\t    revenue, margin or capex; 336 were linked elsewhere and 306 kept unlinked.\n   149\t  - **The cause is the prompt's rule, by decision:**\n   150\t    - D382 (Alex: \"我觉得财务类型不应该是thesis，而更多的是条件…\"): \"a company's own figures are conditions, not questions\".\n   151\t    - D384: \"opens only the big matters\", with class A, the main-driver quantity, left out under D382.\n   152\t    - The week acceptance (2026-09-22..28) already found the same thing: the clean path lacked FY27 and FY28 revenue and the FY28\n   153\t      margin, and its stored reasoning named this do-not-open sentence.\n   154\t  - **Size of the class.** 7 of the 32 matters are company figures (M06, M07, M09, M10, M11, M18, M30). The old system serves 5–6 of\n   155\t    them and the new system 0. That is 4 of the old system's 7–8 old-only matters.\n   156\t  - **Outside the company figures** the new system still trails: old serves 6 and new 3. It misses M04, hyperscaler capex (a shared\n   157\t    quantity, which D384 allows), M17, the Anthropic anchor investment (an obligation), and M19 in 2 of its draws.\n   158\t- 2026-11-19 ~14:00: **The goal's loop stops, on its limits.**\n   159\t  - **A pass needs much broader opening.** At least 9 of 14 rule-allowed matters under D382, against 0–1 today, or D382 reversed. The $0\n   160\t    census found three loss points, and none yields to a wording fix.\n   161\t  - **Confirming any candidate needs a full comparison,** about $110. That is above D439's $40 ceiling, so it starts only on Alex's word.\n   162\t  - **Probe spend this round:** about $3 by the ledgers.\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/FINDINGS.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/score_comparison.py\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/mutants-score-comparison.txt\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/test_score_comparison.py\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/verdict-rule.json\n23:- **The old system** is today's default configuration (`poc-v118`, kept unchanged for comparison). Its last full measurement was on\n23:  Dev ×3 on the frozen golden-v5 (a lead): helpful 214, 211 and 212 of 234; search 98.9–100%; clear wrong merges about 1%. Step 1\n97:**Split prompt structure v2 small test (2026-11-05):** Thirty calls on two previously seen golden-v5 dev articles completed in `../hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review`. The blind model reader found complete helpful matters in the fresh c\n99:**Split extraction small test (2026-11-05):** At Alex's request, the isolated `hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review` worktree ran two real golden-v5 articles once through each split lane. An independent model reader found 7 of 19 helpful \n105:Alex decided future gold scoring should measure helpful versus not helpful evidence without requiring separate scores for core and supporting. Use frozen golden-v5 as-is: combine core and supporting as helpful, treat not-kept as unhelpf\n785:  as records); three fresh 14-day draws completed 2026-11-13 03:46 (`poc/data/clean-e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/draw-q1..q3`: 243 items\n790:  (D430's same deadline against the standard's 18-month range for q23) is recorded apart (D373), scoring unchanged.\n862:- **Stage 2 of D392:** clean 18, 18, 17 against v108 17, 15, 16, inconclusive on q12.\n863:- **Known gap (D394):** capital spending (q12).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/FINDINGS.md | head -155; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/DECISION-PAGE-2026-11-15.md | sed -n '15,53p'; rg -n 'draw-q[123]|243 articles|243 items|0\\\\.53|0\\\\.66' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md docs/DECISIONS-log.md docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance -g '*.md' | cut -c1-310 | tail -70; ls poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/FINDINGS.md | head -155; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/DECISION-PAGE-2026-11-15.md | sed -n '15,53p'; rg -n 'draw-q[123]|243 articles|243 items|0\\\\.53|0\\\\.66' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md docs/DECISIONS-log.md docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance -g '*.md' | cut -c1-310 | tail -70; ls poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Findings outside the comparison's scope (recorded, not acted on; to Alex with the verdict)\n     2\t\n     3\t- 2026-11-17: the answer-choice step's code default is still luna (`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_a/stage_a.py` `SETTING`), although D648\n     4\t  chose astra. The comparison runs astra as a named, hashed variant; the default is not edited by this plan.\n     5\t- 2026-11-17 (stage 0, exposure census): under D667's rule no article of 2026-08-31..09-20 is unread. Every past week of the corpus has been\n     6\t  touched, mostly by corpus storage and code-only corpus censuses, but the week of 08-31 by real old-system development runs as well. An\n     7\t  \"unread weeks\" comparison (D665) is not possible on the current corpus without either a new reading of \"read\" or fresh articles after\n     8\t  2026-10-27.\n     9\t- 2026-11-17: `stage_a_astra.py`'s first test stopped its run (`limit.stopped` true on the resend case); not yet diagnosed. Code work paused\n    10\t  with the census result.\n    11\t- 2026-11-17: a folder `downloaded_files/` with an empty `dashboard.lock` appears in the repository root (18:34, 18:35); not created by this work, not touched.\n    12\t\n    13\t- 2026-11-18 00:40 — **Step 2 line 3 (a hard check) is predetermined under design v6's key.**\n    14\t  - The frozen dossier renderer `group_text` drops a later report's tier, stated day, period and speaker. v6 counted those as details,\n    15\t    and on c1, 78 of 79 eligible groups differ in them.\n    16\t  - The product's judge reads each member's own full record, with a same-claim note (PRD §6), not `group_text`.\n    17\t  - Taken to the council (round 8) before any output; the decision is recorded in D675.\n    18\t\n    19\t- 2026-11-18, new-1 Step 1, one item:\n    20\t  - **What failed:** the c8 model left out the required `figures` on evidence items 2 to 4, twice. This was the run's first format\n    21\t    failure that its retry did not recover. Before this, 9 of 9 retries had recovered.\n    22\t  - **Cost of the rule:** under D449, one failed article out of 1884 forces a Step 1 redo from empty, costing about $21 and about 20 h.\n    23\t    The $65 guard was sized at 1.6 times one pass with no redo, so a redo puts the draw at its guard.\n    24\t  - **Scope:** out of scope for this run. A finding about the redo unit (an item-level redo) and about how the guard is sized.\n    25\t- 2026-11-19: new-1's only failure repeated exactly on the redo: same item, same missing `figures`, twice each time. It was\n    26\t  deterministic in that draw's context, not a transport failure. D449's full-step redo cannot recover such a failure.\n    27\t  - An item-level re-send, about a cent, would have shown this first.\n    28\t  - Proposal, for Alex: before any D449 redo, re-send the failed item's stored request. Redo only if that send passes.\n    15\ta first checkpoint is $5 of further spending. The rest of this page is as written before that decision, and remains the\n    16\tevidence for it.\n    17\t\n    18\t## The decision\n    19\t\n    20\tTwo systems read the same news and produce the same kind of product: questions worth tracking, the statements that bear on them,\n    21\tand an answer to each question.\n    22\t\n    23\t- **The old system** is today's default configuration (`poc-v118`, kept unchanged for comparison). Its last full measurement was on\n    24\t  the fixed test window of July; it has not passed any test of readiness on new news.\n    25\t- **The new system** is the rebuild (`clean-arch/`): a new reading step, its own matching and grouping, an added step that writes\n    26\t  each question's answer choices, and the same judge as the old system. Its fourth step (answer choices and judging) is still in\n    27\t  progress, the step that writes answer choices has not passed its required tests (2026-11-12), and nothing of it is integrated\n    28\t  with production storage (`clean-arch/README.md`).\n    29\t\n    30\t**Which one does the work carry forward toward production?**\n    31\t\n    32\t## The short answer\n    33\t\n    34\tOne fresh week does not pick a winner. By the rule written before the week was read, the result is \"not clear\" (D489), and nothing\n    35\tsince has changed that. The week does show what each system costs a reader, and it shows where Alex's choices of the past two days\n    36\tbear on the comparison. Both are below. **The council's advice is to keep the old system as the default and keep both, and not to\n    37\tchoose from this evidence** (section 5).\n    38\t\n    39\t## 1. One week, both systems\n    40\t\n    41\tThe week of 2026-09-22 to 09-28: 235 articles (232 never read by any earlier run; three had been read in earlier tests of the\n    42\treading step). Each system ran once, starting with no questions (`week/WEEK-RESULT.md`).\n    43\t\n    44\t| At the end of the week | Old system | New system |\n    45\t|---|---|---|\n    46\t| Questions opened | 15 | 7 |\n    47\t| of which worth holding, by two independent reviewing teams | 8 or 9 | 6 |\n    48\t| trivia | 3 | 1 |\n    49\t| duplicates of its own questions | 3 | 0 |\n    50\t| Statements written | 673 | 569 |\n    51\t| thrown away because no question took them | 278 | 0 |\n    52\t| kept, with no question at the week's end | 0 | 389 |\n    53\t| Links between statements and questions | 449 (126 of them to one question, fiscal 2027 revenue) | 196 |\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:785:  as records); three fresh 14-day draws completed 2026-11-13 03:46 (`poc/data/clean-e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/draw-q1..q3`: 243 items\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2575:- Amendment, 2026-10-27 23:20: Alex stopped the restarted run (\"我不是要你看下step 1抽取到底行不行？\") and asked for the prompt to be read and fixed, with examples (\"什么叫重要陈述，你也没给例子\"). Arms B1–B6 ([log](research/2026-10-27-single-call/log.md) §10–17) rewrote the role as the model reads it: evidence\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2580:- Decided: `poc/config/poc-v34.json` (extraction T*-v18; matching, collision judge and judging as `poc-v30`) is the replay default (`scripts/replay.py --config`, README). Evidence: the arms B3–B6 and the two extraction-only scale tests in the [log](research/2026-10-27-single-call/lo\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2583:- Found while switching the default, before the acceptance run: `extraction.ACCOUNT_FROM = 17` made v18 send v17's per-paragraph account shape in production, while arms B3–B6 and both scale tests were sent with the flat shape (`arm.py` restores the stored request and replaces only t\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4250:    Stage 2 (about $11: three paired draws on v108's 243 items) are all approved. If Stage 1 meets its frozen line, Stage 2 runs without\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4304:  - Three unseeded clean draws (c8 from an empty library) on v108's 243 items.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4906:- **Decided:** three fresh 14-day draws from empty (`draw-q1..q3`), the same day; a new shared ledger with ceiling $3.00, conditional on the reservation and retry-billing bounds (an overrun stops later sends but cannot undo a charge); run caps $1.00. The stopped p1–p3 are kept as re\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-8/challenge-1.md:58:- The running pipeline (`p1..p3/prod`) is $0.53 to $0.66 per 14-day draw, about $0.04 a day.\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-8/claude-cold.md:12:8. Record errors: D649 (14 should be 12; line 2 hinges on a listing point, not due day; the split pinned on D403 wrongly; \"pending with Alex\" though D414 decided it); \"Every reader ... unjustified\" false (report-output.txt:31,32,34); D651 \ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-8/codex-challenge-1.md:32:   The completed clean article-reading charges are **$2.36–$2.51 per draw**, about **$0.17–$0.18/day**; running-pipeline draws are **$0.53–$0.66**, about **$0.038–$0.047/day**. Adding the estimated Astra step and the stored matching \ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-6/codex-cold.md:26:   Under a simplifying independent, constant-rate assumption, the **combined** fault probability across all zero-fault lines must be below about **0.53% per send for a 50% chance** of zero faults in 131 sends, or **0.039% for a 95% chance**\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-2/cold-challenge-10.md:23:  text length), and **$3.39 from July's charge per article** (run c1: $2.51 first step and $0.38 matching for 243 articles),\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-10/codex-1.md:16:D623’s rates are descriptive, from overlapping luna-era readings. Under an independence assumption, a combined fault rate of about **0.53% per send** gives only a coin-flip chance of seeing zero faults in 131 sends. That calculation explains \ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/second-week/DESIGN.md:19:  retries; the four stored runs used 0 or 1 retries in 235 to 243 articles. A stop there is the run's stop.\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/second-week/DESIGN.md:45:  $2.51 the first step and $0.38 the matching for 243 articles), about $3.39. The ledger also holds reservations for calls in\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/comparison/COMPARISON-SIZING.md:26:| By code: share of links on the largest question | new 0.20, 0.25, 0.20; old 0.53, 0.32, 0.39 | new 0.26; old 0.28 | July: the ranges do not overlap; the fresh week shows no gap |\nledgers\nnew-1\nnew-1.launcher.log\nnew-1.pid\nnew-2\nnew-2.launcher.log\nnew-2.pid\nnew-3\nnew-3.launcher.log\nnew-3.pid\nold-1\nold-1.launcher.log\nold-1.pid\nold-2\nold-2.launcher.log\nold-2.pid\nold-3\nold-3.launcher.log\nold-3.pid\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
