{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | sed -n '448,538p'; nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '10308,10375p'; ls -l poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-{1,2,3}/\"","aggregated_output":"   448\t**The one next task: none open (D689, D690, 2026-11-20).** poc-v118 is the product (Alex chose A, D690), and the research line\n   449\trests until his new direction. The hybrid's release line is paused, and the judge and c8 lines are closed for now. A line reopens only\n   450\ton its condition below. No paid send is open, and D439 has $0 available without Alex's word.\n   451\t- **D689 (Alex chose option 1; council N closed both lines; record:\n   452\t  [council-n-codex.md](research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-n-codex.md), [council-n2-codex.md](research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-n2-codex.md)).**\n   453\t  - **Judge.** The carried previous conclusion holds rejected forecasts: on full evidence, 0 of 13 move with it and 8 of 13 without it,\n   454\t    with 0 of 8 controls moving.\n   455\t    - The readers jointly support 4 net repairs against the 5 required, including M14 in two of three old draws.\n   456\t    - The frozen gold reads 44.3 against 45.0, with China share regressed.\n   457\t    - It reopens on eight eligible failures on fresh questions, which the design never read and are counted once across draws, with\n   458\t      matched controls and a source-checked summary of the omitted facts (D198 option 2). Then the D198 choice and its price go to\n   459\t      Alex.\n   460\t  - **c8.** It showed no improvement in the final answers tested, and adds about $24 to old's about $9 over 82 days. It reopens on a\n   461\t    traced decisive fact that old missed, c8 delivers, and that could change a named final answer.\n   462\t  - **Spend (an error of mine).** \"Inside D439's $40\" was written in D679, D682 and D684 with no tally. D439 stands at about $39.65 or\n   463\t    $44.42 under the two readings. Phase 1's ledger is $2.64, not $2.4.\n   464\t- **History of this line (D681–D688)** follows. Alex opened the hybrid's build and\n   465\ttest, and asked that problems not be found only at the end (his words are in the D681 record). Plan: [PLAN.md](research/2026-11-20-hybrid/PLAN.md). Design:\n   466\t[DESIGN-J2.md](research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md).\n   467\t- **Where old loses on the 32 matters:**\n   468\t  - it never opens 17;\n   469\t  - it opened M08 and M14 in 3/3 draws, but the judge reasoned wrongly: amounts that overlap were added, and a figure of another scope\n   470\t    was taken as the answer.\n   471\t- **Census:** 24 answers rejected by both readers ([CENSUS.md](research/2026-11-20-hybrid/census/CENSUS.md)).\n   472\t- **Found at $0:** the judge writes the rung first and its reference and derivation last (`schema_for` appends the stance fields to\n   473\t  the end of `properties`).\n   474\t- **Arms:**\n   475\t  - J2a, the schema order only;\n   476\t  - J2b, J2a plus an overlap and scope check.\n   477\t- **The probe and its rule** are written before any J2 send. Its regression guard is the frozen judgement gold: the stored v7 requests\n   478\t  give 15/17, 15/17 and 16/17, and are rebuilt byte for byte.\n   479\t- **Status (D685):**\n   480\t  - **The judge line is paused within D198.** Four angles have failed:\n   481\t    - J2a and J2b fail the locked blind reading;\n   482\t    - removing the previous conclusion misses its screen by one, and the frozen gold reads 44.3 against 45.0;\n   483\t    - H1, the heading only, gives 0 net repairs against 2 in council J's blind diagnostic.\n   484\t  - The carried derivation holds the rejected rungs. Every remaining lever changes D198.\n   485\t  - **No fresh test exists on this corpus.** The judge's errors sit in about ten numeric bets the design has read; 27 fresh bets gave\n   486\t    1 target against 8 needed.\n   487\t- **Opening census (D686):** [OPENING-CENSUS.md](research/2026-11-20-hybrid/OPENING-CENSUS.md). Of the 16 matters old never opens:\n   488\t  - 6 are merged into a held question, because the scoring list is finer than D197 and D248;\n   489\t  - 5 fall outside the library's NVIDIA-only subject;\n   490\t  - 5, plus M05, are never proposed, though D248 allows them; a fix needs a new extraction version (D274).\n   491\t- **D382 answered (D687; his words are in the record):** in the hybrid, a company's own material figure keeps its own question, as\n   492\t  old's opening does.\n   493\t- **Attainable check (D688, council M):** [OPENING-CENSUS.md](research/2026-11-20-hybrid/OPENING-CENSUS.md), last two sections.\n   494\t  - The census found no credible path to a D665 lead through opening changes alone.\n   495\t  - The concrete misses within Alex's rules are M20 (a $125B unsigned obligation, D388) and M05. M09, M30 and M25 are coin flips.\n   496\t  - Noise costs about 1.4.\n   497\t  - What binds: the list counts finer than D248/D388 on 9 matters, the NVIDIA-only subject on 5, and D198 on 2.\n   498\t  - No opening test is sent.\n   499\t- **D688's recommendation, answered by D689:** keep poc-v118 as production and pause the hybrid's release line. Questions on other\n   500\t  research-list companies' key figures are offered only for their own value. Spend: phase 1 $2.64 of $3 (ledger); `phase1b` $0.36 of\n   501\t  $2.\n   502\t\n   503\t**Earlier next task, closed by D676 and D677 (D665–D675): read the release comparison's six draws when they finish, with the council-reviewed tools**\n   504\t(`docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v12.md` §1.4–§1.6; `DESIGN-1.6.md` v7; D675).\n   505\t\n   506\t- **Done:**\n   507\t  - stage 0 and slice 2;\n   508\t  - the full run, six draws, launched together at 22:36 on 2026-11-17 under `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/`;\n   509\t  - every reading instrument built and passed by the council before any output was read: reading tools in round 5, the §1.6 tools in\n   510\t    round 10; the scorer hardened through Codex rounds 11–21 (D675); 101 stage0 tests, 75 mutants on the reading tools.\n   511\t- **Result, 2026-11-19 (diagnostic, 5 draws; Alex stopped new-1).** The new system loses on the release comparison.\n   512\t  - Of 32 key matters, the new system serves 2–3 and the old one 10 (a = 0, b = 7–8). The controls pass.\n   513\t  - Even a perfect new-1 could not reverse it.\n   514\t  - The new libraries miss the core revenue, margin and capex matters.\n   515\t  - Details: `docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-LOG.md`, `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/`.\n   516\t  - **Diagnosed (D676, council):** D382's figure exclusion plus the Step 1→ladder bundled-question loss (D432). Even repaired, the new system ties at best. The old system stays; no further comparison run.\n   517\t  - **The goal loop is closed (D677, council).** The old system stays and no paid work continues. It reopens only if Alex reverses D505\n   518\t    or funds a full run, with a written path to passing first.\n   519\t  - **The one-outcome probe failed its line 1** (`docs/research/2026-11-19-one-outcome-probe/RESULT.md`): it fixes the period bundles\n   520\t    but not the deal bundles.\n   521\t  - **What a pass would take** ($0 arithmetic on the frozen list; pass = a − b ≥ 5 and a ≥ 2b):\n   522\t    - **Under D382:** the old system keeps 4 figure matters the new one can never take, so b ≥ 4. The new system would need at least 9\n   523\t      matters only it serves, out of the 14 its rules allow that the old system misses: 6 shared quantities, 5 obligations and 3\n   524\t      policy steps. Today it serves 0–1 of them.\n   525\t    - **With D382 reversed:** at least 5 of 17, the 14 plus 3 figures the old system misses, provided it also matches the old system on\n   526\t      the rest.\n   527\t    - **Either way:** passing needs much broader opening, not a wording fix.\n   528\t- **(Superseded) When all six draws end, in this order:**\n   529\t  1. `eligibility.py`: six complete draws, launched within 1 h, sends within 72 h.\n   530\t  2. `mapping.py export`, then `read`, `third`, `result`.\n   531\t  3. `mark_cards.py deck`, then `mark`, `debate 1`, `debate 2`, `readings`.\n   532\t  4. `score_comparison.py <run root> <mapping out> <marks folder>`: rebuilds every derived file from the primary data (refuses any that\n   533\t     differs, the readings record included) and gives the verdict and the printed-beside quantities on the rebuilt snapshot.\n   534\t  5. `d400_code_check.py` and `step2_lines.py`: the hard checks and the release status.\n   535\t  6. `d400_reader_lines.py` and `d431_reading.py`: printed beside.\n   536\t  7. A council loop on the result, and a row in `TRIES.md`.\n   537\t- **If a draw stops:** no release verdict; a diagnostic export (plan §1.4 item 10).\n   538\t- **If the verdict is not a practical lead:** the council-loop skill on the traces, and the next try from another angle (D674).\n 10308\t## D689 · 2026-11-20 · Alex chooses option 1 (keep old, pause the hybrid's release line); council N closes the judge and c8 lines for now\n 10309\t\n 10310\t- **Alex, 2026-11-20**, on D688's three options, of which option 1 was recommended (\"旧系统继续上线，混合系统暂停冲'比旧系统强'这一关。判答案和读文章的改进还可以接着做，但算作提升质量，不再当作上线的理由。\"):\n 10311\t  \"1. 好你去做，review deeply with council before your actions, don't haste into making actions\".\n 10312\t- **Decided (Alex):**\n 10313\t  - option 1: poc-v118 stays production, and the hybrid's release line is paused;\n 10314\t  - the release bar (D665) is unchanged;\n 10315\t  - no code or configuration changes.\n 10316\t- **Council N** (`docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-n-*`): a fresh Codex thread (`01a1fac2…`, read-only, memories off) read the\n 10317\t  record cold, while Claude wrote its position apart. Both independently reached the same exit. Round 2 reached CONSENSUS, with three\n 10318\t  wording changes taken here.\n 10319\t- **Decided (council N, under D543):** the judge line and the c8 reading line close for now. Nothing is sent, and D198 is not changed.\n 10320\t  - **The judge.** The carried previous conclusion holds rejected forecasts in place.\n 10321\t    - On identical full evidence, 0 of 13 targets move with it, and 8 of 13 without it, with 0 of 8 controls moving.\n 10322\t    - Both blind readers support 4 net repairs, against the 5 required. The 4 are four test cases, M14 (four companies' 2027 capex)\n 10323\t      twice, in two of three old draws.\n 10324\t    - In the separate test with the usual limited evidence, the frozen gold reads 44.3 against v7's 45.0, with China share regressed.\n 10325\t    - Every remaining lever changes D198, and every big numeric bet on this corpus has been read by the design.\n 10326\t  - **c8** delivered the decisive statements but showed no improvement in the final answers tested. It adds about $24 to old's about\n 10327\t    $9 over 82 days.\n 10328\t- **Reopening conditions:**\n 10329\t  - **Judge.** Eight eligible failures on fresh questions.\n 10330\t    - \"Fresh\" means a question the design never read, counted once across draws, with close variants excluded (council I).\n 10331\t    - New evidence on a read question can show whether a repair holds over time. It does not count toward the eight.\n 10332\t    - Matched supported controls, and a source-checked summary of the omitted facts worth testing (D198 option 2), are also needed.\n 10333\t    - Then the D198 choice and its price go to Alex. A paid test needs his approval and funding.\n 10334\t    - Processing the 523 later articles (09-21..10-22) would cost about $2.5 a draw before readers, with no assurance of enough new\n 10335\t      questions.\n 10336\t  - **c8.** A traced case where:\n 10337\t    - old missed a decisive fact;\n 10338\t    - c8 delivers it;\n 10339\t    - the final answer it could change is named.\n 10340\t\n 10341\t    A paired test with the same judge and question would then show whether it helps.\n 10342\t  - **A future test's pass criteria** (proposed, not confirmed):\n 10343\t    - net repairs on distinct final forecasts, backed by both blind readers in 2 of 3 same-day pairs;\n 10344\t    - at least 4 at 8 targets;\n 10345\t    - no lost control and no added refusal;\n 10346\t    - frozen agreement at least v7's, with China share 3 of 3.\n 10347\t- **Not reopened:**\n 10348\t  - D368 item 2 (dependencies chosen at matching) stays open defect 4 in `CURRENT_STATE.md`, closed as a stretch by D542. None of the\n 10349\t    24 rejected answers traces to it.\n 10350\t  - The D260 stance-field order (D681) stays a recorded defect. J2a measured no effect from it.\n 10351\t- **Spend, an error of mine.** The last D439 tally was about $39.29 of $40 (D647). D679, D682 and D684 then said \"inside D439's $40\"\n 10352\t  with no tally.\n 10353\t  - Under the two readings, D439 stands at about $39.65 (only `phase1b`, $0.36) or about $44.42 (the merge test's $2.13, `phase1` at\n 10354\t    $2.64 by its ledger and `phase1b`).\n 10355\t  - The records' \"$2.4\" for phase 1 is corrected to the ledger's $2.64.\n 10356\t  - **$0 is available for new sends without Alex's word.**\n 10357\t- **Dropped:** Claude's proposed $0 count of how often a forecast repeats. It cannot tell which forecasts were wrong, and it cannot\n 10358\t  change the closure.\n 10359\t\n 10360\t## D690 · 2026-11-20 · Alex chooses A: poc-v118 is the product, the research line rests until his new direction; the D681–D689 records are committed locally\n 10361\t\n 10362\t- **Alex's words** (2026-11-20), replying to the two items put to him after D689: \"1. OK 2. A\". Item 1 was a local commit of the\n 10363\t  D681–D689 records, not pushed. Item 2's options were:\n 10364\t  - **A**, recommended: poc-v118 is the product, and the research line rests until his new direction;\n 10365\t  - **B**, change the rules that bind the hybrid's lead: whether the library tracks other companies' own figures (5 matters, D688),\n 10366\t    and whether the judge carries its previous conclusion (D198). \"One bet, one question\" (D248) was not offered for change, because\n 10367\t    the comparison's list is finer than it;\n 10368\t  - **C**, new test questions from another company or a later NVIDIA window, at a price he would set.\n 10369\t- **Decided (Alex):** A. No improvement line on the hybrid, the judge, c8 or opening is open, and no paid send is open. The reopening\n 10370\t  conditions of D689 stand. B and C are not taken.\n 10371\t- **Done:** the D681–D690 records are committed on `clean-arch`, and nothing is pushed.\n 10372\t- **Asked next by Alex, in the same message:** a description of the end-to-end system (its components, how it runs, its current\n 10373\t  performance) and whether it is ready to go to production for testing. That answer is an assessment, recorded when it is given.\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/:\ntotal 48\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff      0 Nov 17 22:36 launch.lock\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff     98 Nov 17 22:36 preconditions.log\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 6 lchingen  staff    192 Nov 18 01:20 prod\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  15595 Nov 18 01:20 prod.log\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    982 Nov 18 01:20 run.json\n\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/:\ntotal 48\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff      0 Nov 17 22:36 launch.lock\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff     98 Nov 17 22:36 preconditions.log\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 6 lchingen  staff    192 Nov 18 01:20 prod\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  15592 Nov 18 01:20 prod.log\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    982 Nov 18 01:20 run.json\n\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-3/:\ntotal 48\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff      0 Nov 17 22:36 launch.lock\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff     98 Nov 17 22:36 preconditions.log\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 6 lchingen  staff    192 Nov 18 01:20 prod\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  15595 Nov 18 01:20 prod.log\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    982 Nov 18 01:20 run.json\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'model|def |DEFAULT|idea' scripts/hivemind_api.py scripts/hivemind_mcp.py src/hivemind/{idea,search,model}.py | rg '(embed|idea_v|PLANN|do_GET|do_POST|def main|DEFAULT_VIEWS|DEFAULT_ITEMS|DEFAULT_CONFIG|def thesis_library|def make_idea|def assess|def run|PRICES|CACHED_INPUT_SHARE|idea_summary|def discover|def plan|jev-1)' ; nl -ba docs/poc/service.md | sed -n '1,83p'; rg -n 'library|/idea|apiBase' poc/ui/src -g '*.{ts,tsx,js}' | head -35\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'model|def |DEFAULT|idea' scripts/hivemind_api.py scripts/hivemind_mcp.py src/hivemind/{idea,search,model}.py | rg '(embed|idea_v|PLANN|do_GET|do_POST|def main|DEFAULT_VIEWS|DEFAULT_ITEMS|DEFAULT_CONFIG|def thesis_library|def make_idea|def assess|def run|PRICES|CACHED_INPUT_SHARE|idea_summary|def discover|def plan|jev-1)' ; nl -ba docs/poc/service.md | sed -n '1,83p'; rg -n 'library|/idea|apiBase' poc/ui/src -g '*.{ts,tsx,js}' | head -35\"","aggregated_output":"src/hivemind/search.py:7:evaluation rerun costs nothing. The embedding key is read the way model.py reads the chat key and never stored.\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:55:def openai_embeddings(texts, embedding_model=EMBEDDING_MODEL, timeout=120):\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:57:    body = json.dumps({'model': embedding_model, 'input': texts}).encode('utf-8')\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:82:def build_index(ledger, index, embed=openai_embeddings, embedding_model=EMBEDDING_MODEL, batch=64):\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:94:        if have and have['text_sha256'] == digest and have['model'] == embedding_model and usable(json.loads(have['vector_json'])):\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:102:            vectors, used = embed([t for _, _, t in chunk], embedding_model)\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:110:                          [(view_id, digest, embedding_model, json.dumps(vector), used // max(1, len(chunk)), now) for (view_id, digest, _), vector in zip(chunk, vectors)])\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:124:def fresh_vectors(ledger, index, embedding_model=EMBEDDING_MODEL, view_ids=None):\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:129:    stored = {r['view_id']: (r['text_sha256'], json.loads(r['vector_json'])) for r in index.execute('select view_id, text_sha256, vector_json from view_vectors where model=?', (embedding_model,))}\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:143:def query_vector(index, query, embed=openai_embeddings, embedding_model=EMBEDDING_MODEL):\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:145:    row = index.execute('select vector_json from query_vectors where text_sha256=? and model=?', (digest, embedding_model)).fetchone()\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:148:    vectors, tokens = embed([query], embedding_model)\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:150:                  (digest, embedding_model, json.dumps(vectors[0]), tokens, time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S')))\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:155:def warm_queries(index, queries, embed=openai_embeddings, embedding_model=EMBEDDING_MODEL):\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:158:    a row, five seconds of a fourteen-second idea. Returns the number of queries embedded.\"\"\"\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:162:        if digest not in wanted and not index.execute('select 1 from query_vectors where text_sha256=? and model=?', (digest, embedding_model)).fetchone():\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:166:    vectors, tokens = embed(list(wanted.values()), embedding_model)\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:168:        raise model.TransportError(f'the embedding answer held {len(vectors)} vectors for {len(wanted)} queries')\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:171:                      [(digest, embedding_model, json.dumps(vector), tokens // len(wanted), now) for digest, vector in zip(wanted, vectors)])\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:248:def search(ledger, index, query, k=10, as_of=None, include_closed=False, embed=openai_embeddings, embedding_model=EMBEDDING_MODEL, aliases=None, semantic=True):\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:265:    vectors = fresh_vectors(ledger, index, embedding_model, [record['view_id'] for record in candidates]) if semantic else {}\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:272:            q, _ = query_vector(index, query, embed, embedding_model)\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:294:def fake_embed(texts, embedding_model=EMBEDDING_MODEL, dims=256):\nsrc/hivemind/model.py:36:          'jev-1.14.0': (0.042, 0.0)}   # Jev: docs.typesafe.ai/models, 2026-10-25; output free   # DeepSeek: peak-hour list prices, cache misses (2026-10-23 pricing page)\nsrc/hivemind/model.py:277:    price_in, price_out = PRICES.get(setting.model, (0.0, 0.0))\nsrc/hivemind/idea.py:218:def read_idea(ledger, index, items, archive, cfg, text, as_of=None, k=10, aliases=None, semantic=True, transport=None, bundles=True, embed=search.openai_embeddings, on_progress=None):\nsrc/hivemind/idea.py:309:                        cfg.idea_summary and cfg.idea_summary.prompt_version in ('idea-summary-v6', 'idea-summary-v7', 'idea-summary-v8')):\nsrc/hivemind/idea.py:341:    if cfg.idea_summary is not None:\nsrc/hivemind/idea.py:343:        summary_setting = cfg.idea_summary\nsrc/hivemind/idea.py:359:                                  schema, 'idea_summary', transport, prose)\nscripts/hivemind_api.py:155:    def do_GET(self):\nscripts/hivemind_api.py:161:    def do_POST(self):\nscripts/hivemind_api.py:245:def index_at_start(embed=None):\nscripts/hivemind_api.py:256:def main():\nscripts/hivemind_api.py:280:        if CFG.idea_summary is not None:\nscripts/hivemind_api.py:281:            print(f'analyst summary: {CFG.idea_summary.model} ({CFG.idea_summary.prompt_version}, effort {CFG.idea_summary.reasoning_effort})', flush=True)\nscripts/hivemind_mcp.py:92:def thesis_library(as_of: str = '') -> dict:\n     1\t# Hivemind service: a thesis database with search\n     2\t\n     3\tD76, October 24, 2026; English edition and current-document refresh, October 25 (D163). Alex defined Hivemind as a database with a search engine on top. Its read service lets an agent or page find theses, choose what to use and inspect the state, history and evidence. Hivemind stores shared **theses**, not user ideas, positions or commitments. This distinction replaces the ambiguous use of “thesis” for both in the earlier document. The [historical source](../research/2026-10-25-english/service.original.md) retains prior wording and verification details.\n     4\t\n     5\tThe core read service does not choose or arrange results for a caller. The separate [`POST /ideas` application flow](idea-card.md) discovers candidate theses, then adopts and weights them in a final assessment. The default `poc-v118-idea` configuration uses two discovery calls and one final assessment; older configurations retain their own contracts. The Idea specification owns those steps and their response. The route returns a UI-ready response.\n     6\t\n     7\t## Historical visibility\n     8\t\n     9\tReaders accept an `as_of` calendar day, defaulting to the ledger's last completed day. They do not use today's clock to reinterpret history. A row is visible when its dispatch sequence belongs to an item or daily round dated on or before that day. This applies to theses, switches, judgements, evidence links, sources, replacements, dependencies and resolutions. `history` and `changes` use explicit date spans.\n    10\t\n    11\tThe historical sealed-ledger check found 28 dependency rows and 750 source rows newer than the theses/judgements they attach to; those rows must stay hidden in earlier reads. A later quotation or relationship must not appear in an old snapshot.\n    12\t\n    13\t## Interfaces and readers\n    14\t\n    15\tField and route names are compatibility identifiers; `view` in an API name means the glossary's **thesis**.\n    16\t\n    17\t| Interface | Returned content | Reader |\n    18\t|---|---|---|\n    19\t| `search(query, k, as_of, include_closed)` | Query/day, semantic or lexical mode, missing current vectors, ranked results or null; each result includes ID, subject, kind, focus, question, due date, lifecycle, relationships and score components | Caller chooses relevant theses; search evaluation |\n    20\t| `views(object, as_of, include_closed)` | Thesis records | Agent or page |\n    21\t| `view(view_id, as_of)` | Identity, source, dates, ladder, current state or null, dependencies, dependants and counts | Agent or detail panel |\n    22\t| `history(view_id, from_day, to_day)` | Judgements, rung changes, evidence arrivals, replacements and lifecycle switches | History chart and replay |\n    23\t| `evidence(view_id, as_of, tier)` | Evidence in force, original quotes, summaries, tiers, speakers, dates and sources | Agent or evidence list |\n    24\t| `record(view_id, as_of)` | Last completed check with day/round and processed/arriving counts, or null | “Last checked” display |\n    25\t| `changes(since_day, to_day)` | Changed judgements with previous/current positions, reasons and historically visible citations | Polling agent |\n    26\t| `evaluate(view_id, comparator, value_usd, as_of)` | Whether evaluable and why; otherwise claim position, judged position/label/condition and verdict | Numeric claim display |\n    27\t| `thesis_bundles(view_ids, as_of)` / `GET /thesis-bundles?ids=...` | Complete dated bundles with ladder, judgements, historical evidence, sources, dependencies and switches | `fromBundles` in the modular UI |\n    28\t| `thesis_library(as_of)` / `GET /library?as_of=...` | Complete dated library and research groups under the [library envelope](#current-library-envelope-d275) | Library UI and agents |\n    29\t| `POST /ideas` | Idea, search summary, mapped parts and chosen theses, related theses, evaluation, optional bundles, days, trace and cost | Idea application/UI; see its contract |\n    30\t| Derived index | Content hashes, embedding model, vectors, token counts and build timestamps | Search only; not the thesis ledger |\n    31\t\n    32\tThe service returns stored prose as stored. D275 points the read-service defaults at the collected English Jev library and its matching items database, with a separate derived-index directory. Explicit old-ledger paths remain supported. This changes neither matching semantics nor the configured Idea prompt.\n    33\t\n    34\t## Numeric claim evaluation\n    35\t\n    36\tUse structured numeric rung bounds where supplied; the legacy path parses text. Bounds must form an unbroken, non-overlapping partition. Each shared boundary belongs to exactly one band; a lowest money range may begin at zero. A non-money or unparseable ladder returns `evaluable: false` with a reason.\n    37\t\n    38\tLegacy parsing recognises comparator phrases, ranges, postfix bounds and exact amounts. It follows the clauses specifying the amount, ignoring preceding datelines and later remarks. A bare nonzero number is not automatically money; percentages, gigawatts and years are not dollar amounts. Chinese magnitude units remain accepted input. For example, 269.79 hundred-million dollars is exactly $26,979,000,000. The original-language regression strings remain in tests and the historical source document.\n    39\t\n    40\tThe evaluation asks whether every amount in the judged band satisfies the user's claim (`holds`), none does (`not_yet`), or only some do (`borderline`). An equality claim holds only for a singleton amount. Missing judgement returns `not_judged`; an unassigned boundary is not guessed.\n    41\t\n    42\tHistorical validation covered all 43 money ladders selected independently by text pattern and refused six non-money ladders. Boundary, exact-amount and dateline cases remain regression requirements. That result does not validate newly translated English-only bands; D163 must test those separately.\n    43\t\n    44\t## Search contract\n    45\t\n    46\tThe index embeds each thesis's own text, not its evidence. A content hash detects outdated vectors. Search can report semantic mode only when all relevant candidates have usable current vectors; absent, empty or stale vectors require lexical mode and explicit missing-vector reporting. A second unchanged index build embeds nothing. A failed batch reports already stored progress.\n    47\t\n    48\tD91's null means no recorded coverage, not low relevance. D132 checks named subjects using IDs, full names and configured aliases (including products), the text index, and semantic coverage where enabled. An off-subject similarity floor is not a universal relevance threshold: an irrelevant sentence naming NVDA can score above a relevant narrower query. The caller still judges relevance.\n    49\t\n    50\t`--lexical` disables embedding calls throughout startup and requests. Query vectors are cached by text and model. The historical evaluation checks four example questions within their top three accepted matches, plus day-zero coverage; mapper suggestions are not human gold labels.\n    51\t\n    52\t## State × event and failures\n    53\t\n    54\t| State/event | Required behavior |\n    55\t|---|---|\n    56\t| Historical read | Filter every attached value by its own sequence/day, not only the thesis creation date |\n    57\t| Missing thesis | HTTP 404 or MCP tool error |\n    58\t| Invalid parameter | HTTP 400 |\n    59\t| Corrupt judgement | Raise `LedgerError`; HTTP 500, not fabricated state |\n    60\t| Missing/stale vector | Truthful lexical mode and missing-vector list |\n    61\t| Lexical configuration | No embedder invocation |\n    62\t| Read request | No ledger writes; derived index/cache writes remain separate |\n    63\t| Concurrent HTTP requests | Each request owns its SQLite connections |\n    64\t| Embedding failure | Report status/type without exposing the response body or credentials |\n    65\t\n    66\tNo query opens, closes or rejudges a thesis. No read route stores user commitments or performs trades. The ingestion pipeline remains the ledger writer.\n    67\t\n    68\t## Transports and local operation\n    69\t\n    70\t- `scripts/hivemind_mcp.py` exposes the readers as tools over stdio or streamable HTTP at `/mcp`.\n    71\t- `scripts/hivemind_api.py` is the threaded HTTP front, listening on localhost by default.\n    72\t- Both build required index content at startup unless lexical mode is selected.\n    73\t- `Dockerfile`, `Dockerfile.mcp` and `docker-compose.yml` mount the ledger/items read-only and service index/archive storage read-write. Credentials remain server-side and are never included in a bundle.\n    74\t\n    75\tThe October 24 environment check found both containers could answer local HTTP/MCP reads, but the host VPN did not carry Docker VM traffic for external model calls. The recorded options were host networking or an explicitly configured reachable proxy. This is an environment observation, not a current connectivity claim or authorisation to change networking.\n    76\t\n    77\tThe [README](../../README.md#run-the-service-for-testing) owns executable startup and shutdown instructions. The HTTP default is port 8788. MCP defaults to stdio; port 8789 serves `/mcp` only when streamable HTTP is selected. Use `--lexical --config ''` on the HTTP front for reads without model calls; MCP's read-only tool set needs only `--lexical`. Local source databases are required and are not included in a clone.\n    78\t\n    79\tVerification requirements live in `tests/test_service.py`, `tests/test_search.py` and transport/bundle tests. New language behavior must retain their historical visibility, numeric, cache and failure guarantees. The [UI integration](../../poc/ui/README.md) documents the rendering boundary.\n    80\t\n    81\t## Current library envelope (D275)\n    82\t\n    83\t`GET /library?as_of=YYYY-MM-DD` and MCP `thesis_library` return all dated theses, including closed ones, and stored research groups. They call the same read-only bundle writer as `GET /thesis-bundles` / MCP `thesis_bundles`. The complete read is pinned in SQLite read transactions. No search, model call or ledger write occurs. HTTP bundle/library requests do not open an index or model archive.\npoc/ui/src/model/library.js:3:/** All filtering reads the same dated library; no group, score or edge is inferred. */\npoc/ui/src/model/library.js:4:export function librarySelection(\npoc/ui/src/model/library.js:42:export function libraryCounts(data, day = data.as_of) {\npoc/ui/src/model/library.js:43:  const theses = librarySelection(data, { day });\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:4:import { readIdea, readBundles, idsOf, graphOf, ideaCard } from './idea/idea.js';\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:6:import { createIdeaDetail } from './idea/analysis.js';\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:13:} from './idea/composite.js';\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:15:import { advanceIdeaProgress } from './idea/progress.js';\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:16:import { createIdeaComposer } from './components/idea-composer.js';\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:23:const libraryRoot = document.getElementById('library');\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:24:if (input && root && libraryRoot) {\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:32:    const library = createLibrary(libraryRoot, { dataset: data });\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:38:    const libraryRequest = new AbortController();\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:47:    const libraryButton = document.getElementById('show-library');\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:88:      libraryRoot.hidden = false;\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:89:      libraryButton.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'true');\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:93:      library.close();\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:94:      libraryRoot.hidden = true;\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:96:      libraryButton.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'false');\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:107:        app.showGraph({ day: library.getDay() });\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:174:        day: library.getDay(),\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:179:        day: library.getDay(),\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:195:          asOf: library.getDay(),\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:256:        const response = await fetch(`${API}/library`, { signal: libraryRequest.signal });\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:259:        if (next.coverage !== 'library')\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:260:          throw new Error('The service did not return a complete library');\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:261:        if (libraryRequest.signal.aborted) return;\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:262:        library.setDataset(next, { day: next.as_of }); // the supplied snapshot defines the displayed date (thesis-ui.md)\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:270:    libraryButton.addEventListener('click', showLibrary);\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:276:        libraryRequest.abort();\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:277:        library.destroy();\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:292:    libraryRoot.append(message);\npoc/ui/src/components/library.js:2:import { librarySelection, libraryCounts } from '../model/library.js';\npoc/ui/src/components/library.js:11:/** A read-only, dated library. Networking and Idea requests belong to its host. */\npoc/ui/src/components/library.js:15:  const scope = `library-${++nextId}`;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
