{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'reserve|ledger|guard|price|cost' docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/{run-old*,*launch*} scripts/cost_report.py src/hivemind/{model,jev}.py; rg -n 'upstream|schedule|current|implement|auth|health|notify' README.md docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/live-service/{OPERATING-CONTRACT.md,RESULT.md} docs/prd/README.md; rg --files .github | head -70; rg --files | rg -i 'ingest|corpus|cron|scheduler|snapshot' | head -65\"","aggregated_output":"zsh:1: no matches found: docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/run-old*\nrg: docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/live-service/RESULT.md: No such file or directory (os error 2)\ndocs/prd/README.md:33:Correct inconsistencies and list what changed and why. Update decisions and current state in the same slice.\nREADME.md:18:| Work on this repository | [Working rules](AGENTS.md), [current state](docs/CURRENT_STATE.md) and [decisions](docs/DECISIONS.md) |\nREADME.md:40:  ↓ determines what upstream supplies\nREADME.md:60:The thesis has one current state: a rung on its ladder. A dependency means one thesis reads another's conclusion when judged. Succession records which period follows which. A research group collects the questions that track one ongoing matter; extraction declares it (D165), and it is distinct from a dependency or duplicate identity.\nREADME.md:70:## Design and implementation status\nREADME.md:72:The foundational design was frozen on October 22, 2026; later decisions authorize specific changes and the POC build. A design freeze does not imply that the implementation has passed acceptance. Changes to a frozen module require a recorded decision.\nREADME.md:114:Then restart the API in a new dated service folder (below) so the search index is built for the new ledger. The current default, `served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828`, is the three-month NVDA run (`poc-v34`, extraction v18) stopped and sealed at 2026-08-28 on evidence bloat (D358); its folder README names the one empty thesis removed.\nREADME.md:144:python3 -m pip download mcp==1.26.0 --dest build/wheels --only-binary=:all: --platform manylinux2014_aarch64 --platform manylinux_2_17_aarch64 --platform any --python-version 3.12 --implementation cp --abi cp312 --abi abi3 --abi none   # once, for the MCP image\nREADME.md:154:Replay writes a new thesis ledger and model-call archive. Before a paid run, replay the relevant saved answers through the current checks at no model cost:\nREADME.md:163:Inspect changed refusals before continuing. A replay is a paid run: it starts only when authorized, in a new dated folder, with the agreed spending cap. The default starts without seeded questions and can read an existing article-created library:\nREADME.md:196:| `AGENTS.md` | Working rules: authority, diagnosing, design, code, tests, verification, writing prompts, measuring and iterating; `CLAUDE.md` points to it |\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/live-service/OPERATING-CONTRACT.md:47:2. **One committed state per request, one connection per concurrent request** (detailed in council rounds 125 and 126).\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/live-service/OPERATING-CONTRACT.md:60:     - The instructions name the day: \"objects as of <day>, when this server started; every tool reads the current last completed\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/live-service/OPERATING-CONTRACT.md:294:   - two concurrent searches for one new query: both answers are well formed, and the cache holds one vector for it; no equality with\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/live-service/OPERATING-CONTRACT.md:381:- **Not deployed:** no running service is restarted. D439 does not authorize a deploy, and the change reaches the running product\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/live-service/OPERATING-CONTRACT.md:581:   tool functions are called in-process. This exercises the tools' implementation, not the MCP transport, which stays a stated\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/live-service/OPERATING-CONTRACT.md:596:**Concurrent reads.** A poller asks `GET /library` back to back from the API's start to the writer's return. The harness brackets\nrg: .github: IO error for operation on .github: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nscripts/snapshot_store.py\ndocs/poc/corpus-plan.md\npoc/reports/2026-10-25-ingestion-smoke/results.md\ndocs/research/2026-10-25-ingestion-smoke/plan.md\ndocs/research/2026-10-25-ingestion-smoke/source-review.md\npoc/corpus/scripts/topics.json\npoc/corpus/scripts/sweep_pages.py\npoc/corpus/scripts/harvest_nvidianews.py\npoc/corpus/scripts/backfill-gdelt.sh\npoc/corpus/scripts/author-table.json\npoc/corpus/scripts/harvest_extra.py\npoc/corpus/scripts/harvest_gnews.py\npoc/corpus/scripts/companies.json\npoc/corpus/scripts/harvest_edgar.py\npoc/corpus/scripts/test_clean.py\npoc/corpus/scripts/common.py\npoc/corpus/scripts/resolve_gnews.py\npoc/corpus/scripts/test_labels.py\npoc/corpus/scripts/fetch_bodies.py\npoc/corpus/scripts/assemble.py\npoc/corpus/scripts/review.py\npoc/corpus/scripts/freeze_window.sh\npoc/corpus/scripts/extra-urls.json\npoc/corpus/scripts/clean_pages.py\npoc/corpus/scripts/freeze_nvda_window.sh\npoc/corpus/scripts/overnight.sh\npoc/corpus/scripts/harvest_gdelt.py\npoc/corpus/scripts/harvest_official.py\npoc/corpus/scripts/relabel.py\npoc/corpus/scripts/harvest_gnews_topics.py\npoc/corpus/scripts/requirements.txt\npoc/corpus/scripts/harvest_edgar_peers.py\npoc/corpus/scripts/regenerate_text.py\npoc/corpus/scripts/harvest_nvblog.py\npoc/corpus/scripts/backfill.sh\npoc/corpus/scripts/harvest_truenorth.py\npoc/corpus/manifest.md\npoc/corpus/README.md\npoc/corpus/sample.md\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/unsigned-deals/snapshot-acceptance-2026-09-07.json\npoc/reports/2026-10-25-ohio-grouping-01/post-run-source-snapshot.json\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/identity-probe/snapshot-c3-2026-07-14.json\npoc/reports/