   80\t2026-09-17 | items  32 extracted  29 merged  3 skipped  0 failed  0 | evidence  43 new views  0 judged  40 changed  17 closed 0 | open views 46 | day $0.13 total $6.97 calls 8617\n    81\t2026-09-18 | items  43 extracted  39 merged  4 skipped  0 failed  0 | evidence 117 new views  0 judged  41 changed  16 closed 0 | open views 46 | day $0.17 total $7.14 calls 8816\n    82\t2026-09-19 | items  34 extracted  29 merged  5 skipped  0 failed  0 | evidence  42 new views  0 judged  42 changed  17 closed 0 | open views 46 | day $0.14 total $7.28 calls 8929\n    83\t2026-09-20 | items  34 extracted  28 merged  6 skipped  0 failed  0 | evidence  33 new views  0 judged  40 changed  15 closed 1 | open views 45 | day $0.13 total $7.40 calls 9030\n    84\ttotals: {'items': 2077, 'extracted': 1884, 'skipped': 0, 'merged': 193, 'not_processed': 0, 'returned': 0, 'failed': 0, 'evidence': 5406, 'new_views': 47, 'judged': 1609, 'changed': 832, 'closed': 2}\n    85\tledger: {'ceiling': 25.0, 'spent': 9.83343153399997, 'reserved': 2.1163626406917047e-16, 'overrun': False, 'refused': 0, 'attempts': 9031, 'stopped': False, 'stop_reason': None, 'launchers': {'old-1': '/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/launch.lock'}}\n5:  python3 scripts/cost_report.py /abs/run-dir [/abs/run-dir ...]\n17:def price(run):\nrg: docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/launch.py: No such file or directory (os error 2)\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/launch_comparison.py\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/census/launches.jsonl\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/census/third/claude--huawei-ascend-960dt-launch--claude.json\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/census/third/claude--huawei-ascend-960dt-launch--codex.json\n81:- **Verdict: not clear. The next small step targets the largest difference observed, not a choice of system.**\n89:## The largest difference observed\n109:  frozen question gold marks optional (may_open).\n     1\t# POC 第一步：NVDA 过去 90 天的素材库\n     2\t\n     3\t2026-10-23。Alex 的话：先把过去九十天的材料完整准备好，新闻一类、财报一类，大量地抓，不管费用，自己审视一遍，再建管线。观点的数量不设限，由模型定。这份是素材库怎么建、建成什么样、怎么审。\n     4\t\n     5\t## 一句话\n     6\t\n     7\t把 2026-07-24 到 2026-10-22 这 90 天里关于 NVDA 的材料全部抓下来，分成两类，新闻和公司材料（财报、申报、电话会、公司发布），每条带发布日、来源、原文，存成一个测试库。不调模型，不筛内容，相关不相关由后面的管线判。\n     8\t\n     9\t## 从哪抓，能抓到什么（今天探过的）\n    10\t\n    11\t| 来源 | 给什么 | 量 | 限制 |\n    12\t|---|---|---|---|\n    13\t| SEC EDGAR（公开，免费） | 申报全文和附件：10-Q、8-K 正文、业绩稿（99.1）、CFO 评论 | 窗口内 4 份申报（8-17 8-K、8-26 8-K 和 10-Q、9-3 8-K），加开题用的 2-25（10-K、8-K）、5-20（10-Q、8-K） | 无 |\n    14\t| TrueNorth（团队的数据服务，旧仓库的只读客户端） | 电话会文字稿全文（每份约 4.7 万字符）；申报全文（10-Q 约 15 万字符）；新闻故事：标题、约 300 字摘要、来源链接，同一事件的多家报道已聚成一条 | 文字稿 3 份（2-25、5-20、8-26）；新闻 90 天共 279 条故事 | 新闻只有摘要没有正文；只回溯 90 天，每天少一天 |\n    15\t| GDELT（公开，免费） | 每天的英文新闻链接、标题、域名、时间 | 忙的日子一天超过 250 条，要按小时切；90 天估计 1 到 2 万条链接，去重后约一半 | 每 5 秒最多一次请求；只给链接，正文要自己去抓 |\n    16\t| NVIDIA 新闻室 | 公司新闻稿全文 | 窗口内估计 100 到 150 篇 | 要翻页 |\n    17\t| Google News RSS | 每天 100 条标题和来源名 | 只用来核对覆盖，不当正文来源 | 链接是 Google 的跳转页，拿不到真实地址 |\n    18\t| Distilla | 新闻标题加摘要、文件 | 这个账号本月配额用完，11 月 1 日恢复 | 暂不用 |\n    19\t\n    20\t正文抓取：GDELT 的链接逐条去抓网页，抽正文段落；抓不到的（付费墙、反爬）留标题和摘要，标明只有部分。\n    21\t\n    22\t## 素材必须是原件（Alex 2026-10-23：\"要像是原始数据……不能是你自己已经处理过的\"）\n    23\t\n    24\t管线要读的是原件，不是我或别人处理过的东西，处理过的就已经是观点了。所以：\n    25\t\n    26\t- 每条材料存两样：抓回来的原样文件（HTML、JSON）和整页转成的纯文本，转的时候只去掉脚本和样式，一个字不删，导航、页脚都留着，由管线自己读。\n    27\t- 我写的「抽文章段落」只用来给审视报表估算正文有多少，另存一栏，不进管线。\n    28\t- TrueNorth 新闻故事自带的摘要是它家模型写的，不是原件：只当目录，正文去原始链接抓；抓不到的标「只有供应商摘要」，不进管线，只在报表里数。\n    29\t- Codex 用网搜列的大事件表和高管露面表，只用来核对覆盖，不进管线。\n    30\t- 按分类 PRD 的规则贴 T 类标签、标「同一篇的转载」，是上游分类该做的事，不动内容。\n    31\t- 测试库里每条有一个 `feed` 标记：原件齐全的为 1，管线只读这些。\n    32\t\n    33\t## 扩成完整数据集（Alex 2026-10-23：\"这肯定不够……半导体行业的、宏观经济的、战争供应链相关的……甚至噪音……起码多两倍\"）\n    34\t\n    35\t只有标题带 Nvidia 的材料撑不起管线要开的主题观点（出口管制、AI 资本开支、半导体周期、利率、地缘），也测不出「不该抽的不抽」。所以加四层，每条都标「哪个话题抓来的」和「讲的是哪个对象」（公司代码或主题编号），正文一样是整页原件：\n    36\t\n    37\t| 层 | 内容 | 来源 | 量级 |\n    38\t|---|---|---|---|\n    39\t| 产业链 | TSMC、AMD、Broadcom、Micron/SK Hynix/三星存储、ASML、Intel/Arm/高通、半导体板块；四大云厂商和 Oracle、CoreWeave、OpenAI 的资本开支；自研芯片；数据中心电力；AI 泡沫争论 | Google News 13 组话题，每组每天 10–20 条；14 家公司窗口内的申报和附件（EDGAR）；13 份电话会文字稿（TrueNorth） | 新闻约 1.5 万条标题，申报约 100 份 |\n    40\t| 宏观 | 美联储议息和讲话、CPI、非农、国债收益率、关税、衰退 | Google News 5 组话题；官方原文：美联储新闻稿、讲话、证词（RSS），BLS 的 CPI、PPI、非农发布稿 | 新闻约 5 千条，官方原文几十份 |\n    41\t| 地缘和供应链 | 对华芯片管制和中国国产芯片、台海、中东和油价、俄乌、稀土和航运 | Google News 5 组话题；联邦公报里 BIS、USTR、商务部的文件原文（公开 API） | 新闻约 5 千条，公报文件几十份 |\n    42\t| 噪音 | 消费、娱乐、加密货币、房贷、医药、体育、天气 | Google News 3 组话题，每组每天 5–8 条 | 约 2 千条 |\n    43\t\n    44\t对照 NVDA 核心层的约 7 千条，合计约三倍以上。Google News 的链接要先解析成真实地址再抓整页，这一步最慢，通宵跑。\n    45\t\n    46\t## 两类材料，每条带什么\n    47\t\n    48\t| 类 | 包括 | 细标签（分类 PRD 的 16 类，当属性留着） |\n    49\t|---|---|---|\n    50\t| 公司材料 | 业绩稿、10-Q、10-K、8-K 正文和附件、电话会文字稿、公司新闻稿 | T1 业绩发布、T2 定期报告、T4 电话会、T6 公司其他发布 |\n    51\t| 新闻 | 媒体报道、评论和分析、通稿转载 | T7 新闻、T8 观点与分析（作者是分析方或个人的） |\n    52\t\n    53\t每条按分类 PRD 的字段存：编号、内容指纹、渠道、原始地址、作者、作者类型、发布时间、发布日（纽约时间）、取得时间、形式、体裁、相关对象（NVDA）、正文或摘要、正文是全的还是部分的。\n    54\t\n    55\t去重：同一个链接只收一次；同一天同一标题同一作者的算同一条的另一个出处；aol、yahoo 这类转载站的文章，标题和原作者对得上的，并到原作者那条。\n    56\t\n    57\t## 存在哪\n    58\t\n    59\t```\n    60\tpoc/corpus/\n    61\t  raw/edgar/ raw/truenorth/ raw/gdelt/ raw/nvidianews/ raw/gnews/ raw/pages/   # 抓回来的原样\n    62\t  items.sqlite        # 整理后的测试库：一条材料一行，带上面的字段\n    63\t  manifest.md         # 每天每类多少条、来源分布、正文抓取成功率、空白日、失败清单\n    64\t  scripts/            # 抓取和整理的脚本，都能重跑，已抓的不再抓\n    65\t```\n    66\t\n    67\t## 怎么审（建完我自己做，再给 Alex 看）\n    68\t\n    69\t1. 每天两类各多少条，画成一张表；有没有一天新闻是零。\n    70\t2. 大事件在不在：8-26 财报和电话会、9-3 的 8-K、窗口内每一次股价单日涨跌超过 4% 的那天有没有对应的新闻。\n     1\t# The corpus toolchain\n     2\t\n     3\tRaw harvest in `raw/` (listings, resolved links, fetched pages with their HTML under `raw/pages/`, EDGAR, official\n     4\tnotices, company blogs). Scripts in `scripts/`:\n     5\t\n     6\t| step | script | writes |\n     7\t|---|---|---|\n     8\t| harvest | `harvest_*.py`, `resolve_gnews.py`, `fetch_bodies.py` | `raw/` (resumable; window from `HIVEMIND_WINDOW_START/END`) |\n     9\t| assemble | `assemble.py` | `items.sqlite`: one row per document, whole-page text (`common.page_text`), labels |\n    10\t| freeze | `relabel.py --in items.sqlite --out poc/data/<name>.page.sqlite` | the window a run reads, whole pages as fetched |\n    11\t| clean (D351) | `clean_pages.py --in <name>.page.sqlite --out <name>.sqlite` | the source every script reads: line rules plus the trafilatura extractor over the stored HTML; the page stays in `text_page`, counts in `cleaning` |\n    12\t| check | `check_corpus.py` (worktree, `docs/research/2026-10-27-nvda-3m/`), `sweep_pages.py` | per-day feed counts; a census of what still looks like junk |\n    13\t| all of it | `freeze_window.sh <name> <from> <until>` | the chain above into new dated files |\n    14\t\n    15\tTests: `python3 -m pytest poc/corpus/scripts/test_labels.py poc/corpus/scripts/test_clean.py -q`. Dependency of the corpus\n    16\tscripts only: `pip3 install -r poc/corpus/scripts/requirements.txt`. The cleaning's numbers and audits:\n    17\t`poc/reports/items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27-cleaned.census.md`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"head -3 poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/ledgers/old-1.attempts.jsonl | cut -c1-450; nl -ba scripts/cost_report.py; rg -n 'budgeted replay|Budgeted|def.*cost|price\\\\(' docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/launch_comparison.py clean-arch -g '*.py' | head -45; rg -n 'refused|rejected|Retry|failed|error' poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod.log | rg -v 'failed  0|not_processed|ceiling' | head -25; ls poc/data | rg 'accept|week|comparison|v118'; rg -n 'p[1-3]/prod|golden-v5|score_evidence_gold' clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13 -g '*.md' | cut -c1-290 | head -40\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"head -3 poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/ledgers/old-1.attempts.jsonl | cut -c1-450; nl -ba scripts/cost_report.py; rg -n 'budgeted replay|Budgeted|def.*cost|price\\\\(' docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/launch_comparison.py clean-arch -g '*.py' | head -45; rg -n 'refused|rejected|Retry|failed|error' poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod.log | rg -v 'failed  0|not_processed|ceiling' | head -25; ls poc/data | rg 'accept|week|comparison|v118'; rg -n 'p[1-3]/prod|golden-v5|score_evidence_gold' clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13 -g '*.md' | cut -c1-290 | head -40\"","aggregated_output":"{\"kind\": \"llm\", \"reserved\": 0.014791, \"charged\": 0.00067851, \"pid\": 43600, \"at\": \"2026-11-17T22:36:18-0800\"}\n{\"kind\": \"llm\", \"reserved\": 0.0103966, \"charged\": 0.00044151000000000005, \"pid\": 43600, \"at\": \"2026-11-17T22:36:19-0800\"}\n{\"kind\": \"llm\", \"reserved\": 0.010286400000000001, \"charged\": 0.00049751, \"pid\": 43600, \"at\": \"2026-11-17T22:36:20-0800\"}\n     1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n     2\t\"\"\"Price a run's model calls from its archive at the published rates (model.PRICES; cached input at CACHED_INPUT_SHARE), per\n     3\tpurpose and model, and print a Markdown table. The token columns are the measurement; the provider's bill is the truth.\n     4\t\n     5\t  python3 scripts/cost_report.py /abs/run-dir [/abs/run-dir ...]\n     6\t\"\"\"\n     7\timport json\n     8\timport os\n     9\timport sqlite3\n    10\timport sys\n    11\t\n    12\tROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))\n    13\tsys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(ROOT, 'src'))\n    14\tfrom hivemind import model  # noqa: E402\n    15\t\n    16\t\n    17\tdef price(run):\n    18\t    archive = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{run}/archive.sqlite?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    19\t    rows = {}\n    20\t    for purpose, name, response, input_tokens, output_tokens in archive.execute('select purpose, model, response_json, input_tokens, output_tokens from model_calls'):\n    21\t        try:\n    22\t            usage = json.loads(response).get('usage') or {}\n    23\t        except (TypeError, ValueError):\n    24\t            usage = {}\n    25\t        cached = min(input_tokens or 0, int((usage.get('prompt_tokens_details') or {}).get('cached_tokens') or 0))\n    26\t        if name.startswith('jev'):\n    27\t            input_tokens = int(usage.get('input_tokens') or input_tokens or 0)\n    28\t        d = rows.setdefault((purpose, name), {'calls': 0, 'input': 0, 'cached': 0, 'output': 0})\n    29\t        d['calls'] += 1\n    30\t        d['input'] += input_tokens or 0\n    31\t        d['cached'] += cached\n    32\t        d['output'] += output_tokens or 0\n    33\t    lines = ['| purpose | model | calls | input tokens | of them cached | output tokens | USD |', '|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|']\n    34\t    total = 0.0\n    35\t    for (purpose, name), d in sorted(rows.items()):\n    36\t        price_in, price_out = model.PRICES.get(name, (0.0, 0.0))\n    37\t        usd = (d['input'] - d['cached']) / 1e6 * price_in + d['cached'] / 1e6 * price_in * model.CACHED_INPUT_SHARE + d['output'] / 1e6 * price_out\n    38\t        total += usd\n    39\t        lines.append(f\"| {purpose} | {name} | {d['calls']} | {d['input']:,} | {d['cached']:,} | {d['output']:,} | {usd:.3f} |\")\n    40\t    lines.append(f'| **total** | | | | | | **{total:.3f}** |')\n    41\t    return '\\n'.join(lines), total\n    42\t\n    43\t\n    44\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n    45\t    for run in sys.argv[1:]:\n    46\t        table, total = price(run)\n    47\t        print(f'## {os.path.basename(run.rstrip(\"/\"))}\\n\\n{table}\\n')\nclean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/test_ladder_step.py:587:def test_check_8_an_answer_that_cannot_be_read_is_refused_and_sent_back_and_its_text_and_cost_are_kept(tmp_path, unreadable):\nclean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_a/test_stage_a.py:146:    def costly_transport(provider, request):\nclean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_b/build_baseline.py:37:        'reasons': 'The reference is NVIDIA’s forecast that the big four hyperscalers’ 2027 data-center capex will exceed $1 trillion, which is rung 5. Microsoft and Meta have said they will defer about $150 billion of 2027 data-center spending to 2028, which takes the implied total to about $850 billion, in rung 3. The AWS GPU deployment plan spans 2027–2028 and does not offset the deferral; rack-cost estimates and tight computing capacity lean toward higher spending but do not establish a different total. The NVIDIA revenue dependency v2 is not yet judged and supplies no input.',\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/identity-probe/test_probe_identity.py:32:def test_real_usage_settles_at_its_token_price():\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:240:def llm_cost(response, request):\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:365:    log(f'--- budgeted replay {args.from_day}..{args.until_day} config {cfg.version}/{cfg.checksum} provider {cfg.provider} universe {uni.version} '\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/identity-probe/probe_identity.py:127:    def cost_of(self, usage):\nclean-arch/e2e-2026-11-09/budget.py:30:def worst_cost(request):\nclean-arch/e2e-2026-11-09/budget.py:41:def cost(request, response):\nclean-arch/step1/live.py:1:\"\"\"Budgeted use of the repository's existing transport for OpenAI Luna and, in JSON mode, DeepSeek.\"\"\"\nclean-arch/step1/live.py:108:def ledger_cost(request, response, estimated):\nclean-acceptance-2026-11-09\nclean-e2e-comparison-2026-11-13\nclean-lean-week-2026-11-14\nclean-second-week-2026-11-15\nclean-step1-source-text-comparison-2026-11-07\ncomparison-2026-11-17\nenglish-v32-nvda-week-2026-10-27\nenglish-v33-nvda-week-2026-10-27\nenglish-v34-nvda-week-2026-10-27\nenglish-v34b-nvda-week-2026-10-27\nenglish-v34c-nvda-week-2026-10-27\nrun-v14-week.out\nrun-v14-week.pid\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"agent_message","text":"All three v118 replays finished the 82-day window. The page and tools still default to the older sealed library, so the replay result and the live handoff need separate checks."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/live-service/OPERATING-CONTRACT.md | sed -n '348,396p;583,640p'; nl -ba scripts/snapshot_store.py | head -90; nl -ba scripts/replay.py | sed -n '46,100p'; rg -n 'EMBEDDING_MODEL|def _|def read_idea' src/hivemind/{idea,search}.py | rg 'idea\\\\.py:(1[0-9][0-9]|2[0-9][0-9])|EMBEDDING_MODEL'; rg -n 'def |mod|MATCH|COLLIS' src/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py | tail -42; rg -n 'collision|search_top_n|reasoning_effort' src/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py src/hivemind/jev.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/live-service/OPERATING-CONTRACT.md | sed -n '348,396p;583,640p'; nl -ba scripts/snapshot_store.py | head -90; nl -ba scripts/replay.py | sed -n '46,100p'; rg -n 'EMBEDDING_MODEL|def _|def read_idea' src/hivemind/{idea,search}.py | rg 'idea\\\\.py:(1[0-9][0-9]|2[0-9][0-9])|EMBEDDING_MODEL'; rg -n 'def |mod|MATCH|COLLIS' src/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py | tail -42; rg -n 'collision|search_top_n|reasoning_effort' src/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py src/hivemind/jev.py\"","aggregated_output":"   348\t  - The check's own mutant (a new public function without the call) must fail it.\n   349\t\n   350\t**The response, per channel.**\n   351\t\n   352\t| Channel | First day not completed | Bound after the last completed day | Range start not before its end |\n   353\t|---|---|---|---|\n   354\t| API | 503 `{\"error\": \"the store's first day has not completed\"}` | 409 `{\"error\": \"day not completed\", \"requested\": X, \"last_completed_day\": Y}` | 409 `{\"error\": \"range start after its end\", \"start\": S, \"end\": T}` |\n   355\t| MCP tools | a tool error whose message carries the same fields | the same | the same |\n   356\t| Streamed Idea route | the status and body, before any header | the same | — |\n   357\t\n   358\t- `error_response` returns `(status, payload)`. The three new exceptions get the payloads above, and every other error keeps\n   359\t  `{\"error\": message}`. `_answer` and `_stream_answer` send the payload as given.\n   360\t- **The streamed route, in one transaction:**\n   361\t  - it opens its connections, begins the read transaction and resolves the bound and first-day check;\n   362\t  - **only then** does it send its 200 headers and run the Idea work in the same transaction, which it ends after;\n   363\t  - a refusal is sent as a normal status and body before any header.\n   364\t  - The Idea work includes model calls, so this transaction lasts the whole request, up to minutes. That is within row 5's\n   365\t    one-request rule, and it holds back a checkpoint that long.\n   366\t\n   367\t**Callers.**\n   368\t\n   369\t- **The page, when its live library read succeeds:** it sends only days from the served dataset (`library.getDay()` to `/ideas`;\n   370\t  the returned `card.idea.as_of` to `/thesis-bundles`). These are never after the last completed day.\n   371\t- **The page, when its live library read fails:**\n   372\t  - it keeps its embedded snapshot silently (as `thesis-ui.md` specifies), and that snapshot's day can be later than the service's\n   373\t    last completed day;\n   374\t  - `/ideas` is then refused with 409, and the page shows its existing Idea error naming no day;\n   375\t  - this is documented here and tested; it is not claimed impossible.\n   376\t- **MCP clients and direct API users with a later date:**\n   377\t  - on the running product's store, they would get an error naming 2026-08-28 instead of today's half-processed 2026-08-29 (99\n   378\t    evidence records, 117 links);\n   379\t  - on a finished store, they would get an error instead of today's identical answer.\n   380\t  - This is the behaviour change, recorded for Alex.\n   381\t- **Not deployed:** no running service is restarted. D439 does not authorize a deploy, and the change reaches the running product\n   382\t  only on a restart, which is on Alex's page.\n   383\t\n   384\t**Proofs added to the plan (2b to 2e):**\n   385\t\n   386\t- 2b. The structural check, and its mutant.\n   387\t- 2c. Each public function called directly with a future bound, an omitted one and a past one, on the four store states (finished,\n   388\t  partial, first day, empty with tables) and a copy of the served store's state. Each call's actual output or error is compared\n   389\t  with the expected one: today's recorded output where the rule keeps it, the named refusal where the rule changes it.\n   390\t- 2c′. `view_bundle` and `not_judged` called directly for a view created after the resolved day are refused (404). `days()` on an\n   391\t  empty store returns `[]` as today.\n   392\t- 2d. The ranges: a start after its end is refused for both; equality reads as before (`changes` empty, `history` that day).\n   393\t- 2e. The streamed route on a first-day store and with a future date: a status before any header. With a writer committing during\n   394\t  an Idea request, the request's data are the state at its start.\n   395\t- 2f. The page verifier (`poc/ui/verify-*.mjs`): live read successful, then the Idea call succeeds; live read failed with a later\n   396\t  embedded day, then the Idea error shows and nothing else breaks.\n   583\t   - On the first day, its instructions say no day has completed, and `thesis_library()` and `views()` refuse.\n   584\t   - Afterwards, `thesis_library()`'s day and view ids equal `/library`'s.\n   585\t3. **Lock and copies:**\n   586\t   - `live_lock.acquire` is refused, and so is preflight's `store_copies`, which names the snapshot route;\n   587\t   - the store is in WAL mode.\n   588\t4. **Snapshots in two distinct states:**\n   589\t   - **2026-09-25 before judging, a day's articles committed and the day not completed:** the copy's last day is 2026-09-24 and it\n   590\t     holds processing steps dated 2026-09-25;\n   591\t   - **2027-01-31 before close, a due-day closing not yet completed (no articles that day):** the copy's last day is 2027-01-30 and\n   592\t     none of the three questions due that day (v3, v4, v7) is closed in it. A switch has no day of its own, so the first run's query\n   593\t     of a day column failed: my error, the harness's, not the product's.\n   594\t   - Both copies are out of WAL mode, with integrity `ok`.\n   595\t\n   596\t**Concurrent reads.** A poller asks `GET /library` back to back from the API's start to the writer's return. The harness brackets\n   597\teach day's completion with the times just before and just after `close_and_complete`. For every answer:\n   598\t\n   599\t- the status is 200, or 503 only for a request sent before the first day's completion ended;\n   600\t- the day it serves completed no later than the answer arrived (the day's completion started before the answer was received);\n   601\t- it is no older than the last day whose completion had ended before the request was sent;\n   602\t- the days never go backwards;\n   603\t- after the run, `GET /library?as_of=<that day>` decodes to the same JSON (compared by a hash of its canonical form). The first\n   604\t  difference is read before anything is called a leak; this is a test of the historical filter, not a guarantee row 3 already\n   605\t  gives.\n   606\t- **The polling must not be vacuous:** at least 20 answers, and at least one day whose completion has answers on both sides (one\n   607\t  served an earlier day and arrived before the completion started; one served that day or later).\n   608\t\n   609\t**After the writer ends:**\n   610\t\n   611\t- the lock is free;\n   612\t- the store is out of WAL mode, or WAL is kept with \"another connection held the store at the end\" recorded (the poller may hold a\n   613\t  read at that moment);\n   614\t- the API answers as of the store's last completed day.\n   615\t\n   616\t**It exits 1 unless every check holds.** A failure is read to its first differing value before anything is changed.\n   617\t\n   618\t## Slice 5: row 1's reader rules and the proofs still open (council rounds 143 and 144)\n   619\t\n   620\t**Row 1, made true in code** (a product change: today readers set no busy timeout of their own, and a failed open names no path):\n   621\t\n   622\t- **One opener for a reader's pinned state:** `service.open_pinned(path)` opens with `mode=ro`, runs `BEGIN` and the first read, and\n   623\t  returns the connection. The API's `Connections` and MCP's `connections()` both call it, replacing their own copies of those three\n   624\t  steps.\n   625\t- **Loud, with the store's path:** if the open, the `BEGIN` or the first read fails with a SQLite error, `open_pinned` closes what it\n   626\t  opened and raises `service.StoreUnreadable(\"<path>: <SQLite's message>\")`, a `LedgerError`.\n   627\t  - The API answers 500 with that message, before any header on the streamed route.\n   628\t  - MCP raises it from the tool.\n   629\t  - It never serves an empty or stale answer in its place.\n   630\t- **An explicit busy timeout:** `store.open_read_only` connects with `timeout=READ_BUSY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` (5 s, the value Python\n   631\t  applied by default until now). SQLite's busy handler retries `SQLITE_BUSY` within it; there is no application-level retry, and\n   632\t  row 1's wording is narrowed to say so.\n   633\t\n   634\t**Tests, at $0:**\n   635\t\n   636\t- **6a.** A WAL store whose side files are absent, in a read-only directory:\n   637\t  - `open_pinned` raises `StoreUnreadable` naming the path;\n   638\t  - `GET /days` answers 500 with the path;\n   639\t  - the streamed Idea route answers 500 before any header;\n   640\t  - an MCP tool raises it.\n     1\t\"\"\"A snapshot of a store, even while it is written (AGENTS §9's route; live-service/OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 7): SQLite's backup API,\n     2\ttaken out of WAL mode, integrity checked, published at a new path without replacing anything. Nothing is left on failure.\n     3\t\n     4\t  python3 scripts/snapshot_store.py <store> <new destination>\n     5\t\"\"\"\n     6\timport os\n     7\timport sqlite3\n     8\timport sys\n     9\t\n    10\tsys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))), 'src'))\n    11\tfrom hivemind import live_lock  # noqa: E402\n    12\t\n    13\t\n    14\tdef main(arguments):\n    15\t    if len(arguments) != 2:\n    16\t        print(__doc__, file=sys.stderr)\n    17\t        return 2\n    18\t    try:\n    19\t        destination = live_lock.snapshot(arguments[0], arguments[1])\n    20\t    except (OSError, RuntimeError, sqlite3.Error) as error:          # LockRefused is a RuntimeError\n    21\t        print(f'snapshot refused: {error}', file=sys.stderr)\n    22\t        return 1\n    23\t    print(f'snapshot: {destination}')\n    24\t    return 0\n    25\t\n    26\t\n    27\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n    28\t    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))\n    46\t                raise SystemExit(f'existing ledger has {seeded} seeded questions; use a clean ledger')\n    47\t    except sqlite3.Error as error:\n    48\t        raise SystemExit(f'cannot inspect existing ledger: {error}') from error\n    49\t\n    50\t\n    51\tdef main():\n    52\t    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    53\t    parser.add_argument('--from', dest='from_day', required=True)\n    54\t    parser.add_argument('--until', dest='until_day', required=True)\n    55\t    parser.add_argument('--day0', default=None)\n    56\t    parser.add_argument('--testdb', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite'))\n    57\t    parser.add_argument('--views', required=True, help='the ledger this run writes (a new run: a new dated folder)')\n    58\t    parser.add_argument('--archive', required=True, help='the model-call archive of this run')\n    59\t    parser.add_argument('--config', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'config', 'poc-v118.json'))\n    60\t    parser.add_argument('--universe', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'universe.json'))\n    61\t    parser.add_argument('--only', default=None, help='comma-separated object ids to restrict the stream to')\n    62\t    parser.add_argument('--cap', type=float, default=None, help='USD spend cap for this run')\n    63\t    parser.add_argument('--max-items-per-day', type=int, default=None)\n    64\t    parser.add_argument('--workers', type=int, default=16, help='extraction requests prepared at a time (D183); 1 is the serial path')\n    65\t    parser.add_argument('--jev-workers', type=int, default=None,\n    66\t                        help='Jev matching questions sent at a time when --workers > 1; default 8 for Jev, 1 for another engine')\n    67\t    args = parser.parse_args()\n    68\t    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(args.views), exist_ok=True)\n    69\t    log_path = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(args.views), 'replay.log')\n    70\t\n    71\t    def log(*parts):\n    72\t        line = ' '.join(str(p) for p in parts)\n    73\t        print(line, flush=True)\n    74\t        with open(log_path, 'a', encoding='utf-8') as handle:\n    75\t            handle.write(line + '\\n')\n    76\t\n    77\t    cfg = config.load(args.config)\n    78\t    if cfg.baseline is not None:\n    79\t        raise SystemExit(f'config {cfg.version} uses retired seeded-question baseline; select a configuration without it')\n    80\t    refuse_seeded_ledger(args.views)\n    81\t    uni = universe.load(args.universe)\n    82\t    archive = model.Archive(args.archive)\n    83\t    day_runner = None\n    84\t    if args.workers > 1:\n    85\t        jev_workers = args.jev_workers if args.jev_workers is not None else (8 if cfg.matching.engine == 'jev' else 1)\n    86\t        day_runner = parallel_day.ParallelDay(os.path.abspath(args.testdb), os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(args.views)), 'manifests'),\n    87\t                                              extraction_workers=args.workers, jev_workers=jev_workers)\n    88\t    log(f'--- replay {args.from_day}..{args.until_day} config {cfg.version}/{cfg.checksum} provider {cfg.provider} universe {uni.version}'\n    89\t        f' workers {args.workers}')\n    90\t    totals = replay.run(testdb_path=args.testdb, views_path=args.views, archive=archive, cfg=cfg, universe=uni,\n    91\t                        from_day=args.from_day, until_day=args.until_day, day0=args.day0, spend_cap_usd=args.cap, log=log,\n    92\t                        only_objects=set(args.only.split(',')) if args.only else None, max_items_per_day=args.max_items_per_day,\n    93\t                        day_runner=day_runner)\n    94\t    log('totals:', totals)\n    95\t\n    96\t\n    97\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n    98\t    main()\nsrc/hivemind/idea.py:218:def read_idea(ledger, index, items, archive, cfg, text, as_of=None, k=10, aliases=None, semantic=True, transport=None, bundles=True, embed=search.openai_embeddings, on_progress=None):\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:24:EMBEDDING_MODEL = 'text-embedding-3-small'\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:55:def openai_embeddings(texts, embedding_model=EMBEDDING_MODEL, timeout=120):\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:82:def build_index(ledger, index, embed=openai_embeddings, embedding_model=EMBEDDING_MODEL, batch=64):\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:124:def fresh_vectors(ledger, index, embedding_model=EMBEDDING_MODEL, view_ids=None):\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:143:def query_vector(index, query, embed=openai_embeddings, embedding_model=EMBEDDING_MODEL):\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:155:def warm_queries(index, queries, embed=openai_embeddings, embedding_model=EMBEDDING_MODEL):\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:248:def search(ledger, index, query, k=10, as_of=None, include_closed=False, embed=openai_embeddings, embedding_model=EMBEDDING_MODEL, aliases=None, semantic=True):\nsrc/hivemind/search.py:294:def fake_embed(texts, embedding_model=EMBEDDING_MODEL, dims=256):\n14:from .. import config, jev, model, universe as _universe\n19:# ledger, each judged 'new'); the generative model, asked the analyst's question, merged five of six. It is asked only for the theses of\n21:COLLISION_RELATIONS = ['same_question', 'same_question_other_period', 'distinct_question_same_matter', 'different']\n22:COLLISION_SCHEMA = {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': ['relations'],\n24:                                   'properties': {'thesis_id': {'type': 'string'}, 'relation': {'type': 'string', 'enum': COLLISION_RELATIONS}, 'why': {'type': 'string'}}}}}}\n56:def candidate_state(c, evidence):\n64:def thesis_text(conn, view_id):\n71:def group_text(group):\n76:def piece_state(e, said_day):\n80:def relation_question(text):\n85:def member_question(text):\n90:def piece_question(text):\n95:def event_home(conn, view_id, key, c):\n102:def can_succeed(conn, view_id, key, c):\n111:def shared_quantity_target(conn, c):\n128:def succession_target(conn, c, listed):\n129:    \"\"\"The succession code decides alone: the same scope as well (a model-worded scope that differs goes to the judge).\"\"\"\n139:def _summary(answer):\n146:def _answers(archive, cfg, jobs, workers, transport):\n151:    def ask(job):\n162:        _, key = model.request_identity(jev.request_for(cfg.matching, state, questions))\n169:        def fill():\n202:def collision_peers(conn, c, listed):\n212:def ask_collision_judge(archive, cfg, conn, state, peers, llm_transport):\n217:    answer = model.call(archive, cfg, cfg.collision, system, user, COLLISION_SCHEMA, 'collision', 'match', transport=llm_transport)\n221:def decide(archive, cfg, conn, item, candidates, evidence, lists, shown_views, *, extra_views=(), retry_note='', transport=None, llm_transport=None, workers=1):\n247:    def answers_for(index):\nsrc/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:18:# D190: the collision judge. Jev reads wording and calls a population variant of one aggregate 'part of' (six 2026 aggregates on the r3\nsrc/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:202:def collision_peers(conn, c, listed):\nsrc/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:212:def ask_collision_judge(archive, cfg, conn, state, peers, llm_transport):\nsrc/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:214:    with open(config.prompt_path(cfg.collision.prompt_version + '.txt'), encoding='utf-8') as handle:\nsrc/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:217:    answer = model.call(archive, cfg, cfg.collision, system, user, COLLISION_SCHEMA, 'collision', 'match', transport=llm_transport)\nsrc/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:307:            # merges into an amount), and the collision judge below may keep a component apart under its rule.\nsrc/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:322:        peers = collision_peers(conn, c, listed) if getattr(cfg, 'collision', None) else []\nsrc/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:325:            answer, verdicts = ask_collision_judge(archive, cfg, conn, candidate_state(c, evidence), peers, llm_transport)\nsrc/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:333:            judged = '; collision judge: ' + ', '.join(f'{v}: {verdicts.get(v, \"(no answer)\")}' for v in peers)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py | sed -n '220,314p;340,398p'; rg -n 'budget_replay|prod totals|emit|limit|workers' docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/launch_comparison.py; for d in poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-{1,2,3}; do nl -ba \\\"\"'$d/run.json\" | sed -n '\"'14,42p'; nl -ba \\\"\"'$d/prod/replay.log\" | tail -6; done; rg -n '\"'refus|fail|log\\\\(' src/hivemind/views/round.py src/hivemind/{replay,extraction}.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py | sed -n '220,314p;340,398p'; rg -n 'budget_replay|prod totals|emit|limit|workers' docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/launch_comparison.py; for d in poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-{1,2,3}; do nl -ba \\\"\"'$d/run.json\" | sed -n '\"'14,42p'; nl -ba \\\"\"'$d/prod/replay.log\" | tail -6; done; rg -n '\"'refus|fail|log\\\\(' src/hivemind/views/round.py src/hivemind/{replay,extraction}.py\"","aggregated_output":"   220\t            fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\n   221\t            try:\n   222\t                return json.loads(self.path.read_text())\n   223\t            finally:\n   224\t                fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_UN)\n   225\t\n   226\t\n   227\tdef llm_estimate(request):\n   228\t    price_in, price_out = model.PRICES[request['model']]\n   229\t    cap = request.get('max_completion_tokens', request.get('max_tokens'))\n   230\t    if isinstance(cap, bool) or not isinstance(cap, int) or cap <= 0:\n   231\t        raise model.TransportError('request without a positive output cap: refused by the budget')\n   232\t    tokens_in = 2 * len(json.dumps(request).encode('utf-8')) + 4096\n   233\t    return (tokens_in * price_in + cap * price_out) / 1e6\n   234\t\n   235\t\n   236\tdef whole(count):\n   237\t    return isinstance(count, int) and not isinstance(count, bool) and count >= 0\n   238\t\n   239\t\n   240\tdef llm_cost(response, request):\n   241\t    \"\"\"The answer's cost by `model.call`'s formula; None (settled at the reservation) unless the counts are whole, nonnegative numbers\n   242\t    with some input.\"\"\"\n   243\t    usage = response.get('usage') if isinstance(response, dict) else None\n   244\t    if not isinstance(usage, dict):\n   245\t        return None\n   246\t    tokens_in, tokens_out = usage.get('prompt_tokens'), usage.get('completion_tokens')\n   247\t    details = usage.get('prompt_tokens_details') or {}\n   248\t    cached = (details.get('cached_tokens') or 0) if isinstance(details, dict) else None\n   249\t    if not (whole(tokens_in) and whole(tokens_out) and whole(cached)) or tokens_in == 0:\n   250\t        return None\n   251\t    price_in, price_out = model.PRICES[request['model']]\n   252\t    cached = min(tokens_in, cached)\n   253\t    return (tokens_in - cached) / 1e6 * price_in + cached / 1e6 * price_in * model.CACHED_INPUT_SHARE + tokens_out / 1e6 * price_out\n   254\t\n   255\t\n   256\tdef jev_estimate(request):\n   257\t    price_in, _ = model.PRICES[request['model']]\n   258\t    tokens_in = 2 * len(json.dumps(request, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False).encode('utf-8')) + 4096\n   259\t    return jev.ATTEMPTS * tokens_in * price_in / 1e6\n   260\t\n   261\t\n   262\tclass BudgetTransport:\n   263\t    \"\"\"Called as production calls a transport: (provider, request) for a language model, (request,) for Jev.\"\"\"\n   264\t\n   265\t    def __init__(self, ledger, sleep=time.sleep):\n   266\t        self.ledger, self.sleep = ledger, sleep\n   267\t\n   268\t    def __call__(self, *args):\n   269\t        if len(args) == 1:\n   270\t            return self._jev(args[0])\n   271\t        provider, request = args\n   272\t        for attempt in range(3):\n   273\t            estimate = llm_estimate(request)\n   274\t            if not self.ledger.reserve(estimate):\n   275\t                raise model.TransportError('the shared budget ceiling would be passed: not sent')\n   276\t            try:\n   277\t                response = model.openai_transport(provider, request, max_attempts=1)\n   278\t            except model.TransportError as error:\n   279\t                self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate)\n   280\t                status = getattr(error, 'http_status', None)\n   281\t                if status in CLIENT_ERRORS or attempt == 2 or (status is not None and status != 429 and status < 500):\n   282\t                    raise\n   283\t                self.sleep(5 * (attempt + 1))\n   284\t                continue\n   285\t            except Exception:\n   286\t                self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate)\n   287\t                raise\n   288\t            cost = llm_cost(response, request)\n   289\t            self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate if cost is None else cost)\n   290\t            return response\n   291\t        raise model.TransportError('no answer after three attempts')\n   292\t\n   293\t    def _jev(self, request):\n   294\t        estimate = jev_estimate(request)\n   295\t        if not self.ledger.reserve(estimate):\n   296\t            raise model.TransportError('the shared budget ceiling would be passed: not sent')\n   297\t        try:\n   298\t            response = jev.transport(request)\n   299\t        except Exception:\n   300\t            self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate, kind='jev')\n   301\t            raise\n   302\t        usage = response.get('usage') if isinstance(response, dict) else None\n   303\t        tokens = usage.get('input_tokens') if isinstance(usage, dict) else None\n   304\t        if isinstance(tokens, int) and not isinstance(tokens, bool) and tokens > 0:\n   305\t            # an unanswered attempt inside jev.transport was the same request, so each of the three is billed at most this input;\n   306\t            # the whole charge is settled, so a charge above the reservation sets the overrun flag\n   307\t            actual = jev.ATTEMPTS * tokens * model.PRICES[request['model']][0] / 1e6\n   308\t        else:\n   309\t            actual = estimate                       # usage missing, invalid, or zero for a nonempty request: the whole reservation\n   310\t        self.ledger.settle(estimate, actual, kind='jev', tokens=tokens if isinstance(tokens, int) else None)\n   311\t        return response\n   312\t\n   313\t\n   314\tdef main():\n   340\t    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(args.views), exist_ok=True)\n   341\t    log_path = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(args.views), 'replay.log')\n   342\t\n   343\t    def log(*parts):\n   344\t        line = ' '.join(str(p) for p in parts)\n   345\t        print(line, flush=True)\n   346\t        with open(log_path, 'a', encoding='utf-8') as handle:\n   347\t            handle.write(line + '\\n')\n   348\t\n   349\t    cfg = config.load(args.config)\n   350\t    if cfg.baseline is not None:\n   351\t        raise SystemExit(f'config {cfg.version} uses the retired seeded-question baseline: refused')\n   352\t    import importlib.util\n   353\t    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('scripts_replay', ROOT / 'scripts/replay.py')\n   354\t    scripts_replay = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n   355\t    spec.loader.exec_module(scripts_replay)\n   356\t    scripts_replay.refuse_seeded_ledger(args.views)          # the same refusal scripts/replay.py makes\n   357\t    uni = universe.load(args.universe)\n   358\t    archive = model.Archive(args.archive)\n   359\t    ledger = SharedLedger(args.ledger)\n   360\t    install_stop_gate(ledger)                              # Jev's internal retries read the run's stop too (council mo R1)\n   361\t    transport = BudgetTransport(ledger)\n   362\t    jev_workers = args.jev_workers if args.jev_workers is not None else (8 if cfg.matching.engine == 'jev' else 1)\n   363\t    day_runner = parallel_day.ParallelDay(os.path.abspath(args.testdb), os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(args.views)), 'manifests'),\n   364\t                                          extraction_workers=args.workers, jev_workers=jev_workers) if args.workers > 1 else None\n   365\t    log(f'--- budgeted replay {args.from_day}..{args.until_day} config {cfg.version}/{cfg.checksum} provider {cfg.provider} universe {uni.version} '\n   366\t        f'workers {args.workers}; ledger {args.ledger} {ledger.read()}')\n   367\t    totals = replay.run(testdb_path=args.testdb, views_path=args.views, archive=archive, cfg=cfg, universe=uni,\n   368\t                        from_day=args.from_day, until_day=args.until_day, spend_cap_usd=args.cap, log=log,\n   369\t                        only_objects=set(args.only.split(',')) if args.only else None, transport=transport, day_runner=day_runner)\n   370\t    log('totals:', totals)\n   371\t    log('ledger:', ledger.read())\n   372\t\n   373\t\n   374\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   375\t    main()\n6:`new` runs the clean pipeline (astra-frozen, the comparison limits, the judge to <until day>, three passes); `old` runs poc-v118. Both read\n22:BUDGET_REPLAY = ROOT / 'clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py'\n72:        argv += ['--limits', str(DATA / 'comparison-limits.json'), '--ladder-variant', 'astra-frozen', '--judge-end-day', until_day,\n    14\t \"state\": \"complete\",\n    15\t \"components\": {\n    16\t  \"prod\": {\n    17\t   \"attempts\": [\n    18\t    {\n    19\t     \"folder\": \"prod\",\n    20\t     \"state\": \"completed\",\n    21\t     \"started at\": \"2026-11-17T22:36:15-0800\",\n    22\t     \"pid\": 43600,\n    23\t     \"ended at\": \"2026-11-18T01:20:48-0800\"\n    24\t    }\n    25\t   ],\n    26\t   \"state\": \"completed\",\n    27\t   \"folder\": \"prod\"\n    28\t  }\n    29\t },\n    30\t \"prod totals\": {\n    31\t  \"items\": 2077,\n    32\t  \"extracted\": 1884,\n    33\t  \"skipped\": 0,\n    34\t  \"merged\": 193,\n    35\t  \"not_processed\": 0,\n    36\t  \"returned\": 0,\n    37\t  \"failed\": 0,\n    38\t  \"evidence\": 5406,\n    39\t  \"new_views\": 47,\n    40\t  \"judged\": 1609,\n    41\t  \"changed\": 832,\n    42\t  \"closed\": 2\n    80\t2026-09-17 | items  32 extracted  29 merged  3 skipped  0 failed  0 | evidence  43 new views  0 judged  40 changed  17 closed 0 | open views 46 | day $0.13 total $6.97 calls 8617\n    81\t2026-09-18 | items  43 extracted  39 merged  4 skipped  0 failed  0 | evidence 117 new views  0 judged  41