{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '3673,3720p;4787,4828p;4962,5006p'; rg -n '\"'^(#|.*must-open|.*judgement|.*gold)'\"' clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/{RESULT,SLICE-RESULT,DESIGN,MATCHING-v2}.md | cut -c1-270 | head -100; ls -la clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13 | head -80; rg -n 'old [0-9].*draw|p1.*p2.*p3|p1.*old|production.*gold' docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/comparison/COMPARISON-SIZING.md docs/DECISIONS-log.md | cut -c1-280 | tail -35\"","aggregated_output":"  3673\t  the commit. Nothing is lost from history.\n  3674\t- Carried from the `main` checkout's uncommitted work, where it has run since 2026-10-28 (not a new choice): the served data is the\n  3675\t  sealed three-month ledger `served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828` with the cleaned items database (README, \"Switching the\n  3676\t  served data\"), which also makes the two library-count tests pass that failed on `main`; a judgement's cites are read once each by\n  3677\t  the bundle and the service; the corpus scripts that built and cleaned the item database (`poc/corpus/`, D351); the three curated\n  3678\t  benchmark files its cleaning test reads (`poc/reports/2026-10-27-extraction-stability/inputs/*.clean.txt`); the 90-thesis review\n  3679\t  notes AGENTS §8 cites (`research_notes/对冲基金论点粒度与金标/`); the flow page `reports/2026-11-02-extraction-to-judgement.html`.\n  3680\t- Left out of Git and kept only in the backup `/Users/lchingen/hivemind-backups/local-main-2026-11-03/` (a tar of every uncommitted\n  3681\t  file of the `main` checkout with its file list and the tracked-file patch): the checkout's experiment outputs (about 2,600 files,\n  3682\t  1.6 GB, mostly run databases), the source-track runner code (`src/hivemind/source_reading.py` and its test, used only by those\n  3683\t  runners), the study scripts never committed, and the checkout's superseded copies of files the merge brought.\n  3684\t\n  3685\t## D354 · 2026-11-03 · Steps 3 and 4 (opening and matching questions, judging them) are frozen as `poc-v108` runs them, after three draws on the frozen extraction\n  3686\t\n  3687\t- Alex, after the extraction was frozen (D274): \"now that the extraction stage is done and frozen, we freeze that as well\"; on the plan to\n  3688\t  run the whole line on the frozen extraction and freeze steps 3 and 4 if their numbers did not get worse: \"好你跑\"; then \"那你跑了吧，我们赶紧确认step 3,4 可以freeze\".\n  3689\t- The run (`research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/log.md` row 29): `poc-v108` with the 22 frozen seeds over 2026-07-01..07-14, three draws at once\n  3690\t  from a pinned worktree, predictions and freeze conditions written before the send (`predictions-r9-frozen-v108.md`, sha256 beside it).\n  3691\t  All four conditions hold: every draw finished with no halted day; must-open questions 28/28 in every draw; the judgement agrees with the\n  3692\t  frozen gold on 15/17, 15/17 and 16/17 judged questions (control `poc-v94`: 16/18, 16/19, 16/18) and no question that agreed in all three\n  3693\t  control draws disagrees in all three new ones; core matters reaching judgement average 77.7 (control 74.3) and estimated noise reaching\n  3694\t  judgement 49.5 (bound 51).\n  3695\t- Frozen: the collision judge's prompt `collision-v2`, the judge's prompt `judging-v7`, the matching prompt the configuration names\n  3696\t  (`matching-v3`), the judge's answer schema and the three questions the Jev matcher is asked; `tests/test_frozen_questions_and_judgement.py`\n  3697\t  pins them (a one-character change to a prompt or to a matcher question fails it, both mutants checked). The configuration itself is\n  3698\t  pinned by `tests/test_frozen_extraction_prompt.py`. A change is a new version only Alex opens.\n  3699\t- Known defects, recorded and not fixed: (1) the collision judge splits one bet on a fine detail: the seed H200 question and an identical\n  3700\t  candidate were judged distinct (\"any\" against \"public\" authorization) in one draw; ten re-sends of the stored request gave the same\n  3701\t  question 8 times, so about one encounter in five opens a duplicate; (2) the frozen extraction proposed the lidar-legislation question the\n  3702\t  gold rules out in one draw of three; (3) the operating-margin question (gold q10) had one or two pieces in each control draw and none in\n  3703\t  any new draw, so it was never judged; (4) the root-revenue fallback of the frozen extraction raised the total-revenue question's share of\n  3704\t  all links from 9–12% to 23–24%, and the narrower questions lose the evidence that answers them: Broadcom's AI-chip revenue ($10.8bn in Q2,\n  3705\t  $16.0bn guided for Q3), the gold's basis for custom-chip spending (q16), was filed under that question in two of three control draws and in\n  3706\t  none of the frozen ones (it went to the total-revenue, data-center and accelerator-share questions), and the judge then chose below $40bn\n  3707\t  three times against the gold's $60–85bn; defect (3) is the same class. Over 14 days the judge requests stayed under 18,500 tokens, but a longer window is where evidence bloat\n  3708\t  appeared before (the three-month run stopped and sealed at 2026-08-28). (5) `scripts/preflight.py` cannot judge the one-decider\n  3709\t  architecture (D264): it does not rebuild the questions open at the time, so every stored link reads as \"links to nothing shown\".\n  3710\t\n  3711\t## D355 · 2026-11-04 · The filing topic closes without a change: filing is about 85% right; the remaining misses are recorded as known defects\n  3712\t\n  3713\t- Alex opened the topic on 2026-11-03 (\"你这个单独开一个专题出来解决 … 是promot，是系统结构设计还是到底哪里有问题挂错一堆东西，机制是不是有问题（一定要挂吗？有没有可能是杂音\"),\n  3714\t  set the method on 2026-11-04 (\"We need to validate the hypothesis in a very simple way and to make sure that it works on a high level before we\n  3715\t  dive into do the full analysis stability test\"; \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\"), and closed it: \"那就1吧\"\n  3716\t  (option 1: close the topic, record the pattern as a known defect, go to step 5).\n  3717\t- What was found (`research/2026-11-03-filing/report.html`, `log.md` rows 1–17): three rounds of Claude–Codex review converged on \"the question\n  3718\t  definition is too narrow\"; an independent challenge and the first stored-request test refuted it (the earlier version's definition was already\n  3719\t  broad; the same request gives different filings from send to send). Two cheap tests of fixes did not fit their hypotheses and stopped: removing the\n  3720\t  total-revenue fallback alone leaves good indirect evidence unlinked; teaching \"one fact, two uses\" made the model add a second company-revenue\n  4787\t  - Options: the same publication counts as the same day (recommended): \"数字题：只要两个到期日指的是同一时期数字的同一份公布，就算相同；事件题的截止日必须完全相同。最多 13 个合格。按字面的读法也会在旁边列出。\"; the literal reading (at most 8, likely too few, Stage B cannot pass whatever it judges); drop the control line.\n  4788\t  - Alex: \"指同一份年报就算相同 (Recommended)\".\n  4789\t- **Decided:** for Stage B's line 3 (design §8), a control thesis whose judged question is a figure is eligible on the due day\n  4790\t  when its due day and the ruler question's both mark the publication of the same period's figure (the ladder step's due day\n  4791\t  of a year's figure is set by code, D414); an event's deadline must equal the ruler's. The literal reading is counted beside.\n  4792\t  Fixed before the send and before any Stage B result exists.\n  4793\t- **Scope:** the clean path's Step 4, Stage B, line 3.\n  4794\t\n  4795\t## D431 · 2026-11-12 · The clean path is compared end to end with production as it now runs, with no preset questions on either side\n  4796\t\n  4797\t- **Asked:** \"整条新线路要和谁比，才算“比线上好”（你定的上线门槛 D427）？新系统不开公司财务指标题；线上版本自 11 月 5 日起也不再预设题目。\"\n  4798\t  - Options: current production (recommended): \"双方都不预设题目，条件相同；用冻结的标准、同一天、各跑三轮。“可评分的 7 道题”的结果单独列出。\"; the seeded version with 22 preset questions (\"新系统每轮天然少约 11 道公司财务指标题，几乎不可能赢\"); the seven graded questions only.\n  4799\t  - Alex: \"和现在的线上版本比 (Recommended)\".\n  4800\t- **Decided:** D427's end-to-end comparison is the clean path against production as it now runs (no preset questions, D370),\n  4801\t  on the frozen ruler, the same day, three draws each; the seven graded questions (D395) are reported beside. The seeded\n  4802\t  comparison (D392) remains a diagnostic, not the gate. Raised by the council's read of where the path stands\n  4803\t  (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/kr-consensus.md`).\n  4804\t- **Scope:** the clean path's end-to-end acceptance (D427).\n  4805\t\n  4806\t## D432 · 2026-11-12 · After Stage B, the next phase is how Step 1 cuts a matter into theses\n  4807\t\n  4808\t- **Asked:** \"第二段测完之后，先做哪件大事？两位评审都认为最大的差距在第 1 步“把一件事切成题”的方式。\"\n  4809\t  - Options: diagnose how Step 1 cuts theses first (recommended): \"逐篇对照自己开题时漏掉的 9 道标准题、8 个没出题的论点和第一段剩下的错，找出共同原因；再提一个改法，作为第 1 步的新版本，在没用过的新文章上测。开工前会把诊断结果和改法报给你。\"; mend the ladder step's remaining faults (would lift D426's freeze); capital spending (q12) first.\n  4810\t  - Alex: \"先查清第 1 步怎么切题 (Recommended)\".\n  4811\t- **Decided:** once Stage B is read, the next work is a source-by-source diagnosis of how Step 1 cuts a matter into theses (one\n  4812\t  quantity, one period, one question a year, D38): the nine graded questions the unseeded draws did not open, the eight theses\n  4813\t  with no ladder, and the remaining Stage A faults. The diagnosis and one proposed change, as a new Step 1 version to be\n  4814\t  measured on fresh articles, go to Alex before any build. c8 stays until then (D391).\n  4815\t- **Scope:** the clean path's Step 1 and its effect on Step 4.\n  4816\t\n  4817\t## D433 · 2026-11-12 · Open Step 1 version c14: D38's year boundary in the two merge sentences, tested small first\n  4818\t\n  4819\t- **Asked**, after the D432 diagnosis (`clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/DIAGNOSIS.md`, version 8; seven council rounds): \"第 1 步漏开题，最大的一类是：同一个数只开一年 … 我建议只改这两句，加约 150 个字元，不删任何东西。要不要开一个第 1 步的新版本（c14）来试？\"\n  4820\t  - Options: open c14 and test small first (recommended): \"先用存档里的几篇文章，让原版 c8 和新版各发 3 次，约 0.5 美元，每个对照案例都事先写好停止线；两年都开出来要达到 9 次里至少 8 次，原版最多 2 次，才在没用过的新文章上和 c8 正式比。不过关就停，报给你。\"; investigate the second-thing class first; keep c8 unchanged.\n  4821\t  - Alex: \"开 c14，先小测 (Recommended)\".\n  4822\t- **Decided:** a candidate Step 1 version c14 is opened: c8 with D38's year boundary carried into two sentences (shared_quantity: \"another year of it is not: this year's and next year's figure are two theses when an analyst would bet on each\"; the closing check: \"(for a yearly quantity, the same year)\"), +151 characters, nothing removed. Its first test is the small probe of the diagnosis (c8 and c14, three sends each from each draw's stored state, the pass line and stop lines fixed there, about $0.5). It goes to the prompt audit and a council read of the changed request before its first send. A failed probe stops the line and goes to Alex; a passed probe leads to the fresh-article comparison against c8 on his protocol (D386). c8 stays in force (D387, D391) until c14 is shown better on new, unused articles.\n  4823\t- **Scope:** clean Step 1. Ohio (D388–D391), the second-thing shapes and the other findings of the diagnosis stay recorded, not changed.\n  4824\t- **Wording settled before any send (2026-11-12, mine to settle, within D433's scope):** a blind second reader\n  4825\t  (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ll-codex.md`) found that \"another year of it is not\" reads as barring another\n  4826\t  year's figure as evidence, against c8's \"do not exclude evidence solely because it concerns a related period\". The sentences\n  4827\t  sent are: shared_quantity \"… evidence for it. Its figure for another year is a separate quantity, not another wording: this\n  4828\t  year's and next year's figure are two theses when an analyst would bet on each.\"; the closing check \"… about the same subject\n  4962\t  that began work other than a normal return, and any exit leaving an attempt `started` on disk, writes the shared stop first, then ends\n  4963\t  the child, then marks the draw; the registration is removed only after a normal end, a refusal before any work, or that stop, so a\n  4964\t  failed stop leaves it for the gate. `test_run_fresh.py` 30 tests, each new rule with its mutant; `proof_end_to_end.py` 3 of 3; full\n  4965\t  suite 287. **Consensus (round 7): \"Council position: ready for the slice.\"**\n  4966\t\n  4967\t## D450 · 2026-11-13 · Launch the slice: one fresh day through the wired path, live, on its own $1.50 ledger (council consensus under D439)\n  4968\t\n  4969\t- **Council** (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mo-slice-proposal.md`, `mo-codex-8.md` to `mo-codex-10.md`): the proposal was\n  4970\t  agreed after two changes: the $0 preflight before the paid run (`clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/preflight/PREFLIGHT-SLICE.md`,\n  4971\t  v118 q1–q3 through the current code) and measurement records that substantiate per-component spend and time without touching a frozen\n  4972\t  file (one ledger line per settled or refused attempt, written after the ledger's state and best-effort, with process id, call kind and\n  4973\t  reported tokens; each attempt's pid and start and end times in the draw record; `spend_by_component.py`). Consensus: \"Council\n  4974\t  position: launch the slice.\"\n  4975\t- **Decided:** `poc/data/clean-e2e-slice-2026-11-13/`, a new ledger with a $1.50 ceiling; at the same time, after a machine and network\n  4976\t  check, `run_fresh.py clean --label s1 --until-day 2026-07-01 --passes 1` and `run_fresh.py prod --label sp1 --until-day 2026-07-01`,\n  4977\t  each detached with a log and a pid file. A wiring check, not a draw and not evidence of quality. Any stop is read before anything else is\n  4978\t  sent; a redo only by a recorded council decision with `--redo-reason`. The component figures are ledger charges, not bills; a lost line\n  4979\t  makes the breakdown incomplete and the ledger's spent and reserved give the total. A day that opens no thesis reports the ladder and the\n  4980\t  judge unexercised. After it: every trace read by Claude (13 Step 1 answers beside their articles, Step 2's decisions, the cases, every\n  4981\t  ladder answer, every judgement with its evidence shown, production's day, the ledger against the archives' tokens, each log), then a\n  4982\t  separate council decision on the full run (ledger $15.00 minus the slice's spent and anything still reserved).\n  4983\t\n  4984\t## D451 · 2026-11-13 · Launch the full run: three clean draws and three production draws, same day, ledger $14.84 (council consensus under D439)\n  4985\t\n  4986\t- **Slice read** (`clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/SLICE-RESULT.md`): the wiring works live; $0.1593 of ledger, about $0.15 at the\n  4987\t  published rates; every answer read.\n  4988\t- **Council** (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mp-full-run-proposal.md`, `mp-codex.md`, `mp-codex-2.md`): one change before\n  4989\t  the send: a written reading commitment (`clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/READING-COMMITMENT.md`: the two families, the capacity\n  4990\t  already shown at this volume, the expected volume, briefs unchanged unless a council round changes them, an incomplete reading reported\n  4991\t  not measured). Consensus: \"Council position: launch the full run.\"\n  4992\t- **Decided:** `poc/data/clean-e2e-full-2026-11-13/`, a new ledger with ceiling $14.84 ($15.00 − the slice's $0.1593, nothing reserved);\n  4993\t  six launchers at once after a machine and network check: `run_fresh.py clean` c1, c2, c3 (2026-07-01..07-14, the ladder step's three\n  4994\t  passes) and `run_fresh.py prod` p1, p2, p3 (same window). Projection about $10.4 of ledger, about 2.5 h. D449's stop rules; no edit to\n  4995\t  code or prompt files while it runs. After it: spend and time by component, every trace read by Claude, then a reading plan for\n  4996\t  WIRING-DESIGN.md §E's lines reviewed by the council before any reader starts. What it can decide is §E's (a diagnostic census, Stage A's\n  4997\t  lines on fresh theses, Stage B's six conditions), never D427's acceptance.\n  4998\t\n  4999\t## D452 · 2026-11-13 · The reading plan for the full run (council consensus under D439)\n  5000\t\n  5001\t- **Council** (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mq-reading-plan.md`, `mq-codex.md` to `mq-codex-3.md`): reviewed against its\n  5002\t  sources in three rounds; the census's selection, eligibility, outcome and loss-trace rules, Stage B line 3's special rules and Stage A's\n  5003\t  NOT MEASURED rules carried as written; consensus: \"Council position: record and run the reading plan.\"\n  5004\t- **Decided** (`clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/READING-PLAN.md` version 3): (1) **Stage A line 5 on the fresh population is a\n  5005\t  council-set diagnostic line**: right ≥ ceil(35·N/44), right by a ladder ≥ ceil(28·N/44); D400's 44-theses wording printed beside with N and\n  5006\t  the result; never reported as Alex's line; N = 0 reads NOT MEASURED; a send refused twice counts as not right. (2) Stage B gets **two new\nrg: clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/MATCHING-v2.md: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/SLICE-RESULT.md:1:# The slice (D450): one fresh day through the wired path, live — reading (2026-11-13)\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/SLICE-RESULT.md:8:## Spend and time\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/SLICE-RESULT.md:27:## What each component produced (read by Claude, every answer)\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/SLICE-RESULT.md:50:## What the slice does not show\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/RESULT.md:1:# The end-to-end census (D442–D444): result, 2026-11-13\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/RESULT.md:3:**Answer.** On the seven graded questions, under the frozen judgement ruler and D430's eligibility, both systems agree with reader B on\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/RESULT.md:4:one or two questions a draw, and **every eligible judgement in either system agrees with reader B**: no graded answer is lost at\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/RESULT.md:5:judgement. Every loss is at opening: the question was not opened in the ruler's shape, or was opened for another deadline, period or\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/RESULT.md:10:## Graded questions, per draw (outcome by DESIGN.md v4, procedure 6)\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/DESIGN.md:1:# The end-to-end comparison as an exploratory census (shape B'), design version 4, 2026-11-13\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/DESIGN.md:9:**What it is for.** An exploratory census of observed final-answer losses on the frozen judgement ruler: the clean path's stored chain\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/DESIGN.md:16:2026-11-10/`); ladders, Stage A run 4 send 1, 2026-11-10/11 (`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_a/`); judgements, Stage B, 2026-11-11\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/DESIGN.md:17:(`poc/data/clean-stage-b-2026-11-11/`). Production arm: each draw's launch and finish times from its manifest. A judgement selected\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/DESIGN.md:20:## $0 verification, done before any send\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/DESIGN.md:24:| frozen-prompt, frozen-judgement and frozen-ruler tests | 8 passed |\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/DESIGN.md:27:| the production record reader (`prod_records.py validate`) on the seed views of the same runs | 69 question outcomes compared with the frozen scorer's printed outcome: 0 mismatches; outcomes include \"no judgement\" (d2),\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/DESIGN.md:28:| the evidence-visibility reader (`prod_records.py validate-shown`) | the pattern: in 711 judgements every cited id is listed in that judgement's own request; 11,134 (judgement, evidence created after its request) pairs \nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/DESIGN.md:35:## Procedure\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/DESIGN.md:40:   judges them, and the readers above read its views, rungs, judgements and requests. A failure stops and goes to the council.\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/DESIGN.md:51:6. **Outcomes, per ruler question, per draw, per arm, the first that applies:** (i) reader B's gold open or no gold view: \"not\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/DESIGN.md:56:   \"unresolved\"; (vi) not eligible: \"opened, not eligible\", with the reason; (vii) no judgement on or before 2026-07-14: \"no judgement\";\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/DESIGN.md:61:   judgement on or before the window end), *shown* (listed in a judge request for that view on or before that day:\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/DESIGN.md:64:   facts' marks are listed as observations, never as the cause of a judgement that does not exist, and never as a judgement error;\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/DESIGN.md:67:   (g) every item shown and the rungs could express it: judgement; (h) the readers cannot settle a fact: \"ambiguous\". A loss with\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/DESIGN.md:72:## Spending: an enforced shared ceiling\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/DESIGN.md:82:all later attempts. An attempt that would pass the ceiling is not sent: production records that item or judgement as failed, and the\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/DESIGN.md:103:path of a judgement.\ntotal 616\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 58 lchingen  staff   1856 Nov 14 11:12 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 67 lchingen  staff   2144 Nov 16 12:20 ..\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff   2503 Nov 13 01:07 AUDIT-CONTRACT.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff   3565 Nov 13 01:08 AUDIT-RESULT.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff   4697 Nov 13 06:09 CENSUS-FULL-RESULT.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff   3649 Nov 13 10:13 CHOICES-FOR-ALEX-2026-11-13.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff  11930 Nov 13 00:06 DESIGN.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff   1970 Nov 13 02:43 READING-COMMITMENT.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff   7800 Nov 13 03:05 READING-PLAN.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff   4535 Nov 13 01:06 RESULT.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff   4700 Nov 13 02:41 SLICE-RESULT.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff   1398 Nov 13 00:08 SLICE.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff   2938 Nov 13 06:04 STAGE-A-FULL-RESULT.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff   7149 Nov 13 07:04 STATUS-FOR-ALEX-2026-11-13.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff   5793 Nov 13 01:07 TRACE.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff  14975 Nov 13 02:12 WIRING-DESIGN.md\ndrwxr-xr-x@  7 lchingen  staff    224 Nov 18 00:37 __pycache__\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff  20109 Nov 13 02:29 budget_replay.py\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff   4821 Nov 13 02:29 budget_step2.py\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff  11768 Nov 13 02:29 check_budget.py\ndrwxr-xr-x@  7 lchingen  staff    224 Nov 13 00:54 eligibility\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff   1348 Nov 13 00:08 extract_opened_prod.py\ndrwxr-xr-x@  5 lchingen  staff    160 Nov 13 05:54 full-eligibility\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 52 lchingen  staff   1664 Nov 13 06:01 full-eligibility-answers\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 14 lchingen  staff    448 Nov 13 05:42 full-matching\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 40 lchingen  staff   1280 Nov 13 05:48 full-matching-answers\ndrwxr-xr-x@  9 lchingen  staff    288 Nov 13 05:36 full-matching-sources\ndrwxr-xr-x@  9 lchingen  staff    288 Nov 13 06:06 full-trace\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 40 lchingen  staff   1280 Nov 13 06:08 full-trace-answers\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 lchingen  staff     96 Nov 13 06:05 full-trace-sources\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 25 lchingen  staff    800 Nov 14 18:06 identity-probe\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 20 lchingen  staff    640 Nov 13 08:28 ladder-cost\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 13 lchingen  staff    416 Nov 13 08:36 ladder-refusal\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 24 lchingen  staff    768 Nov 13 00:51 matching\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 10 lchingen  staff    320 Nov 13 06:37 opening-review\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 26 lchingen  staff    832 Nov 13 10:36 outcomes-at-opening\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 14 lchingen  staff    448 Nov 13 09:16 period-probe\ndrwxr-xr-x@  9 lchingen  staff    288 Nov 13 02:27 preflight\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff   5427 Nov 13 00:10 prod_controls.py\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff  14714 Nov 13 00:00 prod_records.py\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff   1404 Nov 13 02:29 proof_end_to_end.output.txt\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff  17063 Nov 13 02:29 proof_end_to_end.py\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff   3313 Nov 13 02:11 proof_interception.output.txt\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff  24115 Nov 13 02:07 proof_interception.py\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff   1214 Nov 13 02:08 proof_wiring.output.txt\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff   7906 Nov 13 02:08 proof_wiring.py\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 20 lchingen  staff    640 Nov 13 10:07 reachability\ndrwxr-xr-x@  9 lchingen  staff    288 Nov 13 08:44 refused-shapes\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff   7102 Nov 13 00:27 resume_check.py\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff   2257 Nov 13 00:04 run_budgeted_draw.sh\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff  29210 Nov 17 20:49 run_fresh.py\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff   3181 Nov 13 02:29 spend_by_component.py\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 lchingen  staff     96 Nov 13 08:38 stage-a-splits\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 lchingen  staff     96 Nov 13 06:33 stage-a-trace\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 14 lchingen  staff    448 Nov 13 07:06 step1-audit\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff  25395 Nov 17 20:49 test_run_fresh.py\ndrwxr-xr-x@  6 lchingen  staff    192 Nov 13 06:20 unlinked-trace\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 27 lchingen  staff    864 Nov 13 09:49 unsigned-deals\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/comparison/COMPARISON-SIZING.md:18:| Big matters covered, both teams (outside the company's own financial level) | trial, one draw each: new 6 of 7 (one team: the seventh missed; the other: folded into another question), old 7 of 7 | one dr\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/comparison/COMPARISON-SIZING.md:20:| Answers supported by what the judge was shown, both teams | trial, one draw each: new 7 of 9, old 10 of 12 | one draw each: new 6 of 7, old 10 of 15 | **none** |\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/comparison/COMPARISON-SIZING.md:24:| By code: questions opened | new 9, 8, 12; old 12, 13, 14 | new 7; old 15 | three draws each in July |\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2386:- The study shares at most two provider requests across all stages. It keeps the $1.50 total conservative ceiling and a 144-call ceiling, stops on failure, and does not alter production prompts, grouping rules, default transports or source/gold database\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2783:- D222 result: 19 of 48 planned comparison calls returned complete responses (10 control, 9 treatment); one treatment fabricated a question ID and was refused, so the remaining 29 were not sent. Target facts stayed present (7/7 control, 6/6 treatment ob\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2787:Alex explicitly rejected stopping at D222's failed result and asked to trace causes and improve. The [single-note experiment](research/2026-10-29-single-note/design.md) tests a bounded contract change in the fourth-step research harness: write the inves\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2831:- Measurement, in this order: the per-article reference for the v38 week's 98 items and the 20-article holdout of 2026-07-08..14 (`holdout-pick.json`) written from the texts and frozen before any send; three gpt-6-luna draws of the production bytes and \ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2940:- Decided: role-v42 replaces role-v29 as the extraction request; `scripts/replay.py` defaults to `poc/config/poc-v58.json`, which differs from `poc-v45` only in the ten extraction prompt versions (T*-v42). What it buys, pooled over the five runs on the \ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3561:- No new model calls, production changes, old-label edits or long-run restart. The worked examples are proposed semantic criteria, not accepted gold or measured model improvement.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3606:- Alex, after the concrete D346 standard and prompt were presented, instructs: “你开始你的尝试/研究”. Proceed with the [fixed development trial](research/2026-10-27-analyst-extraction-eval/trial-plan.md), freezing the assistant-authored 14-argument/37-requiremen\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3629:- This is a research comparison using the D347 assistant-authored development standard, not production adoption, independent human gold, held-out evaluation or downstream routing/Jev acceptance.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3641:- Review explicit evaluation units and ambiguous gold before another comparison. Use an unexposed full article with a reference prepared before its model output, then exercise the actual downstream reader. No production contract, default, gold replaceme\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4039:The previous implementation and the stopped seven-day run used day-start snapshots. This record is a design decision, not a claim that the production default has changed or that a new experiment has passed. Historical requests, results, frozen gold and \ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4883:- **Amended 2026-11-13 (council round mj-5, `council/mj-codex-5.md`: \"Council position: consensus on (a)\"):** the 11 jobs the $2.0 ceiling never sent are sent alone, same requests, under a $1.2 completion ceiling (a recorded departure from D440's step c\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4893:- **Council** (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mk-*`): Claude's reflection written first (`mk-my-reflection.md`); an independent Codex member investigated cold and reached the same recommendation (`mk-codex.md`: \"Run the bounded D431 compar\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4994:  passes) and `run_fresh.py prod` p1, p2, p3 (same window). Projection about $10.4 of ledger, about 2.5 h. D449's stop rules; no edit to\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5056:- **Reflection council** (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mt-claude.md`, a fresh cold read `mt-codex.md`, `mt-codex-2.md`): Claude\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5237:- **Council** (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mu-claude.md` written first; a fresh cold read `mu-codex.md`; `mu-codex-2.md`): \"同意停止当前\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5617:- **Read** (Claude's own trace reading, `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mx-claude-reflection.md`; a fresh Codex session's cold read,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/CENSUS-FULL-RESULT.md | sed -n '1,92p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v12.md | sed -n '20,37p;106,145p;218,244p;255,273p;292,335p'; rg -n '## D274|## D370' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; rg -n 'v74i' docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/log.md | tail -6 | cut -c1-460; rg -n 'v74i|test.*gold' docs/research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard -g '*.md' | rg 'D274|v74i' | cut -c1-420 | tail -18\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/CENSUS-FULL-RESULT.md | sed -n '1,92p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v12.md | sed -n '20,37p;106,145p;218,244p;255,273p;292,335p'; rg -n '## D274|## D370' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; rg -n 'v74i' docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/log.md | tail -6 | cut -c1-460; rg -n 'v74i|test.*gold' docs/research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard -g '*.md' | rg 'D274|v74i' | cut -c1-420 | tail -18\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# The census of the full run (D451, D452) — same day, both systems, 2026-11-13\n     2\t\n     3\t**Answer: on the seven graded ruler questions the clean path and production agree with reader B about equally often, and no eligible\n     4\tjudgement disagrees in either; every loss happens before judging.** Settled agreements per draw: **clean 2 / 1 / 0, production 1 / 1 / 1**\n     5\t(points the two third readers split on left out); **clean 2 / 2 / 1, production 2 / 2 / 2** with those points counted eligible. The earlier\n     6\tcensus (q1–q3 against u1–u3, different days) read production 1/1/1 and clean 1/2/1. A description, not an acceptance (D442): it cannot show\n     7\teither system is better.\n     8\t\n     9\t## How it was read (READING-PLAN.md v3, D452)\n    10\t\n    11\t- **Matching** (MATCHING-v2; `full-matching-answers/`): 79 opened questions under neutral names; two families; 73 agree; 6 disputes to a\n    12\t  third reader of each family: 1 resolved SAME, 5 unresolved (the Codex third reader NOT SAME, the Claude one SAME). A reader's answer counts\n    13\t  SAME when its relation is \"same\" (last time's derivation); so the credit-support questions, which both readers called \"narrower\" than\n    14\t  q09's total, count as not opened in q09's shape (last time's recorded limit, carried).\n    15\t- **Eligibility** (Stage B's control-reader brief; `full-eligibility-answers/`): 28 matched views, both families, 17 differing points (9 on\n    16\t  same_question, 8 on an item shown), every one ruled the Codex way by the Codex third reader and the Claude way by the Claude third reader:\n    17\t  all 17 unresolved. Eligible means same question and same due day (D430's reading); the literal reading (the same due day) is printed\n    18\t  beside each.\n    19\t- **Outcome**: the design's order (i)–(ix); agreement by the frozen scorer's rule (`control_theses.agrees`).\n    20\t\n    21\t## Per draw (graded subset q04, q05, q08, q09, q13, q18, q23)\n    22\t\n    23\t| draw | agrees | not opened in the ruler's shape | opened, not eligible | unresolved |\n    24\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n    25\t| c1 | q04, q13 | q05, q09, q23 | q08 (question), q18 (question, due) | — |\n    26\t| c2 | q04 | q05, q08, q09, q13, q23 | — | q18 (eligibility) |\n    27\t| c3 | — | q09, q13, q23 | q18 (question, due) | q04 (eligibility), q05, q08 (matching) |\n    28\t| p1 | q04 | q05, q08, q09 | q18 (question), q23 (due) | q13 (eligibility) |\n    29\t| p2 | q04 | q05, q08, q09, q23 | — | q13 (eligibility), q18 (matching) |\n    30\t| p3 | q04 | q05, q08, q09, q23 | q18 (question, due) | q13 (eligibility) |\n    31\t\n    32\tEach unresolved-eligibility view would agree if counted eligible (c2 q18, c3 q04, p1–p3 q13). The not-eligible Kyber views of c1, c3 and\n    33\tp3 ask about a 2028 deadline and answer Yes where reader B answers No for 2027; p1's Ohio view is due 2027-07-01 against the ruler's\n    34\t2027-06-30 (its last judgement, Yes, would agree). Outside the graded subset: production's q07, q01, q22 and q02 agree wherever eligible;\n    35\tthe clean draws' q07 is eligibility-unresolved in all three.\n    36\t\n    37\t## The loss trace (point 7; D454)\n    38\t\n    39\tEvery lost graded answer is outcome (iii) or (vi), so its cause is (a), opening, by the design's first-applies order; no loss is a\n    40\tjudgement. The marks behind it (`full-trace/`, `full-trace-answers/`; both families agree on all 110 extracted marks):\n    41\t\n    42\t| draw | reader B's decisive items of its lost questions extracted by the run | not extracted |\n    43\t|---|---|---|\n    44\t| c1 / c2 / c3 | 19 / 17 / 15 | 1 / 2 / 1 |\n    45\t| p1 / p2 / p3 | 14 / 8 / 17 | 6 / 7 / 3 |\n    46\t\n    47\t**The clean path loses only at opening:** it had kept 51 of the 55 facts reader B relied on for the questions it lost, and in its opened\n    48\tbut not-eligible views (c1 and c3 Kyber, c1 China H200) every decisive item but one (c1's i305, \"domestic suppliers sold out\") was linked\n    49\tand shown to the judge. **Production has a second loss behind the opening:** besides 16 facts never kept, its Kyber views (p1 v9, p3 v8)\n    50\twere never linked to the extracted cancellation of the four-die Rubin Ultra (i179) and the Oberon-rack cover (i181), and its Ohio view\n    51\t(p1 v2) to the extracted $3.5bn lease guarantees (i006) and \"has started backstopping leases\" (i116): cause (d), never linked in time,\n    52\tlisted after (a).\n    53\t\n    54\t**Literal due-day reading** (the same due day, printed beside D430's reading), of the 28 matched views: clean: events 5 equal, 2 differ; figures 0 equal, 4 differ; production: events 4 equal, 2 differ; figures 3 equal, 8 differ. A figure view whose due day differs literally counts as the ruler's only under D430's same-annual-report reading; an event must match literally under both readings.\n    55\t\n    56\t## Limits\n    57\t\n    58\tOne draw of each system a day; the readers' family thresholds decide many points (both counts are given); the period field of the\n    59\tmatching packets still shows which system wrote a question; the gold is the frozen ruler (D261), unchanged.\n    20\t## 0. Scope\n    21\t\n    22\t**In:**\n    23\t- poc-v118 against the new system (astra-frozen), from empty at 2026-07-01, three draws each;\n    24\t- the blind matter census;\n    25\t- the council's reading;\n    26\t- D665's verdict and everything D665 prints beside it;\n    27\t- the report to Alex.\n    28\t\n    29\t**Out** (written to `FINDINGS.md`, not acted on):\n    30\t- any prompt or answer-choice change (D662);\n    31\t- model trials;\n    32\t- live-store, planner or integration work;\n    33\t- D658;\n    34\t- other weeks or companies;\n    35\t- any \"while we are here\" fix.\n    36\t\n    37\t## 1. Stage 0 ($0): built, proved, frozen, then reviewed\n   106\t2. **Readers.** Codex (memories off, closed, D661) and Claude (closed command line), apart. Nine weeks × 2 families, in fresh sessions.\n   107\t3. **Merge.** One matter is one bet. Two entries are one matter only when the same outcome settles both and their answers cannot move apart.\n   108\t   Another year of a figure is another matter.\n   109\t   - Each family merges its own nine lists in one session.\n   110\t   - Two reconcilers, one per family, map every matter across the two families' lists (`same` or `none`). A matter is listed by both when\n   111\t     both reconcilers say `same`.\n   112\t   - A one-family matter goes to two third readers (one per family) with its articles. It joins the list when both say it is worth a question.\n   113\t4. **The company-figure flag.** Each family marks every listed matter `company figure` or not, using D505's own list: 营收、毛利率的指引、市场预期、实际业绩.\n   114\t   The flag is set when both say yes; a split is listed.\n   115\t5. **N** is every listed matter (D665). The flagged subgroup is printed beside the verdict with its own a, b and N, because by D505 the new\n   116\t   system does not open such questions. Alex sees how much of any gap that rule makes. (D431: the comparison is of the products as\n   117\t   configured.)\n   118\t6. **De-duplication and freeze (D671).** Both families group the entries that are one bet (D248); a pair only one family grouped, or one a reviewer names, goes to one blind adjudicator of each family with its articles; a merge needs both families or both adjudicators. **Frozen:** `stage0/census/matters.json`, the only scoring list: each matter with one canonical question, its source articles, its first source day and its flag; its hash is in the versions manifest.\n   119\t7. **Too small at once:** if N < 20, the verdict is \"too small\" and goes to Alex before any paid send.\n   120\t\n   121\t### 1.4 The verdict rule (`verdict-rule.json`, hashed; `score_comparison.py` with a test and a mutant per rule)\n   122\t\n   123\t1. **The cutoff:** one for every matter, the end of the invocation's last day (09-20 in the full run). Libraries are read as they stand then.\n   124\t   - Closed questions still count.\n   125\t   - Timeliness is not scored. The days from first source to opening are printed beside.\n   126\t2. **Covers (mapping, A2's form, blind):**\n   127\t   - **The rule:** both families mark the question `opened`, or `narrower` with both saying it carries the matter's main outcome\n   128\t     (ACCEPTANCE-DESIGN A; `tally_week.covered`). `broader` and `missed` do not cover.\n   129\t   - **Blinding:** the readers see each draw's library under a random X/Y label, the key outside the repository, and are told to ignore\n   130\t     style.\n   131\t   - **Disagreements:** two third readers, one per family. A remaining split is resolved per counting (item 7, order: covers > does not\n   132\t     cover).\n   133\t3. **Same question:**\n   134\t   - **A question** is an id in a system-draw's library at the cutoff, the system's own identity. Distinct questions are distinct ids.\n   135\t   - **Matter to question:** the mapping rule above.\n   136\t   - **Question to question:** two questions of one library are the same bet when the same outcome settles both and their answers cannot move\n   137\t     apart (A1's rule; D248). Of such a pair, **the earlier-opened question is the original and the later one the duplicate** (as\n   138\t     `week/brief-A2.md` named the order).\n   139\t   - **During mapping:** the readers, who read each whole library, also mark its duplicates.\n   140\t   - **Distinct bets** are the ids less the duplicates both families mark. The 30-question minimum counts distinct bets. A split duplicate is\n   141\t     counted both ways, and the minimum must hold both ways.\n   142\t   - **On cards:** a duplicate stays a question in the worth guardrail.\n   143\t4. **The cards and their marks:**\n   144\t   - **Worth tracking:** worth, trivia or duplicate. Each card lists its library's other questions in opening order, with their opening days.\n   145\t     `duplicate` is marked only on the later question of a same-bet pair.\n   218\t\n   219\t### 1.6 What D665 prints beside, with its tool and input\n   220\t\n   221\t| What | Status | Tool and input |\n   222\t|---|---|---|\n   223\t| D400 accounting, all three passes (`stage_a/accounting.py`) | **Hard:** figure ranges meet end to end; the favourable end is stable; the due day agrees across all three sends for ≥ 90% of eligible questions. A failure is a release blocker reported with the verdict. Lines 1–5: reported | The new system's three draws. The reader lines use Stage A's two-family reading (`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_a/build_reader_packets.py` and its tally, D400) on every draw |\n   224\t| Step 2's three lines (D427; PRD §5) | **Hard**, like D400's code-decided parts: a failed line is a release blocker reported with the verdict. Pass: earlier version found ≥ 90%; clearly wrong merges ≤ 2%; no fewer later details than no merging. Each decided on its point estimate, intervals printed. A line with fewer eligible cases than its frozen sample is **not measured** and cannot clear release | The Step 2 log §12 method on draw 1 of the new system: recall over 100 records with a labelled earlier version (stratified random); blind review of 200 random merges; the no-merge dossier comparison on 30 groups. The sample sizes are a recorded design choice |\n   225\t| D431's frozen-reference reading, 07-01 to 07-14 | Printed beside | The D395 method (`clean-arch/unseeded-2026-11-10/MATCHING-v2.md`: the seven graded questions against the frozen judgement gold) on **both** systems' draws as they stood at 07-14 |\n   226\t| Proposed absolute floors | Printed beside | Coverage ≥ 80%, trivia ≤ 20% and supported ≥ 90% come from this comparison's cards. Wrong citations ≤ 5% and zero answer-changing omissions need source-first readings this plan does not run: printed as **not measured** (agreed in the council before the send) |\n   227\t\n   228\t### 1.7 Long-run risk, checked at $0\n   229\t\n   230\t- **The old judge's request size.** poc-v118's `evidence_in_view` (`views/judging.py:41`) shows every arrival since the fifth most recent\n   231\t  judgement, which is unbounded.\n   232\t  - Proxy: the sealed v34 ledger (07-01 to 08-28, 8 halt files).\n   233\t  - Code computes the size of every request v118's rule would build on it.\n   234\t  - If any exceeds the model's input limit or v34's halting size (292 KB), the risk is reported before the send.\n   235\t- **The same for the new judge,** on the carried fortnight, scaled.\n   236\t\n   237\t### 1.8 Preflight\n   238\t\n   239\t- Every stored answer of the latest runs of both systems goes through the current checks (AGENTS §5).\n   240\t- Both launchers run dry over two days with every code change in place.\n   241\t\n   242\t**Freeze review:** the council reads §1's artifacts, proofs and outputs. A finding is fixed and the review repeated. The paid stages start\n   243\twhen it finds nothing serious.\n   244\t\n   255\t## 3. Stage 2: the full run\n   256\t\n   257\t- **What runs:** three draws of each system, 07-01 to 09-20, detached, each with a log and a pid.\n   258\t- **One ledger per draw** (six), so a stop ends only that draw.\n   259\t  - **Absolute guards** (stops, not a budget): $65 per new-system draw, about 1.6 × the upper estimate; $25 per old-system draw, about\n   260\t    1.7 ×. That is $270 in all.\n   261\t  - This replaces, for this run only, D449's whole-run stop across draws and D666's single $250 ledger. It is recorded as a council decision\n   262\t    before the send.\n   263\t- **D449 within each draw, unchanged:**\n   264\t  - a redo is launched only on an eligible failure shown in the component's output, with its reason written;\n   265\t  - once per component;\n   266\t  - a second stop ends that draw (§1.4 item 10).\n   267\t- **The measured risk:**\n   268\t  - the 4 stored Step 1 failures (of 2,549 articles) were dropped connections from before the network retry;\n   269\t  - 0 failures in 624 articles since;\n   270\t  - 9 of 9 format retries recovered.\n   271\t- **A stopped ledger** refuses later launches. A relaunch would be a diagnostic only (§1.4 item 10).\n   272\t\n   273\t## 4. Stage 3: reading and verdict\n   292\t## 5. Estimates (measured rates; checked at the slice)\n   293\t\n   294\t**New system, per draw:**\n   295\t- Step 1: 1,976 articles at 26 to 34 s (measured) is 14 to 19 h, at $0.0089 to $0.0102 an article: $18 to $20.\n   296\t- Step 2: about $3.\n   297\t- The answer-choice step: about 55 theses × 3 passes × $0.037 to $0.050, about $6 to $8.\n   298\t- The judge: about $5 to $10 (the least certain).\n   299\t- **About $32 to $41 and about 20 h a draw.**\n   300\t\n   301\t**Old system, per draw:** poc-v118's own $0.53 to $0.66 for 243 articles, scaled up, is about $5. But cost per article rises as the library\n   302\tgrows: the sealed v34 run went from $0.0026 to $0.0077. So about $5 to $15, over 2 to 4 h.\n   303\t\n   304\t**In all:** about $110 to $170 and about 20 h of wall clock.\n   305\t\n   306\t**The reading:** the census takes a few hours. About 330 to 450 cards, marked by the council in about 6 to 10 h. The §1.6 readings come after\n   307\tthe verdict reading.\n   308\t\n   309\t## 6. Monitoring\n   310\t\n   311\t- **Sources** (never a live database):\n   312\t  - each ledger's `ledger.json` and attempt log;\n   313\t  - each draw's `run.json`;\n   314\t  - production's `replay.log` day and cost lines;\n   315\t  - **a snapshot of each live trace and archive** every heartbeat (SQLite online backup, as `snapshot.sh` does), counting completed articles,\n   316\t    completed judge days, the largest judge request and refused judge answers.\n   317\t- **Monitor:** one `Monitor` raises an event on:\n   318\t  - every component state change, stop, crash, refusal or redo;\n   319\t  - every 100 completed articles per new-system draw;\n   320\t  - every 7 replay days per old-system draw.\n   321\t- **Heartbeat:** every 20 minutes, spend per completed article (Step 1) and per completed day (judges and production), compared like with\n   322\t  like:\n   323\t  - each draw against its two sibling draws at the same progress;\n   324\t  - the old system against the sealed v34 curve scaled by the slice.\n   325\t- **Stalls:**\n   326\t  - a new-system draw with no ledger attempt for 35 minutes (one call can wait 3 × 600 s plus 90 s);\n   327\t  - an old-system draw with no new day line for 45 minutes.\n   328\t\n   329\t  I read the logs and the process state within one heartbeat.\n   330\t- **The stops,** each through that draw's own ledger, with the reason recorded:\n   331\t  - **automatic:** its absolute guard ($65 or $25);\n   332\t  - **mine:**\n   333\t    - a runaway: a draw spending over 2 times the median of its running siblings at the same progress, over at least 50 articles or 5 days;\n   334\t    - a hang: 0% CPU beyond the stall limit.\n   335\t- **Watched and reported, never a stop:** the largest judge request and refused judge answers. A day the judge halts on is D449's to handle.\n3151:## D274 · 2026-11-03 · The extraction production prompt is frozen at v74i (`poc-v108`); the unadopted variants are retired\n3998:## D370 · 2026-11-05 UTC · Remove the separate earnings-report import\n53:| 26 | 2026-11-02 22:10 | v74i / poc-v108：v74h 的复核三句例外收窄回标准原话（Alex：\"收窄那三句，直接测\"） | 核心 v74d 59 → 70、辅助 87 → 117、杂音 89 → 81（扣长引文 56 → 54），核心三次全没到 3 → 0 | `proof-v108-*` | 候选；设不设默认 Alex 定 |\n55:| 28 | 2026-11-02 23:10 | 冻结 + 清理（D274；Alex：\"上一个版本是不是freeze作为我们的抽取生产提示词吧 … clean up sanitize\"） | v74i / poc-v108 为生产默认并由测试钉住；54 个没采用的变体文件备份后删除，相关代码路径一并移除；保留配置的请求字节前后一致 | `retired-2026-11-03/`、`tests/test_frozen_extraction_prompt.py` | 冻结 |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/views/round.py | sed -n '62,162p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/replay.py | sed -n '51,143p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/jev.py | sed -n '15,78p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/model.py | sed -n '26,41p'; rg -n '\"'^def default_as_of|''^def resolve_bound|def open_pinned'\"' src/hivemind/service.py; nl -ba docs/prd/00-system.md | sed -n '16,34p;131,154p'; rg -n '\"'^##|model|seconds|cost|stable|repl'\"' docs/poc/idea-card.md | tail -33\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/views/round.py | sed -n '62,162p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/replay.py | sed -n '51,143p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/jev.py | sed -n '15,78p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/model.py | sed -n '26,41p'; rg -n '\"'^def default_as_of|''^def resolve_bound|def open_pinned'\"' src/hivemind/service.py; nl -ba docs/prd/00-system.md | sed -n '16,34p;131,154p'; rg -n '\"'^##|model|seconds|cost|stable|repl'\"' docs/poc/idea-card.md | tail -33\"","aggregated_output":"    62\t\n    63\t\n    64\tdef changed_views_of_day(conn, day):\n    65\t    \"\"\"The views whose reading changed on a replay day: the union of the 'written' records of that day's items and of the coverage-start reading's\n    66\t    record dated that day (D364: the questions it linked starting figures to are judged in the first day's round).\"\"\"\n    67\t    changed = set()\n    68\t    for row in conn.execute(\"select reason from processing_steps where step in ('written', 'baseline') and result='ok' and publication_day=?\", (day,)):\n    69\t        changed.update(json.loads(row['reason']).get('changed', []))\n    70\t    return changed\n    71\t\n    72\t\n    73\tdef judge_day(conn, archive, cfg, day, seq, *, transport=None, log=print):\n    74\t    \"\"\"D63: one re-judging round per day over every open view whose reading changed that day, dependencies first,\n    75\t    recorded under the day's own processing record (input 'day:<date>'); a view already judged at this sequence\n    76\t    number (a resumed day) is not judged twice.\"\"\"\n    77\t    marker = {'input_id': f'day:{day}', 'publication_day': day}\n    78\t    changed = changed_views_of_day(conn, day)\n    79\t    result = RoundResult(marker['input_id'])\n    80\t    if not changed:\n    81\t        return result\n    82\t    try:\n    83\t        judged = judging.round_of_judgements(archive, cfg, conn, sorted(changed), seq, marker, transport=transport)\n    84\t        result.judged = len(judged)\n    85\t        result.changed = sum(1 for j in judged if j['changed'])\n    86\t        result.cost += sum(j['cost'] for j in judged)\n    87\t        result.cached_calls += sum(1 for j in judged if j['cached'])\n    88\t        dispatch.mark(conn, marker, seq, 'judged', 'ok', f'{len(changed)} views changed, {len(judged)} judged, {result.changed} changed conclusions')\n    89\t        conn.commit()\n    90\t    except judging.JudgementRefused as error:\n    91\t        return _fail(conn, marker, seq, result, 'judged', 'judgement_refused_twice', 'judgement refused twice: ' + str(error), 'day')\n    92\t    except Exception as error:\n    93\t        return _fail(conn, marker, seq, result, 'judged', 'judging_failed', 'judging: ' + repr(error), type(error).__name__)\n    94\t    return result\n    95\t\n    96\t\n    97\tdef run(conn, archive, cfg, universe, item, seq, *, resume_from=None, transport=None, log=print, extractor=None, matching_workers=1):\n    98\t    result = RoundResult(item['input_id'])\n    99\t    if resume_from in ('judged', 'handed_over'):       # written already; judging is the day's step\n   100\t        dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'handed_over', 'ok', 'resumed')\n   101\t        conn.commit()\n   102\t        return result\n   103\t    objects = [o['value'] for o in item.get('object_identifiers') or [] if universe.has(o['value'])]\n   104\t    shown = extraction.shown_views(conn, cfg, item, objects)\n   105\t    # extraction (or its stored handover on resume)\n   106\t    handover = None\n   107\t    if resume_from and resume_from != 'extracted':\n   108\t        row = conn.execute('select handover_json from handovers where input_id=? order by id desc limit 1', (item['input_id'],)).fetchone()\n   109\t        if row:\n   110\t            saved = vocabulary.extraction_answer(json.loads(row['handover_json']))          # a handover saved by a Chinese version reads in the canonical vocabulary\n   111\t            handover = extraction.Handover(saved['evidence'], saved['candidates'], saved['dropped'], 0, '', True, 0.0, saved.get('new_groups') or [])\n   112\t    if handover is None:\n   113\t        try:\n   114\t            handover = (extractor or extraction.extract)(archive, cfg, item, item['text'], shown, universe, transport=transport)\n   115\t        except Exception as error:\n   116\t            return _fail(conn, item, seq, result, 'extracted', 'extraction_failed', 'extraction: ' + repr(error), type(error).__name__)\n   117\t        result.cost += handover.cost_usd\n   118\t        result.cached_calls += int(handover.cached)\n   119\t        store.insert(conn, 'handovers', input_id=item['input_id'], seq=seq,\n   120\t                     handover_json=json.dumps({'evidence': handover.evidence, 'candidates': handover.candidates, 'dropped': handover.dropped, 'new_groups': handover.new_groups}, ensure_ascii=False))\n   121\t        dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'extracted', 'ok', f'{len(handover.evidence)} evidence, {len(handover.candidates)} candidates, {len(handover.dropped)} dropped')\n   122\t        conn.commit()\n   123\t    result.evidence, result.candidates, result.dropped = len(handover.evidence), len(handover.candidates), len(handover.dropped)\n   124\t    if not handover.evidence and not handover.candidates:\n   125\t        dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'handed_over', 'ok', 'nothing to match')\n   126\t        conn.commit()\n   127\t        return result\n   128\t    # first matching call: the candidates and the evidence linked straight to existing views\n   129\t    lists = matching.build_lists(conn, handover, shown, cfg.search_top_n)\n   130\t    checked = _match(conn, archive, cfg, universe, item, seq, result, handover.candidates, handover.evidence, lists, shown, transport=transport, workers=matching_workers)\n   131\t    if checked is None:\n   132\t        return result\n   133\t    # second call: evidence linked to candidates that attached to an existing view, compared under that view\n   134\t    second_pass = {}\n   135\t    pending = []\n   136\t    for e in handover.evidence:\n   137\t        for link in e['links']:\n   138\t            outcome = checked.outcomes.get(link)\n   139\t            if outcome and outcome[0] == 'merge':\n   140\t                pending.append((e, outcome[1]))\n   141\t    if pending:\n   142\t        lists2 = matching.Lists({}, {(e['id'], view_id): matching.rank_evidence(conn, view_id, e['one_line'], cfg.search_top_n) for e, view_id in pending})\n   143\t        evidence2, seen = [], set()\n   144\t        for e, view_id in pending:\n   145\t            if e['id'] not in seen:\n   146\t                evidence2.append(dict(e, links=[v for x, v in pending if x['id'] == e['id']]))\n   147\t                seen.add(e['id'])\n   148\t        checked2 = _match(conn, archive, cfg, universe, item, seq, result, [], evidence2, lists2, [], extra_views=sorted({v for _, v in pending}),\n   149\t                          call_offset=2, transport=transport, workers=matching_workers)\n   150\t        if checked2 is None:\n   151\t            return result\n   152\t        second_pass = checked2.evidence\n   153\t    dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'matched', 'ok', f'{len(checked.outcomes)} candidates placed')\n   154\t    # write, and record what changed in the same commit (a resume at 'judged' reads it)\n   155\t    try:\n   156\t        written = writing.write(conn, universe, seq, item, handover, checked, second_pass)\n   157\t    except Exception as error:\n   158\t        return _fail(conn, item, seq, result, 'written', 'writing_failed', 'writing: ' + repr(error), type(error).__name__)\n   159\t    result.new_views = len(set(written.new_views.values()))\n   160\t    dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'written', 'ok', json.dumps({'changed': sorted(written.changed_views), 'new': written.new_views, 'notes': written.notes[:20]}, ensure_ascii=False))\n   161\t    dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'handed_over', 'ok', '')\n   162\t    conn.commit()\n    51\tdef run(*, testdb_path, views_path, archive, cfg, universe, from_day, until_day, day0=None, spend_cap_usd=None,\n    52\t        transport=None, log=print, only_objects=None, max_items_per_day=None, day_runner=None):\n    53\t    items_db = testdb.open_db(testdb_path)\n    54\t    conn = store.open_db(views_path)\n    55\t    refuse_unfinished_parallel(conn)\n    56\t    last_done = store.last_completed_day(conn)\n    57\t    start = from_day\n    58\t    if last_done and from_day <= last_done:\n    59\t        next_day = (datetime.date.fromisoformat(last_done) + datetime.timedelta(days=1)).isoformat()\n    60\t        if next_day > until_day:\n    61\t            raise BackdatingError(f'views database already completed {last_done}; nothing to run before it')\n    62\t        log(f'resuming after the last completed day {last_done}')\n    63\t        start = next_day\n    64\t    last_written = conn.execute('select max(publication_day) from processing_steps where sequence_no > 0').fetchone()[0]\n    65\t    if last_written and start < last_written:\n    66\t        raise BackdatingError(f'views database already holds rounds of {last_written}; a replay cannot start before it (D31)')\n    67\t    totals = {'items': 0, 'extracted': 0, 'skipped': 0, 'merged': 0, 'not_processed': 0, 'returned': 0, 'failed': 0,\n    68\t              'evidence': 0, 'new_views': 0, 'judged': 0, 'changed': 0, 'closed': 0}\n    69\t    calls_before, cost_before, *_ = archive.totals()\n    70\t    for day in calendar_days(start, until_day):\n    71\t        day_stats = {k: 0 for k in totals}\n    72\t        day_cost_before = archive.totals()[1]\n    73\t        processed = 0\n    74\t        to_run = []\n    75\t        for item in testdb.feed(items_db, day, day):\n    76\t            if item['publication_day'] > day:\n    77\t                raise LookAheadError(f'{item[\"input_id\"]} is dated {item[\"publication_day\"]}, after replay day {day}')\n    78\t            if only_objects and not any(o['value'] in only_objects for o in item['object_identifiers']):\n    79\t                continue\n    80\t            if max_items_per_day and processed >= max_items_per_day:\n    81\t                break\n    82\t            day_stats['items'] += 1\n    83\t            route = dispatch.route(conn, item, universe)\n    84\t            if route.kind != 'extract':\n    85\t                day_stats[route.kind] += 1\n    86\t                if route.kind == 'skipped':\n    87\t                    processed += 1      # written by an earlier run of this day: a restart keeps the day's item limit\n    88\t                if route.kind == 'merged':\n    89\t                    dispatch.mark(conn, item, 0, 'merged', 'ok', route.reason)\n    90\t                    conn.commit()\n    91\t                continue\n    92\t            processed += 1\n    93\t            to_run.append((item, route))\n    94\t        results = (day_runner(conn, archive, cfg, universe, to_run, day=day, transport=transport, log=log) if day_runner else\n    95\t                   (round_module.run(conn, archive, cfg, universe, item, route.sequence_no, resume_from=route.resume_from, transport=transport, log=log)\n    96\t                    for item, route in to_run))\n    97\t        finished = 0\n    98\t        try:\n    99\t            for index, result in enumerate(results):\n   100\t                if index >= len(to_run) or result.input_id != to_run[index][0]['input_id']:\n   101\t                    raise RuntimeError('day runner returned results out of input order')\n   102\t                finished += 1\n   103\t                day_stats['extracted'] += 1\n   104\t                day_stats['evidence'] += result.evidence\n   105\t                day_stats['new_views'] += result.new_views\n   106\t                day_stats['judged'] += result.judged\n   107\t                day_stats['changed'] += result.changed\n   108\t                if result.failed:\n   109\t                    day_stats['failed'] += 1\n   110\t                    log(f'  ! {result.input_id[:60]}: {result.failed}')\n   111\t                    raise RuntimeError(f'item failed; day {day} remains resumable: {result.failed}')\n   112\t                if spend_cap_usd is not None and archive.totals()[1] - cost_before > spend_cap_usd:\n   113\t                    raise RuntimeError(f'spend cap {spend_cap_usd} reached on {day}')\n   114\t        finally:\n   115\t            if hasattr(results, 'close'):\n   116\t                results.close()\n   117\t        if finished != len(to_run):\n   118\t            raise RuntimeError('day runner did not complete every routed item')\n   119\t        seq = store.next_sequence(conn) - 1\n   120\t        judged = round_module.judge_day(conn, archive, cfg, day, seq, transport=transport, log=log)\n   121\t        day_stats['judged'] += judged.judged\n   122\t        day_stats['changed'] += judged.changed\n   123\t        if judged.failed:\n   124\t            day_stats['failed'] += 1\n   125\t            log(f'  ! day judging: {judged.failed}')\n   126\t            raise RuntimeError(f'judging failed; day {day} remains resumable: {judged.failed}')\n   127\t        closed = pull.end_of_day(conn, day, seq)\n   128\t        day_stats['closed'] = len(closed)\n   129\t        # The day ends at the last sequence it wrote, a closing's own sequence on a day without items included, so the next day starts after it.\n   130\t        store.complete_day(conn, day, store.next_sequence(conn) - 1, time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n   131\t        conn.commit()\n   132\t        for key in totals:\n   133\t            totals[key] += day_stats[key]\n   134\t        calls, cost, _, _ = archive.totals()\n   135\t        day_cost = cost - day_cost_before  # Includes discarded speculative calls and repaired refusals.\n   136\t        open_count = len(store.open_views(conn))\n   137\t        log(f'{day} | items {day_stats[\"items\"]:3d} extracted {day_stats[\"extracted\"]:3d} merged {day_stats[\"merged\"]:2d} skipped {day_stats[\"not_processed\"]:2d} '\n   138\t            f'failed {day_stats[\"failed\"]:2d} | evidence {day_stats[\"evidence\"]:3d} new views {day_stats[\"new_views\"]:2d} judged {day_stats[\"judged\"]:3d} '\n   139\t            f'changed {day_stats[\"changed\"]:3d} closed {len(closed)} | open views {open_count} | day ${day_cost:.2f} total ${cost - cost_before:.2f} calls {calls - calls_before}')\n   140\t        if day0 and day == day0:\n   141\t            conn.commit()\n   142\t            shutil.copy(views_path, views_path + '.day0.sqlite')\n   143\t            log(f'day 0 snapshot written: {views_path}.day0.sqlite')\n    15\tENDPOINT = 'https://api.typesafe.ai/v1/systemone'\n    16\tKEY_NAME = 'TYPESAFE_API_KEY'\n    17\tRETRY_STATUSES = {429, 529}\n    18\tATTEMPTS = 3\n    19\t\n    20\t\n    21\tdef _key():\n    22\t    if os.environ.get(KEY_NAME):\n    23\t        return os.environ[KEY_NAME]\n    24\t    with open(model.CREDENTIALS, encoding='utf-8') as handle:\n    25\t        return json.load(handle)[KEY_NAME]\n    26\t\n    27\t\n    28\tdef transport(request, timeout=60):\n    29\t    \"\"\"POST the request; up to three attempts, pausing before each retry, on a rate-limit or overload status or a\n    30\t    connection that fails without a reply; any other failure is a TransportError. The body is the same sorted text the\n    31\t    archive digests, so a cache hit is byte-identical to what was sent.\"\"\"\n    32\t    body = json.dumps(request, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False).encode('utf-8')\n    33\t    key = _key()\n    34\t    for attempt in range(ATTEMPTS):\n    35\t        req = urllib.request.Request(ENDPOINT, body, {'Authorization': 'Bearer ' + key, 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'Accept': 'application/json'})\n    36\t        try:\n    37\t            with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as response:\n    38\t                raw = response.read()\n    39\t            break\n    40\t        except urllib.error.HTTPError as error:\n    41\t            if error.code not in RETRY_STATUSES or attempt == ATTEMPTS - 1:\n    42\t                raise model.TransportError(f'Jev HTTP {error.code}') from None\n    43\t        except (urllib.error.URLError, OSError, http.client.HTTPException) as error:   # a dropped or truncated reply\n    44\t            if attempt == ATTEMPTS - 1:\n    45\t                raise model.TransportError(f'Jev transport failed: {type(error).__name__}') from None\n    46\t        time.sleep(2 * (attempt + 1))\n    47\t    if key.encode('utf-8') in raw:\n    48\t        raise model.TransportError('Jev response echoed the credential; not archived')\n    49\t    return json.loads(raw.decode('utf-8'))\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\t# Jev reports each probability rounded to two decimals independently of the choice it made on the unrounded values, so the\n    53\t# chosen option may print one unit below another (0.47 against 0.48; 1 of 2,353 archived choice answers on 2026-10-25).\n    54\tROUNDING = 0.01\n    55\t\n    56\t\n    57\tdef validate(answers, questions):\n    58\t    \"\"\"The answers of a response against the request's questions; a list of problems.\"\"\"\n    59\t    problems = []\n    60\t    if not isinstance(answers, dict) or set(answers) != set(questions):\n    61\t        return ['answer set differs from the questions asked']\n    62\t    for qid, question in questions.items():\n    63\t        answer = answers[qid]\n    64\t        if not isinstance(answer, dict) or answer.get('type') != question['type']:\n    65\t            problems.append(f'{qid}: answer type mismatch')\n    66\t            continue\n    67\t        if question['type'] == 'noul':\n    68\t            if not isinstance(answer.get('noul'), (int, float)) or not 0 <= answer['noul'] <= 1:\n    69\t                problems.append(f'{qid}: noul out of range')\n    70\t        elif question['type'] == 'choice':\n    71\t            probabilities = answer.get('probabilities')\n    72\t            if answer.get('choice') not in question['criteria'] or not isinstance(probabilities, dict) or set(probabilities) != set(question['criteria']):\n    73\t                problems.append(f'{qid}: choice or probabilities do not match the criteria')\n    74\t            elif any(not isinstance(v, (int, float)) or isinstance(v, bool) or not 0 <= v <= 1 for v in probabilities.values()) \\\n    75\t                    or abs(sum(probabilities.values()) - 1) > 0.005 * len(probabilities) + 1e-9:\n    76\t                problems.append(f'{qid}: probabilities are not a distribution')\n    77\t            elif probabilities[answer['choice']] < max(probabilities.values()) - ROUNDING - 1e-9:\n    78\t                problems.append(f'{qid}: choice is not the most probable option')\n    26\t# USD per million tokens, for the cost column only (an estimate; the provider's bill is the measurement)\n    27\t# gpt-6.1-sol: the published standard rates on 2026-11-16 (developers.openai.com/api/docs/models: \"$2 / $10\" per million input and output\n    28\t# tokens; D628's model comparison only). gpt-6-astra: the published standard rates on 2026-11-16 (developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/\n    29\t# gpt-6-astra: \"$10 input … $50 output\" per million tokens; D632's comparison only).\n    30\t# claude-opus-5-5: Anthropic's first-party list price, $4 input and $20 output per million tokens (the claude-api skill's model table,\n    31\t# cached 2026-11-03); Alex's Opus trial only (2026-11-16, \"你试试看opus\"). Cache reads ($0.20) are priced at CACHED_INPUT_SHARE, an over-estimate.\n    32\t# gpt-6-luna: the published standard rates on 2026-10-25 (developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-6-luna: $0.10/M input, $0.50/M output,\n    33\t# cached input $0.01/M). Until this date the table carried (1.25, 10.0), so every cost_usd recorded before it is 12.5x (input) to 20x (output)\n    34\t# the published rate; the token columns are the measurement, the bill is the provider's.\n    35\tPRICES = {'gpt-6-luna': (0.10, 0.50), 'gpt-6.1-sol': (2.00, 10.00), 'gpt-6-astra': (10.00, 50.00), 'claude-opus-5-5': (4.00, 20.00), 'deepseek-flash': (0.30, 1.20), 'deepseek-v4-pro': (1.32, 3.96),\n    36\t          'jev-1.14.0': (0.042, 0.0)}   # Jev: docs.typesafe.ai/models, 2026-10-25; output free   # DeepSeek: peak-hour list prices, cache misses (2026-10-23 pricing page)\n    37\tCACHED_INPUT_SHARE = 0.10          # cached input tokens are priced at 10% of the input rate (gpt-6-luna page, read again 2026-10-27)\n    38\t\n    39\tSCHEMA_SQL = \"\"\"\n    40\tcreate table if not exists model_calls (\n    41\t  call_id integer primary key autoincrement, purpose text, config_version text, config_checksum text, model text,\n24:def default_as_of(conn):\n57:def resolve_bound(conn, bound, *, unfiltered=False):\n296:def open_pinned(path):\n    16\tThe old system pulled dated batches. Category definitions existed in nine modules, configuration used five overriding layers, and time had several clocks. Explaining an item's path required reading multiple implementations. The rebuild gives each decision one owner.\n    17\t\n    18\t## System boundary\n    19\t\n    20\t- **Upstream, outside this system:** acquire material, classify it, identify related subjects and publication time, and deliver it. Acquisition details are deferred.\n    21\t- **This system:** dispatch through the library and pull mode, which closes due questions.\n    22\t- **Tests:** stream stored items in publication order through the product's path, with replay time supplied to pull mode.\n    23\t\n    24\t```text\n    25\tUpstream → Dispatch → Extraction → Thesis library ↔ Matching labels\n    26\t                         │               ↑\n    27\t                  read-only; groups   Pull mode: at day end, freeze\n    28\t                                      and close due questions\n    29\t```\n    30\t\n    31\t| From | To | Content |\n    32\t|---|---|---|\n    33\t| Research universe | Upstream | Subjects and tracked categories |\n    34\t| Research universe | Extraction | All themes for candidate selection in block 3 |\n   131\t\n   132\t## Modules\n   133\t\n   134\tSee the [PRD index](README.md) for files and status. The universe defines scope; classification labels; Config selects settings; dispatch routes; extraction reads; the library matches, stores and rejudges; matching labels collect supervision; pull mode owns time and closes questions at their due day, with no separate final verdict (D356); human review receives unresolved matters.\n   135\t\n   136\t## Compared with the old system\n   137\t\n   138\t| Aspect | Old system | Rebuild |\n   139\t|---|---|---|\n   140\t| Input | Date-driven pulls | Incoming upstream items |\n   141\t| Processing | Daily batches | Item sequence order |\n   142\t| Categories | Separate definitions in nine modules | One set of 16 |\n   143\t| Scope | Overriding configuration, arguments and presets | Research universe |\n   144\t| Time | Several clocks | Publication day in the stream; supplied “now” in pull mode |\n   145\t| Sources | Local copies | Retrieve from team storage by ID |\n   146\t| Reports | Repeated downloads and stored individual numbers | Whole-item reading into theses and evidence |\n   147\t| Theses | Accumulation, ambiguous rewritten identity and no exit | Fixed question/ladder/due date, identity matching and due-date freezing |\n   148\t\n   149\t## Not yet designed\n   150\t\n   151\tHuman-review handling; upstream acquisition/classification and return notifications; category prompt wording; library open questions, particularly analyst-level thesis granularity; settlement figures for closed questions (prices, filings). A grouping requirement is not evidence that its implementation has passed acceptance.\n   152\t\n   153\t## Related decisions\n   154\t\n5:The default is `poc/config/poc-v118-idea.json`: two candidate-discovery calls (`idea-v7`) followed by one final adoption and weighting call (`idea-summary-v8`, D290, D335). The model/provider and reasoning settings are unchanged from v33. Older configurations retain their original response contracts.\n7:## Request path\n12:                         └─ model call 1: typed parts and an explicit dollar claim\n14:                            → model call 2: map parts to supplied theses and explain\n20:The browser never receives a model credential. The route runs in the service, keeps no user account or commitment, and returns a complete per-request result. Model calls are archived; the same exact request can replay from the archive. A changed library or request is not automatically an identical cached call.\n22:### Live progress\n24:D281 adds optional streaming to the same endpoint. `Accept: application/x-ndjson` returns newline-delimited `progress` records with a `stage`, followed by one `result` record with the existing response in `data`. A handled failure returns an `error` record with `status` and `message`. Ordinary JSON callers keep the existing response. The [progress contract](../research/2026-10-26-library-ui/idea-progress.md) owns the stage boundaries and pending UI. These are public task steps, not model reasoning. Prompts and model-call count do not change.\n26:## Model and code responsibilities\n30:Code searches each part using the model's query and a canonical query composed from subject, focus and period. It interleaves the two result lists without duplicates and supplies candidate briefs. Where semantic search is available, the parts' query embeddings are batched in one round trip.\n34:The final assessment receives candidate theses, their dated states and endpoint conditions. It returns a variable-length list of adopted IDs, each with a positive impact percentage, endpoint and explanation. Each candidate's entry may name only that thesis's own two endpoint positions, enforced in the request schema (D335), and the answer is checked against the schema that was sent. Omitted candidates are not Idea associations; the JSON has no zero-weight or excluded branch. Code checks uniqueness, non-empty explanations and a 100% total, reverses lower-claim direction once and projects all associations onto the adopted set. A provisional claim/evaluation whose direct thesis is omitted is cleared. The model cannot invent IDs or the calculated composite score.\n36:Code selects the first part's direct thesis only from records the model called direct, using that part's search order and the existing year compatibility rule. It does not choose a different financial measure based only on subject/year. The current rule accepts a following fiscal-year label for a calendar-year query; that heuristic is not proof of exact period equivalence.\n42:## Response and consumers\n56:| `cost` | USD estimate, tokens, seconds, cache status and calls | Operator measurements |\n58:Existing field names containing `view` mean **thesis**. They remain stable compatibility names, not a second concept.\n60:## State × event\n65:| No recorded coverage | Null reading/evaluation, no chosen bundles and no Idea model call |\n67:| Missing Idea configuration | Refuse; do not silently switch models |\n77:## Frontend integration\n81:The Idea card previews `reading.summary`; clicking the card or pressing Enter/Space opens analysis (D278/D280). There is no separate View analysis button. Its drawer uses the shared Thesis-style tabs: Overview contains the full summary and adopted theses; Trace contains reading steps and excluded choices; Response displays the structured response directly (D308). Search trace is not rendered as a separate interface section; its original fields remain available in Response (D311). This is the service’s returned analysis, not a private internal reasoning stream. The detail header shows an `AI confidence: xx%` pill, then `| Idea created: date`, using the shared Thesis metadata style. Confidence follows the selected assessment date. Creation is the browser-local day captured for that UI submission, not the library `as_of`; legacy callers without a creation day show `Not recorded` (D297). In Trace, all reading steps are expanded by default. There is no Search trace section below the reading steps (D311). Expanding a step uses the shared Thesis disclosure control and reveals the complete stored explanation and matched theses (D304). Opening it makes no model call. Tabs switch locally with click or arrow/Home/End keys, reset content scroll, and make no requests. A newly opened Idea starts on Overview. A new submission or leaving the Idea view closes the prior detail.\n83:No redundant decomposition table is placed inside the Idea card. The legacy browser-only matcher has been removed. Components do not call a model or infer new group associations. See the [integration guide](../../poc/ui/README.md).\n85:## Idea confidence\n91:The Idea chart title is “AI confidence”, displayed on a 0–100% scale. Code converts the weighted aggregate with `50 + 25 × aggregate`: −2 maps to 0%, neutral maps to 50%, and +2 maps to 100%. The chart draws at the Idea card’s content width; its subtitle and vertical-axis text match the Thesis chart, and the card fits its content with normal bottom padding (D296). The compact pill rounds to a whole percentage; the analysis header uses the same rounded confidence. The adopted-thesis section is titled “Theses”, without a help icon or popup (D306); the numerical contribution table remains omitted. The redundant confidence/count/date row is omitted. Each adopted-thesis explanation starts with its weight badge followed by the full question. The detail badge has 4px corners and stretches to the title height (D303/D305), then separate relevance and weight-rationale paragraphs. Their labels use black, semibold body-sized text; major sections and consecutive thesis blocks use the shared Thesis-detail divider and spacing; only the first thesis has no leading divider (D301). Every associated Thesis card shows a scale icon and `xx%` at the upper right, with the icon vertically centred against the number and no tooltip (D294). Idea thesis cards and explanations appear in descending impact-weight order; equal weights retain the response order. The chart applies the current plan to historical thesis states; it is not a record of earlier plan choices or an outcome probability. The detail drawer lists the same adopted set and its weight rationale. Candidate IDs remain in search trace only. Exact-request replay retains the chosen weights; fresh model choices may differ.\n95:## Historical measurements and limits\n101:| New-idea latency target ≤6 seconds | Full contract 10.9 seconds; lean alternative 8.6 seconds; earlier serial baseline 20.4 seconds | Target not met; the full contract remains adopted |\n102:| Cost target ≤$0.005 per idea | Full $0.0098; lean $0.0070; earlier $0.012–0.013 | Target not met; no automatic budget/model change |\n106:| Second mapping call simulation | 0.73 overlap at another call's cost | Not adopted |\n108:| Wrong direct ladder for claims | 0/13 after respecting the model's direct label | Earlier subject/year-only rule was removed |\n110:| Model-authored 20-idea gold | Correct direct 18/20; two traps; median wanted-driver recall 65%; canvas noise 22%; claim evaluation 20/20 | Gold is an analyst-model reading, not Alex's own labels |\n112:The adopted full contract retains per-part reasons because measured no-reason variants were less stable. Those measurements cover the earlier two-call flow. The current default adds a final adoption/weighting assessment; its three stages, retrieval coverage and semantic errors remain limitations. Older agent-loop counts, speedups and approximate floors are historical environment measurements, not promises for current hardware or providers.\n114:D280 preserves the original two mapping requests and adds the isolated TLDR after selection. Its focused development comparison and measured cost/latency are in [the TLDR report](../../poc/reports/2026-10-26-analyst-tldr/results.md); this does not establish broad Idea matching quality or meet the historical whole-flow latency target.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '3151,3170p'; nl -ba clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/preflight/PREFLIGHT-SLICE.md | head -100; rg -n 'v118|p1|p2|p3|[0-9]s|seconds|refus' docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/{week/WEEK-RESULT.md,reflection-8/challenge-1.md} clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/STATUS-FOR-ALEX-2026-11-13.md | cut -c1-280 | head -35; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/WEEK-RESULT.md | sed -n '1,89p'; nl -ba docs/poc/idea-card.md | rg -n 'stability|cost|s[ /]|seconds|quality|tested' | head -26\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '3151,3170p'; nl -ba clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/preflight/PREFLIGHT-SLICE.md | head -100; rg -n 'v118|p1|p2|p3|[0-9]s|seconds|refus' docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/{week/WEEK-RESULT.md,reflection-8/challenge-1.md} clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/STATUS-FOR-ALEX-2026-11-13.md | cut -c1-280 | head -35; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/WEEK-RESULT.md | sed -n '1,89p'; nl -ba docs/poc/idea-card.md | rg -n 'stability|cost|s[ /]|seconds|quality|tested' | head -26\"","aggregated_output":"  3151\t## D274 · 2026-11-03 · The extraction production prompt is frozen at v74i (`poc-v108`); the unadopted variants are retired\n  3152\t\n  3153\t- Alex: \"感觉已经瓶颈了，上一个版本是不是freeze作为我们的抽取生产提示词吧。你顺道把所有其他不相关的clean up sanitize吧\". Read as: the last prompt version, v74i (D273's\n  3154\t  three exceptions narrowed), at low reasoning, the configuration every reasoning test of the third round kept unchanged; it beat the D272 default on core\n  3155\t  matters, supporting matters and noise on the 50 stored articles (D273 amended). If he meant v74d, the default goes back to `poc-v103` with one line.\n  3156\t- Frozen: `poc/config/poc-v108.json` is the replay default (`scripts/replay.py`, README, AGENTS); `tests/test_frozen_extraction_prompt.py` pins the sha256 of\n  3157\t  role-v74i, review-v74i, categories-v74i and the configuration, the links rule (`placement.FILING_RULE_ROOT_FALLBACK`, now a constant of its own), the\n  3158\t  code-written takes lines and the evidence schema; a one-character change to the check fails it (mutant checked). AGENTS \"Where to look first\" names it.\n  3159\t- Retired, never run as a stored run and never a default, backed up first (`research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/retired-2026-11-03/retired-variants.tar.gz`,\n  3160\t  54 files, sha256 manifest beside it, restore verified): prompt files of v74b, v74c, v74e–v74h, v74j, v74k, v76, v77, v78, v79, v80; configurations\n  3161\t  poc-v96, v97, v98–v102, v104–v107, v109–v114; `tests/test_evidence_fields.py` (the field route's tests leave with it). Code removed with them: the v78–v80\n  3162\t  classification fields and `evidence_rule` in the sift (and the `>= 78` version gates that would have caught any future version), the section markers\n  3163\t  of v74j, the variant tables of v74f–v74k; `REVIEW_VERSIONS_ALSO` keeps 72–75. Kept: v94 and v95 (stored runs), v74d / `poc-v103` (D272's default), every\n  3164\t  research record, proof, saved answer and probe. The request bytes of `poc-v94`, `poc-v95`, `poc-v103` and `poc-v108` on three stored articles are\n  3165\t  identical before and after the cleanup (sha256 compared). Tests: `test_v74_production_text.py` (v74d and v74i), the review gate test states v76–v80 do\n  3166\t  not exist; suite 283.\n  3167\t- Sanitized: no company, product or bench name in the frozen prompt files; no credential pattern in any changed or new file.\n  3168\t- Not done: the length rule for reasoning (D273 amended) stays a proposal; it would be a new version opened by Alex.\n  3169\t\n  3170\t## Decisions recorded on `main` while the extraction work ran on its branch (renumbered at the 2026-11-03 merge)\n     1\t# Preflight before the slice (AGENTS §5; council mo, 2026-11-13)\n     2\t\n     3\t**Production (v118).** `scripts/preflight.py` over the three stored unseeded v118 draws (`preflight-v118-q1..q3.txt`; exit 0 each), the\n     4\tcurrent code:\n     5\t\n     6\t| check | q1 | q2 | q3 |\n     7\t|---|---|---|---|\n     8\t| A. answers the schema refused | judged 0 | judged 0 | judged 1, refused 1 |\n     9\t| B. extraction checks: judged / refused | 747 / 8 | 769 / 9 | 731 / 9 |\n    10\t| refusal reasons | quote not in item 7, duplicate quote merged 1 | quote not in item 6, duplicate quote 2, a candidate ladder with no rungs 1 | quote not in item 7, a binding obligation due beyond 18 months 1, duplicate quote 1 |\n    11\t| C. matching checks: judged / refused / skipped | 106 / 0 / 2 | 151 / 0 / 4 | 139 / 0 / 3 (skipped: \"request not in this archive\") |\n    12\t| D. enum values named in the prompts | 43, missing 0 | 43, missing 0 | 43, missing 0 |\n    13\t| E. keyed views, duplicates | 13, 0 | 12, 0 | 15, 0 |\n    14\t\n    15\tThe refusals are production's own checks on its own answers, the same kinds and rates as the v116 preflight (`preflight-v116-d*.txt`); none\n    16\tcomes from the wiring, which does not change a request (the byte-for-byte control in `proof_interception.py`). *Does not exercise:* the\n    17\tbudget transport (proved by `proof_interception.py` and `proof_end_to_end.py`), v118's behaviour on a fresh day (the slice shows it).\n    18\t\n    19\t**The clean path.** Its checks on stored answers through the current code are the $0 proofs: `proof_wiring.py` (Stage B rebuilt row for\n    20\trow), `proof_interception.py` (Step 1 one day as stored, Step 2 byte for byte, Stage A run 4 every outcome, the judge every table),\n    21\t`proof_end_to_end.py` (one day through the orchestrator: Step 1, the cases and the ladder outcomes as stored). *Does not exercise:* the\n    22\tcoverage-start reading's check (an open defect of the preflight, `CURRENT_STATE.md`), new model answers (the slice shows them).\n    23\t\n    24\t**Measurement capture added for the slice** (council mo, round 8): the ledger writes one line per settled or refused attempt (process id,\n    25\treserved, charged, time; `check_budget.py` check 17); the draw record keeps each attempt's process id and start and end times;\n    26\t`spend_by_component.py` maps the lines to components. In the end-to-end proof: every line attributed, the lines sum to the ledger's spent,\n    27\tevery attempt timed (Step 1 13 attempts $0.1206, Step 2 19 $0.0089, the ladder 2 $0.0018, the judge 2 $0.0021, production 19 $0.0094; ledger\n    28\tcharges from stored usage).\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-8/challenge-1.md:58:- The running pipeline (`p1..p3/prod`) is $0.53 to $0.66 per 14-day draw, about $0.04 a day.\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/STATUS-FOR-ALEX-2026-11-13.md:6:its own checks. This comparison used the current local replay setup of the existing system (v118).\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/STATUS-FOR-ALEX-2026-11-13.md:40:| Fix the new design's answer-choice step | the judge reads only the first attempt; it had three agreed faults of three kinds, none on a graded question: two reached the judge, one question was wrongly refused \ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/WEEK-RESULT.md:11:`poc/data/clean-lean-week-2026-11-14/week-r2/c1` (after D488), production `…/week/p1`. Readers: Codex (read-only) and Claude subagents, blind\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/WEEK-RESULT.md:17:| | clean c1 | production p1 |\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/WEEK-RESULT.md:29:| matter | listed by | clean c1 | production p1 |\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/WEEK-RESULT.md:44:| | clean c1 (7) | production p1 (15) |\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/WEEK-RESULT.md:68:| production p1 (15) | 10 / 2 / 3 | 14 / 1 / 0 |\n     1\t# Lean step 2: one fresh week, one draw a system — result (D487, D488), 2026-11-14\n     2\t\n     3\t**Answer: by the rule written before reading, the difference is not clear.** Production covers two more of the five big matters both reader\n     4\tfamilies listed (4 against 2), which meets the rule's first half; its share of last judgements both families call supported is lower by 19\n     5\tpoints (10 of 15 against 6 of 7), more than the one in ten the second half allows. Each half has one named cause. The first is one rule: the\n     6\tthree matters the clean path lacks are the company's own revenue and margin, which its request forbids as questions (D382). The second rests\n     7\tmostly on one reader family: Codex failed 2 of the 4 judgements a separate reader had confirmed as supported, both of them production's;\n     8\tboth families call only one judgement unsupported, production's data-center revenue.\n     9\t\n    10\tMaterial: 2026-09-22..28, 235 articles (232 never sent by any run), each system one draw from an empty library: the clean path\n    11\t`poc/data/clean-lean-week-2026-11-14/week-r2/c1` (after D488), production `…/week/p1`. Readers: Codex (read-only) and Claude subagents, blind\n    12\tto the systems and to each other; the keys are outside the repository. Model cost of the step (the one-day slice, production's draw, the\n    13\tclean draw and its two stopped attempts): $4.69. One draw each: every count below is one draw.\n    14\t\n    15\t## What each system holds at the week's end (counted from the stored runs)\n    16\t\n    17\t| | clean c1 | production p1 |\n    18\t|---|---|---|\n    19\t| questions opened | 7 | 15 |\n    20\t| statements written | 569, from 182 articles | 673, from 186 articles |\n    21\t| thrown away for having no question | 0 | 278 |\n    22\t| kept (after joining repeats) | 569 (314) | 385 |\n    23\t| kept with no question: no judgement reads them | 389 | 0 |\n    24\t| links to questions | 196 | 449 (126 on FY2027 total revenue, 94 on data-center revenue) |\n    25\t| judgements | 37 | 72 |\n    26\t\n    27\t## A. Big questions (40 sampled articles; eight matters, five listed by both families)\n    28\t\n    29\t| matter | listed by | clean c1 | production p1 |\n    30\t|---|---|---|---|\n    31\t| M01 FY2027 revenue (total or data center) | both | **missed** | opened (v2, v4) |\n    32\t| M02 FY2028 revenue | both | **missed** | opened (v3, v5) |\n    33\t| M03 FY2028 gross margin against the 72%–73% outlook | both | **missed** | opened (v10) |\n    34\t| M04 supply and capacity purchase commitments ($279B at Q2) | both | opened (clean-2) | **missed** |\n    35\t| M05 Beijing's approval of RTX Pro 5500 purchases | both | opened (clean-7) | opened (v14, v15) |\n    36\t| M06 FY2027 gross margin | one | missed | missed |\n    37\t| M07 Vera Rubin revenue shipments in Q3 | one | opened (Claude) / a later deadline that does not settle Q3 (Codex) | the same split |\n    38\t| M08 AMD's 2027 data-center revenue | one | missed | missed |\n    39\t\n    40\tThe families give the same status on 14 of 16 cells and on all ten cells of M01–M05. **Covered, of the five: clean 2, production 4.**\n    41\t\n    42\tEach opened question, read beside the article it was opened from:\n    43\t\n    44\t| | clean c1 (7) | production p1 (15) |\n    45\t|---|---|---|\n    46\t| worth holding | 6 (both families) | 9 (Codex) / 8 (Claude) |\n    47\t| trivia | 1: the Hugging Face purchase closing | 3: \"tech companies' AI spending\" (nothing settles it), the Hugging Face price as a commitment, the Anthropic IPO stake |\n    48\t| duplicate of another of its own | 0 | 3 by both: FY2028 growth of FY2028 revenue, Rubin by end-2027 of Rubin by January 2027, the second RTX Pro 5500 question; Claude adds data-center revenue of total revenue |\n    49\t\n    50\tChecked by Claude against the stored runs:\n    51\t- Production has no supply-commitments question: its one kept statement on the $279 billion is linked to the credit-support question (v1).\n    52\t- The clean path's three misses are its rule at work. On each article where production opened v2, v3, v4, v5 and v10, the clean draw's\n    53\t  stored reasoning names the request's sentence \"Do not open a thesis about … a financial measure's level, growth, margin or guidance for\n    54\t  any period, on its own\", opens nothing and keeps the statements; 109 of 235 steps' reasoning names that sentence. The request sends such\n    55\t  figures to \"an open thesis about its revenue or earnings path\", which nothing in an empty library is: 145 kept statements of the company's\n    56\t  own figures (from 67 articles) have no question, among them the 70% growth outlook for fiscal 2028, which the articles set against the 45%\n    57\t  the Street had modelled (14 statements, 14 articles), and gross-margin figures of 71% to 73% (11 statements, 9 articles).\n    58\t- Both families call the Hugging Face purchase small (both systems opened a question on it). It is listed as the readers gave it; D389's\n    59\t  size line is for unsigned obligations in its own test and does not rule on this question (council round 11).\n    60\t\n    61\t## B. Judgement support (26 items: 22 real last judgements, 4 planted from earlier judgements)\n    62\t\n    63\t| | Codex | Claude |\n    64\t|---|---|---|\n    65\t| planted wrong judgements caught | 4 of 4 | 4 of 4 |\n    66\t| supported controls passed (confirmed first by a separate reader) | **2 of 4** | 4 of 4 |\n    67\t| clean c1 (7): supported / unsupported / insufficient | 6 / 1 / 0 | 7 / 0 / 0 |\n    68\t| production p1 (15) | 10 / 2 / 3 | 14 / 1 / 0 |\n    69\t\n    70\tSupported by both families: **clean 6 of 7 (86%), production 10 of 15 (67%)**. Unsupported by both: one, production's data-center revenue (v4):\n    71\tits rung is reached by a fourth-quarter growth of about 25% that the judge itself calls an allowance; no shown piece gives the rate, and the\n    72\tshown 18% lands a rung lower. Called not supported by Codex alone: the clean path's credit-support total (a cap read as the amount);\n    73\tproduction's credit-support total and its first RTX Pro 5500 question (**both are confirmed supported controls**), the Hugging Face amount and\n    74\tthe Anthropic stake (both also called trivia in A). Cited statements with a field error: one in each system (a quarter mislabelled; \"more than\n    75\tdoubling to $115 billion\" written as \"will exceed\").\n    76\t\n    77\t## The rule, applied as written (LEAN-LOG §2)\n    78\t\n    79\t- First half (A): production covers two more of the matters both families listed. Met by production.\n    80\t- Second half (B): its share of judgements both families call supported is lower by 19 points, more than one in ten. Not met.\n    81\t- **Verdict: not clear. The next small step targets the largest difference observed, not a choice of system.**\n    82\t\n    83\tWhat weakens each half: A's three-matter gap is one sentence of the clean request, a product rule (D382), not a capability. B compares 7\n    84\tjudgements with 15, so one judgement is 14 points for the clean path; the gap comes from one family, which parted from the separate reader on two of the four supported controls, both production items, with\n    85\treasons that stand as a disagreement (a guarantee cap read as the amount; permission for two named firms read from \"some firms\"). As a\n    86\tsensitivity note only: with those two counted as the separate reader read them, production would stand at 12 of 15; the rule's count stays\n    87\t10 of 15. B at this size cannot say which system judges better.\n    88\t\n    89\t## The largest difference observed\n1:     1\t# Idea card: read a user's idea against the thesis library\n3:     3\tD112–D145; English edition and current-document refresh, October 25, 2026 (D163). A user supplies an **idea**; the library contains **theses**. The service reads the idea against those records and returns the information the frontend needs. User text does not become a stored thesis merely by opening an Idea card.\n5:     5\tThe default is `poc/config/poc-v118-idea.json`: two candidate-discovery calls (`idea-v7`) followed by one final adoption and weighting call (`idea-summary-v8`, D290, D335). The model/provider and reasoning settings are unchanged from v33. Older configurations retain their original response contracts.\n10:    10\tUser idea → POST /ideas → coverage search\n12:    12\t                         └─ model call 1: typed parts and an explicit dollar claim\n13:    13\t                            → code searches each part\n14:    14\t                            → model call 2: map parts to supplied theses and explain\n15:    15\t                            → code validates IDs and claim, reads related theses\n17:    17\t                            → return Idea card, evaluation and optional thesis bundles\n20:    20\tThe browser never receives a model credential. The route runs in the service, keeps no user account or commitment, and returns a complete per-request result. Model calls are archived; the same exact request can replay from the archive. A changed library or request is not automatically an identical cached call.\n24:    24\tD281 adds optional streaming to the same endpoint. `Accept: application/x-ndjson` returns newline-delimited `progress` records with a `stage`, followed by one `result` record with the existing response in `data`. A handled failure returns an `error` record with `status` and `message`. Ordinary JSON callers keep the existing response. The [progress contract](../research/2026-10-26-library-ui/idea-progress.md) owns the stage boundaries and pending UI. These are public task steps, not model reasoning. Prompts and model-call count do not change.\n28:    28\tCall 1 returns two to four typed parts: subject in `object`, figure/event in `looks_for`, period and search query. The first part is the idea's main question. A claim is present only for an explicit US-dollar amount, with part index, comparator and full-dollar value.\n30:    30\tCode searches each part using the model's query and a canonical query composed from subject, focus and period. It interleaves the two result lists without duplicates and supplies candidate briefs. Where semantic search is available, the parts' query embeddings are batched in one round trip.\n32:    32\tCall 2 maps each part to supplied candidates as `direct`, `driver` or `context`, writes a per-part reason and a short summary. The adopted driver definition includes causes or consequences. The service does not use the unadopted `idea-v10` causal-clause requirement. It preserves only allowed candidate IDs; it reports dropped choices.\n34:    34\tThe final assessment receives candidate theses, their dated states and endpoint conditions. It returns a variable-length list of adopted IDs, each with a positive impact percentage, endpoint and explanation. Each candidate's entry may name only that thesis's own two endpoint positions, enforced in the request schema (D335), and the answer is checked against the schema that was sent. Omitted candidates are not Idea associations; the JSON has no zero-weight or excluded branch. Code checks uniqueness, non-empty explanations and a 100% total, reverses lower-claim direction once and projects all associations onto the adopted set. A provisional claim/evaluation whose direct thesis is omitted is cleared. The model cannot invent IDs or the calculated composite score.\n36:    36\tCode selects the first part's direct thesis only from records the model called direct, using that part's search order and the existing year compatibility rule. It does not choose a different financial measure based only on subject/year. The current rule accepts a following fiscal-year label for a calendar-year query; that heuristic is not proof of exact period equivalence.\n38:    38\tIn the current configuration, only the final positively weighted set goes to the canvas; code imposes no thesis-count quota and appends no dependency neighbours. Candidate discovery does not itself establish final associations. Historical configurations retain their prior cap and related-thesis behavior.\n40:    40\tA share-price, market-cap or valuation part is treated as a market reading and is not evaluated against business-figure ladders. A claim must name an existing part, state an amount in the original idea and have a direct thesis. Code evaluates the claim against that thesis's numeric ladder; a driver is not a substitute for the named quantity.\n47:    47\t| `search` | Mode and initial candidate IDs | Trace/debug display |\n49:    49\t| `reading.composite` | Version, method, requested date, named target/direction, adopted representatives with supporting endpoints, positive impact percentages and reasons; older versions retain their own fields | Composite chart, per-Idea card weights and calculation detail |\n50:    50\t| `reading.parts[]` | Subject, focus, period, query, candidates, direct/driver/context IDs, selected direct ID, market-reading flag and reason | Coverage explanation; does not create ledger records |\n52:    52\t| `related[]` | Related thesis ID, `via`, upstream/downstream relation, direction and current judgement | Graph edges |\n53:    53\t| `views[]` | Complete dated bundles for chosen and related theses, unless disabled | `fromIdeaResponse` and shared thesis components |\n54:    54\t| `days[]` | Completed ledger days visible at the requested date | Replay/date controls |\n55:    55\t| `no_recorded_view` | Whether initial coverage search returned null | Distinguish no coverage from no relevant choices |\n56:    56\t| `cost` | USD estimate, tokens, seconds, cache status and calls | Operator measurements |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/model.py | sed -n '39,119p;254,311p'; rg -n 'trace|_attempt|checks_json|refus' scripts/preflight.py src/hivemind/views/judging.py src/hivemind/model.py | head -67; ls poc/data/clean-e2e-full-2026-11-13/{p1,p2,p3}/prod; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v12.md | sed -n '143,173p'; nl -ba scripts/hivemind_api.py | sed -n '26,43p;155,204p'; nl -ba scripts/hivemind_mcp.py | sed -n '27,54p;80,103p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/model.py | sed -n '39,119p;254,311p'; rg -n 'trace|_attempt|checks_json|refus' scripts/preflight.py src/hivemind/views/judging.py src/hivemind/model.py | head -67; ls poc/data/clean-e2e-full-2026-11-13/{p1,p2,p3}/prod; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v12.md | sed -n '143,173p'; nl -ba scripts/hivemind_api.py | sed -n '26,43p;155,204p'; nl -ba scripts/hivemind_mcp.py | sed -n '27,54p;80,103p'\"","aggregated_output":"    39\tSCHEMA_SQL = \"\"\"\n    40\tcreate table if not exists model_calls (\n    41\t  call_id integer primary key autoincrement, purpose text, config_version text, config_checksum text, model text,\n    42\t  request_sha256 text unique, request_json text, response_json text, answer_json text, prompt_chars integer,\n    43\t  input_tokens integer, output_tokens integer, cost_usd real, seconds real, created_at text\n    44\t);\n    45\tcreate index if not exists model_calls_sha on model_calls(request_sha256);\n    46\t\"\"\"\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\tclass SchemaError(ValueError):\n    50\t    pass\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\tclass TransportError(RuntimeError):\n    54\t    pass\n    55\t\n    56\t\n    57\t@dataclasses.dataclass\n    58\tclass Answer:\n    59\t    data: dict\n    60\t    call_id: int\n    61\t    request_sha256: str\n    62\t    cached: bool\n    63\t    prompt_chars: int\n    64\t    input_tokens: int\n    65\t    output_tokens: int\n    66\t    cost_usd: float\n    67\t\n    68\t\n    69\tclass Archive:\n    70\t    \"\"\"Shared by the extraction worker threads: one connection, every access under a lock.\"\"\"\n    71\t\n    72\t    def __init__(self, path):\n    73\t        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(path)), exist_ok=True)\n    74\t        self.conn = sqlite3.connect(path, check_same_thread=False)\n    75\t        self.conn.executescript(SCHEMA_SQL)\n    76\t        import threading\n    77\t        self.lock = threading.Lock()\n    78\t\n    79\t    def lookup(self, sha):\n    80\t        with self.lock:\n    81\t            return self.conn.execute('select call_id, answer_json, prompt_chars, input_tokens, output_tokens from model_calls where request_sha256=?', (sha,)).fetchone()\n    82\t\n    83\t    def record(self, **fields):\n    84\t        \"\"\"One row per distinct request; a second identical request recorded at the same moment (two threads, or a\n    85\t        failed answer repeated within the same second) keeps the first row's id instead of failing.\"\"\"\n    86\t        columns = list(fields)\n    87\t        with self.lock:\n    88\t            cursor = self.conn.execute(f'insert or ignore into model_calls ({\",\".join(columns)}) values ({\",\".join(\"?\" * len(columns))})',\n    89\t                                       [fields[c] for c in columns])\n    90\t            self.conn.commit()\n    91\t            if cursor.rowcount == 0:\n    92\t                return self.conn.execute('select call_id from model_calls where request_sha256=?', (fields['request_sha256'],)).fetchone()[0]\n    93\t            return cursor.lastrowid\n    94\t\n    95\t    def retire(self, call_id):\n    96\t        \"\"\"A code check refused this answer: the row stays for the record, but no later identical request is answered with it\n    97\t        (the same shape as a schema-refused or malformed row, whose hash carries a suffix).\"\"\"\n    98\t        with self.lock:\n    99\t            self.conn.execute(\"update model_calls set request_sha256 = request_sha256 || ':refused:' || ? where call_id=? and request_sha256 not like '%:refused:%'\",\n   100\t                              (uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], call_id))\n   101\t            self.conn.commit()\n   102\t\n   103\t    def totals(self):\n   104\t        with self.lock:\n   105\t            return self.conn.execute('select count(*), coalesce(sum(cost_usd),0), coalesce(sum(input_tokens),0), coalesce(sum(output_tokens),0) from model_calls').fetchone()\n   106\t\n   107\t\n   108\tdef _key(provider):\n   109\t    name = ENDPOINTS[provider][1]\n   110\t    if os.environ.get(name):\n   111\t        return os.environ[name]\n   112\t    with open(CREDENTIALS, encoding='utf-8') as handle:\n   113\t        return json.load(handle)[name]\n   114\t\n   115\t\n   116\tdef build_request(setting, system, user, schema, schema_name, provider):\n   117\t    request = {\n   118\t        'model': setting.model,\n   119\t        'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': system}, {'role': 'user', 'content': user}],\n   254\t    request_json, sha = request_identity(request)\n   255\t    hit = archive.lookup(sha)\n   256\t    prompt_chars = len(system) + len(user)\n   257\t    if hit:\n   258\t        call_id, answer_json, _, input_tokens, output_tokens = hit\n   259\t        return Answer(json.loads(answer_json), call_id, sha, True, prompt_chars, input_tokens or 0, output_tokens or 0, 0.0)\n   260\t    started = time.time()\n   261\t    response = (transport or openai_transport)(provider, request)\n   262\t    seconds = round(time.time() - started, 1)\n   263\t    try:\n   264\t        content = response['choices'][0]['message']['content']\n   265\t        data = json.loads(content)\n   266\t    except (KeyError, IndexError, TypeError, json.JSONDecodeError) as error:\n   267\t        archive.record(purpose=purpose, config_version=cfg.version, config_checksum=cfg.checksum, model=setting.model,\n   268\t                       request_sha256=sha + ':malformed:' + uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], request_json=request_json,\n   269\t                       response_json=json.dumps(response)[:200000], answer_json=None, prompt_chars=prompt_chars,\n   270\t                       input_tokens=0, output_tokens=0, cost_usd=0.0, seconds=seconds, created_at=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n   271\t        raise SchemaError(f'malformed answer: {error}')\n   272\t    errors = check_schema(data, schema)\n   273\t    usage = response.get('usage') or {}\n   274\t    input_tokens = int(usage.get('prompt_tokens') or 0)\n   275\t    output_tokens = int(usage.get('completion_tokens') or 0)\n   276\t    cached_tokens = min(input_tokens, int((usage.get('prompt_tokens_details') or {}).get('cached_tokens') or 0))\n   277\t    price_in, price_out = PRICES.get(setting.model, (0.0, 0.0))\n   278\t    cost = round((input_tokens - cached_tokens) / 1e6 * price_in + cached_tokens / 1e6 * price_in * CACHED_INPUT_SHARE + output_tokens / 1e6 * price_out, 6)\n   279\t    call_id = archive.record(purpose=purpose, config_version=cfg.version, config_checksum=cfg.checksum, model=setting.model,\n   280\t                             request_sha256=sha if not errors else sha + ':schema:' + uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], request_json=request_json,\n   281\t                             response_json=json.dumps(response)[:200000], answer_json=json.dumps(data, ensure_ascii=False),\n   282\t                             prompt_chars=prompt_chars, input_tokens=input_tokens, output_tokens=output_tokens, cost_usd=cost,\n   283\t                             seconds=seconds, created_at=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n   284\t    if errors:\n   285\t        raise SchemaError('; '.join(errors[:5]))\n   286\t    return Answer(data, call_id, sha, False, prompt_chars, input_tokens, output_tokens, cost)\nsrc/hivemind/model.py:96:        \"\"\"A code check refused this answer: the row stays for the record, but no later identical request is answered with it\nsrc/hivemind/model.py:97:        (the same shape as a schema-refused or malformed row, whose hash carries a suffix).\"\"\"\nsrc/hivemind/model.py:99:            self.conn.execute(\"update model_calls set request_sha256 = request_sha256 || ':refused:' || ? where call_id=? and request_sha256 not like '%:refused:%'\",\nsrc/hivemind/model.py:131:def openai_transport(provider, request, timeout=180, max_attempts=3):   # the default preserves the production retry behavior\nsrc/hivemind/model.py:137:    if isinstance(max_attempts, bool) or not isinstance(max_attempts, int) or max_attempts < 1:\nsrc/hivemind/model.py:138:        raise ValueError('max_attempts must be a positive integer')\nsrc/hivemind/model.py:139:    for attempt in range(max_attempts):\nsrc/hivemind/model.py:146:                    if max_attempts != 1:\nsrc/hivemind/model.py:156:                    if max_attempts != 1:\nsrc/hivemind/model.py:164:            body_text = body_bytes.decode('utf-8', 'replace' if max_attempts == 1 else 'ignore')\nsrc/hivemind/model.py:176:        if max_attempts == 3 or attempt + 1 < max_attempts:\nsrc/hivemind/views/judging.py:7:refused before any call. Every answer is stored in the canonical vocabulary.\nsrc/hivemind/views/judging.py:19:rung, and an empty one is refused.\"\"\"\nsrc/hivemind/views/judging.py:323:                archive.retire(answer.call_id)                 # a refused answer never answers the same request again (a resume re-samples)\nscripts/preflight.py:6:the cases judged, the cases refused and the reasons with examples:\nscripts/preflight.py:8:  A. answers the schema refused (prompt and schema disagree: a value the prompt's wording suggested but the enum lacks)\nscripts/preflight.py:50:def tally(title, judged, refused, reasons, examples):\nscripts/preflight.py:51:    share = f'{refused / judged:.0%}' if judged else 'n/a'\nscripts/preflight.py:52:    print(f'\\n== {title}: judged {judged}, refused/dropped {refused} ({share})')\nscripts/preflight.py:61:    rows = archive_conn.execute(\"select purpose, request_sha256, answer_json from model_calls where request_sha256 like '%:schema:%' or request_sha256 like '%:malformed:%' or request_sha256 like '%:refused:%'\")\nscripts/preflight.py:71:    tally('A. answers the schema refused (prompt/schema disagreements; empty when the provider enforces the schema server-side)', judged, judged, reasons, examples)\nscripts/preflight.py:113:        if any(marker in sha for marker in (':schema:', ':malformed:', ':refused:')):\nscripts/preflight.py:157:    print(f'\\n   extraction archive rows {len(rows)}: replayed {judged}, earlier refused {other}, retired {sum(unverifiable.values())}, '\nscripts/preflight.py:185:    written is refused with the snapshot route named; the path checked on both sides of the open and after the copy; the copy made by\nscripts/preflight.py:222:    judged = refused_records = 0\nscripts/preflight.py:253:                judged += 1; refused_records += 1; ledger_judged += 1\nscripts/preflight.py:257:            if checked.refusals:\nscripts/preflight.py:258:                refused_records += 1\nscripts/preflight.py:259:            for refusal in checked.refusals:\nscripts/preflight.py:260:                key = normalise_reason(refusal)\nscripts/preflight.py:262:                examples[key].append(f'{os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(path))} {rec[\"input_id\"][:40]}: {refusal[:90]}')\nscripts/preflight.py:264:    tally('C. matching code checks over stored records (database state is the final one, not the state at the time)', judged, refused_records, reasons, examples)\npoc/data/clean-e2e-full-2026-11-13/p1/prod:\narchive.sqlite\nmanifests\nreplay.log\nviews.sqlite\n\npoc/data/clean-e2e-full-2026-11-13/p2/prod:\narchive.sqlite\nmanifests\nreplay.log\nviews.sqlite\n\npoc/data/clean-e2e-full-2026-11-13/p3/prod:\narchive.sqlite\nmanifests\nreplay.log\nviews.sqlite\n   143\t4. **The cards and their marks:**\n   144\t   - **Worth tracking:** worth, trivia or duplicate. Each card lists its library's other questions in opening order, with their opening days.\n   145\t     `duplicate` is marked only on the later question of a same-bet pair.\n   146\t   - **Answer:** supported, unsupported, insufficient, or no answer (a question not judged by the cutoff).\n   147\t   - **Cannot tell:** a split after the debate rounds, resolved in each counting by item 7.\n   148\t5. **Served in a draw:** at least one covering question is marked `worth` and supported, in each counting after item 7's resolution. A matter **served by a system** is served in\n   149\t   at least 2 of its 3 draws.\n   150\t6. **The quantities:** a = served only by the new system; b = served only by the old; N = all listed matters.\n   151\t7. **The two countings.** A split (\"cannot tell\" after the debate rounds) resolves to one of the marks its readers actually gave.\n   152\t   - **Counting 1:** the new system's cards take the most favourable mark given; the old system's cards take the least favourable.\n   153\t   - **Counting 2:** the reverse.\n   154\t   - **The order:** for the mapping, covers > does not cover; for the answer, supported > insufficient > unsupported; for worth, worth >\n   155\t     duplicate or trivia.\n   156\t   - **How a resolved mark counts:** it counts as that mark. A resolved supported or unsupported mark enters the decided denominators. A\n   157\t     resolved insufficient mark stays out of them, as any insufficient mark does.\n   158\t   - A guardrail subgroup is **exercised** only with at least 10 cards decided **without** a split. A subgroup that is not exercised cannot\n   159\t     breach. It blocks only a practical lead; a loss established otherwise still stands.\n   160\t8. **The guardrails** (D428's measure, which D665 turns into these guardrails):\n   161\t   - **The sample:** the random guardrail sample only, 35 questions per system-draw by seed 20261117, or all of them when a library holds\n   162\t     fewer. Covering cards are not in these shares. The three draws are pooled per system.\n   163\t   - **The shares:**\n   164\t     - the share of **decided** figure-question answers (supported or unsupported) that are unsupported;\n   165\t     - the same for yes/no questions;\n   166\t     - the share of decided worth marks that are trivia or duplicate.\n   167\t   - **Reported beside, not in the shares:** insufficient and no answer, with the number of splits and how each counting resolved them.\n   168\t   - **The bar:** the new system's share may not be more than 10 points above the old system's.\n   169\t   - **Exercised:** each subgroup needs at least 10 cards per system decided without a split (item 7), or it is \"not exercised\".\n   170\t9. **The controls,** outside every product count:\n   171\t   - 6 planted wrong answers (a rung moved, 3 per system). Each needs an explicit unsupported or insufficient mark, or the reading is invalid.\n   172\t   - 4 supported controls, confirmed first by a separate reader.\n   173\t   - 3 hidden repeats.\n    26\timport http.server\n    27\timport json\n    28\timport os\n    29\timport sys\n    30\timport urllib.parse\n    31\t\n    32\tROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))\n    33\tsys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(ROOT, 'src'))\n    34\tfrom hivemind import bundle, config, idea, live_lock, model, search, service  # noqa: E402\n    35\tfrom hivemind.views import store  # noqa: E402\n    36\t\n    37\tPATHS = {}\n    38\tALIASES = {}\n    39\tCFG = None\n    40\tSEMANTIC = True\n    41\tREQUEST_ERRORS = (KeyError, service.LedgerError, live_lock.LockRefused, model.TransportError, model.SchemaError, config.ConfigError, ValueError, TypeError)\n    42\t\n    43\t\n   155\t    def do_GET(self):\n   156\t        url = urllib.parse.urlsplit(self.path)\n   157\t        q = {k: v[0] for k, v in urllib.parse.parse_qs(url.query).items()}\n   158\t        parts = [p for p in url.path.split('/') if p]\n   159\t        self._answer(lambda db: route(db, parts, q), read_only=parts in (['library'], ['thesis-bundles']))\n   160\t\n   161\t    def do_POST(self):\n   162\t        parts = [p for p in urllib.parse.urlsplit(self.path).path.split('/') if p]\n   163\t        length = int(self.headers.get('Content-Length') or 0)\n   164\t        raw = self.rfile.read(length) if length else b''\n   165\t\n   166\t        def request_body():\n   167\t            if parts != ['ideas']:\n   168\t                raise KeyError('/'.join(parts))\n   169\t            try:\n   170\t                body = json.loads(raw or b'{}')\n   171\t            except json.JSONDecodeError as error:\n   172\t                raise ValueError(f'the body is not JSON: {error}')\n   173\t            if not isinstance(body, dict) or not str(body.get('text') or '').strip():\n   174\t                raise ValueError('POST /ideas needs a JSON body with text')\n   175\t            return body\n   176\t\n   177\t        def prepare(db):\n   178\t            \"\"\"The store's date refusals, before any header (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3): a first-day store, and a date after the last\n   179\t            completed day. A malformed body or a missing configuration is answered in the stream, as before (D281).\"\"\"\n   180\t            try:\n   181\t                as_of = request_body().get('as_of') or None\n   182\t            except (KeyError, ValueError):\n   183\t                as_of = None                          # the body's own error is raised by `work`, in the stream\n   184\t            service.resolve_bound(db.ledger, as_of)\n   185\t\n   186\t        def work(db, on_progress=None):\n   187\t            body = request_body()\n   188\t            if CFG is None:\n   189\t                raise config.ConfigError('the server was started without --config, so it cannot read ideas')\n   190\t            return idea.read_idea(db.ledger, db.index, db.items, db.archive, CFG, body['text'], body.get('as_of') or None,\n   191\t                                  int(body.get('k') or 10), aliases=ALIASES, semantic=SEMANTIC, bundles=body.get('bundles', True) is not False,\n   192\t                                  on_progress=on_progress)\n   193\t        accepted = [part.split(';', 1)[0].strip() for part in self.headers.get('Accept', '').split(',')]\n   194\t        if parts == ['ideas'] and 'application/x-ndjson' in accepted:\n   195\t            self._stream_answer(work, prepare)\n   196\t        else:\n   197\t            self._answer(work)\n   198\t\n   199\tdef flag(value):\n   200\t    return str(value).lower() in ('1', 'true', 'yes')\n   201\t\n   202\t\n   203\tdef route(db, parts, q):\n   204\t    ledger, as_of = db.ledger, q.get('as_of') or None\n    27\tparser.add_argument('--transport', choices=['stdio', 'streamable-http'], default='stdio', help='stdio for a local agent; streamable-http to serve /mcp over HTTP (Docker)')\n    28\tparser.add_argument('--host', default='127.0.0.1')\n    29\tparser.add_argument('--port', type=int, default=8789)\n    30\tARGS = parser.parse_args()\n    31\tALIASES = search_module.object_aliases(ARGS.universe)\n    32\t\n    33\tfrom hivemind import idea as idea_module  # noqa: E402\n    34\t\n    35\t\n    36\t@contextlib.contextmanager\n    37\tdef connections():\n    38\t    \"\"\"One tool call's databases (live-service/OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 2): the ledger, items and index opened per call, never shared\n    39\t    between calls (a search writes the index's query cache); the ledger's committed state pinned by BEGIN and a first read; every\n    40\t    connection closed on every path, a failure while opening included.\"\"\"\n    41\t    opened = []\n    42\t    try:\n    43\t        ledger = service.open_pinned(ARGS.views)\n    44\t        opened.append(ledger)\n    45\t        index = search_module.open_index(ARGS.index)\n    46\t        opened.append(index)\n    47\t        items = store.open_read_only(ARGS.items) if os.path.exists(ARGS.items) else None\n    48\t        if items is not None:\n    49\t            opened.append(items)\n    50\t        yield ledger, items, index\n    51\t    finally:\n    52\t        if opened and opened[0].in_transaction:\n    53\t            opened[0].rollback()\n    54\t        for conn in reversed(opened):\n    80\t    'with a search engine on top. To read an idea against it: first break the idea into its parts, the one to four '\n    81\t    'questions whose answers decide it (each about one concrete quantity, date or event); search with the idea and with '\n    82\t    'each part (k=20); map each part to every view whose question answers it or whose outcome would move it, leaving out '\n    83\t    'views that only share a company or a word; then read each mapped view (state as of a day, history, evidence) and '\n    84\t    'say what the judged positions tell about each part and which parts no view covers. Say judged, never true. Every '\n    85\t    'tool takes as_of, a calendar day; the default is the ledger\\'s last completed day. Nothing here changes the ledger. '\n    86\t    'search matches each view\\'s own text (question, what it looks at, ladder conditions; Chinese, English queries work): '\n    87\t    'ask for one object and one quantity or event per query; views(object) lists everything under one object. '\n    88\t    + OBJECTS))\n    89\t\n    90\t\n    91\t@mcp.tool()\n    92\tdef thesis_library(as_of: str = '') -> dict:\n    93\t    \"\"\"All collected theses and their stored research groups, including ungrouped and closed theses.\n    94\t    Membership is not a dependency or a parent-child relationship. No model call or ledger write.\"\"\"\n    95\t    with connections() as (ledger, items, _index):\n    96\t        return bundle.library(ledger, items, as_of or None)\n    97\t\n    98\t\n    99\t@mcp.tool()\n   100\tdef thesis_bundles(view_ids: list[str], as_of: str = '') -> dict:\n   101\t    \"\"\"Complete UI inputs for selected thesis ids: dated states, assessments, sources, evidence and relationships.\n   102\t    Pass this envelope to the frontend's fromBundles adapter. Read-only; does not call a model.\"\"\"\n   103\t    with connections() as (ledger, items, _index):\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
