{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'D335|idea-summary-v8' docs/DECISIONS-log.md docs/poc/idea-card.md poc/reports -g '*.md' | cut -c1-370 | head -42; nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '3134,3152p'; rg -n 'score|core|support|noise' docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/*proof*v108* 2>/dev/null | cut -c1-280 | head -26; rg -n 'def request_for|def call' src/hivemind/jev.py; nl -ba poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js | sed -n '252,269p'; nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '318,327p;353,379p'; nl -ba docs/prd/README.md | head -29; nl -ba docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | sed -n '350,410p'\"","aggregated_output":"docs/poc/idea-card.md:5:The default is `poc/config/poc-v118-idea.json`: two candidate-discovery calls (`idea-v7`) followed by one final adoption and weighting call (`idea-summary-v8`, D290, D335). The model/provider and reasoning settings are unchanged from v33. Older configurations retain their original response contracts.\ndocs/poc/idea-card.md:34:The final assessment receives candidate theses, their dated states and endpoint conditions. It returns a variable-length list of adopted IDs, each with a positive impact percentage, endpoint and explanation. Each candidate's entry may name only that thesis's own two endpoint positions, enforced in the request schema (D335), and the answer is c\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3172:`main` and `fix/extraction-quality-2026-10-28` both numbered from D181 after D170. At the merge the branch kept its numbers (D171–D274) and the 62 decisions `main` recorded were renumbered in order: D181→D275, D182→D276, D183→D277, D184→D278, D185→D279, D186→D280, D187→D281, D188→D282, D189→D283, D190→D284, D191→D285, D192→D286, D193→D287, D\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3499:## D335 · 2026-10-30 · Each adopted thesis offers only its own two endpoints; two-rung cards show their own Yes/No\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3503:- `poc-v33-idea` / `idea-summary-v8` (prompt text identical to v7) sends one item shape per candidate, pinned to its ID and its two endpoint positions; the binder checks the answer against that same schema and then only uniqueness, non-empty text, the 100% total and the unclear-claim rule. v3–v7 keep their binders. `model.check_schema` now r\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:7490:  planner (`idea-summary-v8`) shows a new-system three-choice event as Yes and Still open, leaves out Ruled out, and its binder can\n  3134\t- Measured (`research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/design-v78-fields.md` §12; three sets, 50 stored articles, three sends each against v94's three stored draws, one round): gold matters reaching 132 → 146; gold not-kept statements reaching 95 → 89, and 71 → 56 once records whose long quote also carries a kept matter are set apart (D250 item 5). On the way, v74b (95 → 77 noise) lost a core matter in all three sends (a partner's disclosed backstop amount): my sentence on \"the results a user reports from that use\" contradicted kind 2's reported figures, and the new quote-copy wording dropped the partner figure out of the programme's record; the model's own account (`probe-v101-omitted.txt`) and two cheap re-sends located and fixed both (v74c, v74d).\n  3135\t- Status: `poc-v103` is the candidate; the default stays `poc-v94` until Alex says otherwise. Not done: the v78–v80 field code (a related party's judgement needs no scale, Codex 1) is changed only if the field route is used again. Tests: `tests/test_v74d_text.py`; suite 284.\n  3136\t\n  3137\t## D272 · 2026-11-03 · `poc-v103` (extraction v74d) is the default\n  3138\t\n  3139\t- Alex, on D271's result: \"做成默认\". `scripts/replay.py --config` defaults to `poc/config/poc-v103.json`; README, AGENTS (§9's run settings paragraph) and the entry-point test (`tests/test_concurrency.py`) name it. `poc-v94` stays as the record of D267.\n  3140\t\n  3141\t## D273 · 2026-11-03 · Second review of the extraction request: five misread sentences fixed in text (v74e), the filing structure measured three ways (v74f–v74h); none made the default\n  3142\t\n  3143\t- Alex: \"你要不要同时你和codex subagent 再深度看到底哪里还是没写对，还要进一步优化结构，给我答案\".\n  3144\t- Found (`research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/design-v78-fields.md` §13): the model's own account of seven misses under v74d (`probe-v103-omitted.txt`): \"another company's matter when you cannot say through which path\" read as \"the item does not state the path\" (a customer's backlog, a supplier's revenue: standard 5.1 kind 2's own example class); \"a second item for the same fact\" read across articles (\"item\" names both the article and an evidence record); \"dated to an earlier month\" applied to an expansion under way; a refusal still in force read as common knowledge (standard §5.3: a decision, plan or forecast still in force keeps its weight); \"rental prices for older models are climbing\" read as a typical claim (standard 5.1 lists it as new information). One reported miss was the scorer's (the Omniverse decision written in all three sends under another quote). The independent Codex review (`codex-audit-v74d-r1.md`): the role's reject list and the closing check state one rule twice with eleven differences; every numeric takes line repeats one tail, so the narrowest question cannot be told apart.\n  3145\t- Built: v74e (`poc-v104`): one reject list, owned by the closing check; the five sentences rewritten from the standard (the analyst supplies the connection; a retold plan or decision in force keeps its place; judge the action, not its tense; a market measure moving now is new; the product-progress boundary covers every product line); T8 reads calculations and specific judgements. v74f (`poc-v105`): v74e with the tail and the period allowance stated once in the links rule (`placement.takes(paths_once)`, `FILING_RULE_PATHS_ONCE`, `extraction.PATHS_ONCE_VARIANTS`). v74g (`poc-v106`): tail kept, the v74f links rule. v74h (`poc-v107`): v74f plus the company-wide revenue question as the home of indirect evidence (`FILING_RULE_ROOT_FALLBACK`). Variants keep v74's behaviour flags; `extraction.FILING_RULE_VARIANTS` names the links rule each reads. Test `tests/test_v74d_text.py::test_filing_variants_change_only_the_takes_lines_and_the_links_rule`; suite 285.\n  3146\t- Measured (50 stored articles, three sends each, one round): core presences v74d 59 → v74e 65 / v74f 64 / v74g 64 / v74h 68; supporting 87 → 122 / 70 / 93 / 95; noise 89 → 107 / 53 / 98 / 100 (56 → 83 / 38 / 69 / 64 net of long quotes). The structural finding: whether a statement is kept is decided by whether an open question takes it (D209 with D264); the total-revenue question's shared tail makes it both the only home of indirect evidence (partner adoption, supplier expansion, a country's capex plan) and the sink of noise, so a stricter filing rule removes both.\n  3147\t- Status: the default stays `poc-v103` (D272). Lean put to Alex: v74h (`poc-v107`), the most core with none missed and noise near the old default's, request 4,000 characters shorter; v74e and v74f are the two ends. The next structural lever is not in the prompt: specific homes for indirect evidence (D208's driver questions, designed, not built) would let filing be strict without losing it; the seed questions belong to the frozen ruler, so that is a new ruler version, opened only by Alex.\n  3148\t- Amended 2026-11-02 22:10, after Alex (\"可是最新的问自己啊兜底不是废话变多了吗？\" then \"收窄那三句，直接测\"): v74h's extra noise against v74d (89 → 100) came from three exceptions this review added to the closing check, not from the fallback: \"a specific consequence\" (the standard's 5.3 row lists \"a delay leaves rivals a window\" as not kept), \"a market measure moving now\" (applied to general statements), and \"a party's own revenue, capacity, orders or contracted amounts\" (let existing deals with amounts in). v74i (`poc-v108`) narrows the three to the standard's words. Measured on the same 50 articles: core 59 → 70, supporting 87 → 117, noise 89 → 81 (56 → 54 net of long quotes), no core matter missed in all three sends (three under v74d). Candidate; the default is Alex's word.\n  3149\t- Amended 2026-11-02 23:01, after Alex (\"那致癌案的核心事实不就退步了 … 找codex和你一起review 找到突破的方法\"; \"其实你也可以改成推理xhigh, max 都试试看\"): the debt-backstop article's core regression under v74i is an incomplete walk of a long item at low reasoning (some sends skip whole sections; nine sends each: the opening market judgement 7/9 at low, 9/9 at medium). Measured on the 50 articles with v74i's text: low 70 core / 112 supporting / 81 noise, medium 73 / 140 / 120, high 73 / 171 / 150; xhigh exhausts a 32,000-token budget on long items and returns empty answers; \"max\" is not a value the API accepts. Codex's section walk (v74j, low) did not stop the collapse and lowered recall. A length rule simulated at no cost (medium for items of 15,000 characters or more): 74 / 118 / 87. Not built: a reasoning setting by item length is a code change (settings are chosen by source category); Alex's decision.\n  3150\t\n  3151\t## D274 · 2026-11-03 · The extraction production prompt is frozen at v74i (`poc-v108`); the unadopted variants are retired\n  3152\t\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-collapse-r2.txt:4:   core stored raw 3 reached 3 -> new raw 3 reached 3 | For every $100 spent by U.S. AI companies, $60 is spent on Nvidia’s GPUs, Huang estimated | -/-/-:reached; -/-/-:reached; -/-/-:reached\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-collapse-r2.txt:9:      noise written x3 reached x3 [按留的规则通常不是证据：emissions touch none of ] Over the past three years, Nvidia’s supply chain emissions have more than double | -/-/-:reached; -/-/-:reached; -/-/-:reached\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-collapse-r2.txt:10:      noise written x2 reached x1 [记者的背景和框架（memory makers' expansion st] are pursuing massive expansions to meet surging chip demand, with little attenti | -/-/-:no home; -/-/-:reached\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-collapse-r2.txt:11:      noise written x2 reached x1 [按留的规则通常不是证据：Korea's power plan for a] Yongin will ultimately demand about 15 GW of electricity | -/-/-:no home; -/-/-:reached\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-collapse-r2.txt:12:      noise written x1 reached x1 [没有数字也没有决定的政治、战略表态] Greenpeace’s energy team recently warned that, instead of accelerating renewable | -/-/-:reached\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-collapse-r2.txt:13:      noise written x1 reached x0 [按留的规则通常不是证据：an ESG shareholder propo] The company recommended shareholders vote against the proposal | -/-/-:no home\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-collapse-r2.txt:16:   core stored raw 0 reached 0 -> new raw 3 reached 3 | the general market is still materially lower on shipment volumes and revenue estimates for | -/-/-:reached; -/-/-:reached; -/-/-:reached\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-collapse-r2.txt:17:   core stored raw 0 reached 0 -> new raw 1 reached 0 | Annual AI Capex – including GPUs, networking, storage and attached CPU compute as well as  | -/-/-:no home\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-collapse-r2.txt:19:   core stored raw 3 reached 3 -> new raw 3 reached 3 | Nvidia provides a take-or-pay commitment to Neoclouds – a minimum revenue guarantee on the | -/-/-:reached; -/-/-:reached; -/-/-:reached\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-collapse-r2.txt:20:   core stored raw 2 reached 2 -> new raw 3 reached 3 | Nvidia is diving even deeper, as it has started backstopping datacenter leases | -/-/-:reached; -/-/-:reached; -/-/-:reached\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-collapse-r2.txt:24:   core stored raw 3 reached 3 -> new raw 2 reached 2 | Sharon disclosed a total backstop value of $4.88B | -/-/-:reached; -/-/-:reached\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-collapse-r2.txt:33:      noise written x7 reached x7 [记者的背景和框架 (no number, no period)] Nvidia revenue is skyrocketing | -/-/-:reached; -/-/-:reached; -/-/-:reached; -/-/-:reached; -/-/-:reached; -/-/-:reached; -/-/-:reached\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-collapse-r2.txt:34:      noise written x1 reached x1 [作者的一般性风险清单和没有推导的看法] The incremental revenue from the backstop program will be significant | -/-/-:reached\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-collapse-r2.txt:35:      noise written x1 reached x1 [记者的背景和框架 (framing metaphor)] we first discussed how Nvidia was becoming the Central Bank of AI | -/-/-:reached\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-collapse-r2.txt:36:      noise written x1 reached x1 [记者的背景和框架 (lending mechanics)] They are looking for a DSCR of at least 1.3x | -/-/-:reached\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-collapse-r2.txt:40:   core stored raw 3 reached 3 -> new raw 3 reached 3 | the company denied the speculation, maintaining that its roadmap remains on track | -/-/-:reached; -/-/-:reached; -/-/-:reached\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-collapse-r2.txt:41:   core stored raw 3 reached 3 -> new raw 3 reached 3 | analysts forecasting EPS growth of 90.2% YOY to $8.69 in fiscal 2027 | -/-/-:reached; -/-/-:no home; -/-/-:reached; -/-/-:reached; -/-/-:reached; -/-/-:reached;\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-collapse-r2.txt:45:      noise written x2 reached x2 [作者的一般性风险清单和没有推导的看法] it reinforces concerns that custom silicon could gradually erode the company's p | -/-/-:reached; -/-/-:reached\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-collapse-r2.txt:50:   of the reached noise statements, those whose quote also carries a gold kept matter (a long quote, counted on both lists): stored 6 -> new 10\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-collapse-r2.txt:51:noise reaching the ledger in the new sends, by row: 7 记者的背景和框架 (no number, no period); 3 按留的规则通常不是证据：emissions touch none of the seven drivers; 3 作者的一般性风险清单和没有推导的看法; 1 记者的背景和框架（memory makers' expansion stated without\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-collapse-r2.txt:52:noise written in the new sends, by its news class and fate: - reached 18; - dropped 3\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-collapse-r1.txt:4:   core stored raw 3 reached 3 -> new raw 3 reached 3 | For every $100 spent by U.S. AI companies, $60 is spent on Nvidia’s GPUs, Huang estimated | -/-/-:reached; -/-/-:reached; -/-/-:reached\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-collapse-r1.txt:9:      noise written x3 reached x2 [按留的规则通常不是证据：emissions touch none of ] Over the past three years, Nvidia’s supply chain emissions have more than double | -/-/-:reached; -/-/-:no home; -/-/-:reached\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-collapse-r1.txt:10:      noise written x2 reached x0 [记者的背景和框架（memory makers' expansion st] are pursuing massive expansions to meet surging chip demand, with little attenti | -/-/-:no home; -/-/-:no home\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-collapse-r1.txt:11:      noise written x2 reached x0 [按留的规则通常不是证据：Korea's power plan for a] Yongin will ultimately demand about 15 GW of electricity | -/-/-:no home; -/-/-:no home\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-collapse-r1.txt:12:      noise written x2 reached x0 [按留的规则通常不是证据：an ESG shareholder propo] The company recommended shareholders vote against the proposal | -/-/-:no home; -/-/-:no home\n82:def request_for(setting, state, questions):\n   252\t      }\n   253\t    }\n   254\t    async function loadLibrary() {\n   255\t      try {\n   256\t        const response = await fetch(`${API}/library`, { signal: libraryRequest.signal });\n   257\t        if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`Service returned ${response.status}`);\n   258\t        const next = fromBundles(await response.json());\n   259\t        if (next.coverage !== 'library')\n   260\t          throw new Error('The service did not return a complete library');\n   261\t        if (libraryRequest.signal.aborted) return;\n   262\t        library.setDataset(next, { day: next.as_of }); // the supplied snapshot defines the displayed date (thesis-ui.md)\n   263\t        data = next;\n   264\t      } catch {\n   265\t        // Keep the displayed snapshot when the optional live read is unavailable.\n   266\t      }\n   267\t    }\n   268\t    form.addEventListener('submit', run);\n   269\t    input.addEventListener('input', updateSendState);\n   318\t  is unclear or the gold misreads it, and that goes to Alex before any arm counts it as noise (Alex, 2026-10-31: \"你再次重新检查尺子，看看是不是这些留下的还有歧义；然后再思考怎么降低noise\").\n   319\t- Pair every structural check with its semantic one. Run a data rule over its whole input range and on cases it was not tuned on. Weigh\n   320\t  a case by what it carries in the product, not by count.\n   321\t- A claim about a population (\"the data is clean\") rests on a code sweep of the whole population and an independent read of a fresh\n   322\t  random sample, never on the pages the author looked at.\n   323\t- Cost is priced from tokens at the published rates (`hivemind.model.PRICES`, cached input at `model.CACHED_INPUT_SHARE`), never from a\n   324\t  stored `cost_usd`; say which rates a projection uses.\n   325\t\n   326\t### 7.3 Iterating\n   327\t\n   353\t  你自己作为llm 下去看所有trace\").\n   354\t- **Small first, then one run.** A hypothesis is first validated the simplest way, on a few stored cases and a few cents, and shown to\n   355\t  work at a high level before any full analysis or stability test is built (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"don't overspend resources on wasting time.\n   356\t  We need to validate the hypothesis in a very simple way and to make sure that it works on a high level before we dive into do the full\n   357\t  analysis stability test. This is a principle you should remember\"). A day or week slice before any whole-corpus run; preflight on\n   358\t  stored data before any paid run (§5); no edit while a run is live (§9). A paid run measures a configuration; it never tries a fix.\n   359\t  Before each send, write what it can still change in the decision and which risk the cheaper check left uncovered; a replicate or\n   360\t  control that only re-measures noise or a settled comparison is not sent, and a fix is not sent before the model's own account and the\n   361\t  request locate where the decision is made (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"你跑这么多次真的有意义吗\"; \"我感觉你在为了跑而跑\"). Several fixes on one\n   362\t  base are each proved on stored data in minutes and then run together once (Alex, 2026-11-02: \"快速验证。不要drift,不要跑超级繁琐的全方位验证，先poc 改，能work,有结论，全部改动放到一起再跑完整\"; D266).\n   363\t- **One recommendation, one test.** What reaches Alex as the next step of work is one recommendation and one test of it, reached after\n   364\t  rounds of review (Claude's own, Codex's, an independent reader's) on the traces until a round finds nothing serious; never a menu of\n   365\t  arms or options, never a conclusion the next probe overturns (a choice that changes what the system does still goes to him with its\n   366\t  options and a recommendation, Authority and scope) (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"就测试一种，一次 … 你就没有自己看5轮review，能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议？\").\n   367\t  An agreed recommendation is first challenged by an independent reader on the concrete evidence behind it (\"why you give\n   368\t  recommendations for this. What did you see exactly?\"). A review round reads a rule as its author meant it; only a send shows how the\n   369\t  model applies it: before a registered test, the changed request is sent on the cases that motivated it, a few cents.\n   370\t- **A failed arm is diagnosed before the next one.** When an arm fixes its class and regresses another, write the root cause first: the\n   371\t  process error (what grew, what the small sample did not guard) and the mechanism, traced to the raw answers and the model's account,\n   372\t  never a guess stated as the cause. A small sample guards every class the change can move, not only its own. When a fix keeps moving\n   373\t  another class, the call is doing several jobs: move the rule to its owner (a field's definition sits in the schema beside the field)\n   374\t  rather than add a sentence (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"那你这些修改都是失败的呀，为什么，根因，你要检讨然后再接着尝试。我觉得你已经陷入deep loop 了\").\n   375\t  A failed step of a plan is fixed and re-run at that same step: its failures are the work list, and nothing later in the plan and no\n   376\t  substitute plan starts before it passes (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"你为什么要drift? 你现在明明还有这么多的问题要fix,你到底知不知道你要fix什么？\").\n   377\t  Before a fix is proposed, write which goal the mechanism still serves and what the product already gives for it; a measurement that\n   378\t  removes the reason a mechanism exists retires the mechanism instead of starting its repair (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"I told you to think about\n   379\t  it and you're giving me suggestions that you reject yourself\").\n     1\t# PRD index\n     2\t\n     3\tEach module has one Markdown specification. Select a module on `docs/system-design.html`, then open its PRD link. The system PRD link at the top opens the overview.\n     4\t\n     5\t| File | Module | Status |\n     6\t|---|---|---|\n     7\t| 00-system.md | System overview | Main flow defined |\n     8\t| 01-universe.md | Research universe | First version frozen; specific themes remain a draft |\n     9\t| 02-classification.md | Upstream classification | First version frozen |\n    10\t| 03-config.md | Config | First version frozen |\n    11\t| 04-dispatch.md | Dispatch | First version frozen |\n    12\t| 05-extraction.md | Extraction (read-only) | Foundation frozen; v74i prompt remains in use; separate report import retired and v117 replay not yet accepted end to end (D370) |\n    13\t| 05-extraction-standard.html | Extraction standard: ledger records, question types and opening, evidence and weight, golden set, prompt measurement | Signed (D243), open it in a browser; the one measuring standard for extraction, replacing `docs/research/2026-10-29-analyst-standard/standard.md` (D229) |\n    14\t| 05-extraction-standard-corrections.md | Dated corrections to the frozen standard page: the statements later decisions changed, read with the page and never merged into it | Three records, 2026-11-05 (D368) |\n    15\t| 06-views.md | Thesis library and matching records | Foundation frozen; group handoff and storage in the default pipeline (D165); other open items are in the PRD |\n    16\t| 07-final-verdict.md | Closing at the due day (the final verdict retired, D356) | Decided and built (D54, D356) |\n    17\t| 08-pull-mode.md | Pull mode | Decided and built (D54, D356) |\n    18\t| 09-review-pool.md | Human review pool | First version frozen; intake defined, output deferred |\n    19\t| 10-filing-phase.md | Current phase: filing that links facts the way an analyst does (in English since D368) | In progress since 2026-11-04; read before every step |\n    20\t| 11-production-experiments-from-split.md | Production experiments drawn from the failed split extraction: what to try on production, the evidence for each, and what not to repeat | Proposed 2026-11-06 (D378); each experiment opens only on Alex's word |\n    21\t\n    22\t## Maintenance rules\n    23\t\n    24\tAuthority: Alex's instructions, then `docs/DECISIONS.md`, then the PRDs and design page. If a PRD contradicts a decision, correct the PRD.\n    25\t\n    26\tAfter **every change**, reason through every module in this order: research universe → classification → Config → dispatch → extraction → thesis library → closing at the due day → pull mode → human review pool → system overview. Compare each with the decisions and ask:\n    27\t\n    28\t1. Does this change affect the module?\n    29\t2. Do its page and PRD describe the same behaviour?\n   350\t- **The Idea planner (D580, D581):** a new-system three-choice event is shown to it as Yes and Still open. The design is parked as\n   351\t  recorded input (`idea-planner/`).\n   352\t\n   353\t- **The hold lifted, arm A2 (D582, D583):** Alex's standing instruction to keep going outranks D581's hold. A2 adds D436's rule for a\n   354\t  second side of the same bet to arm A. It is negative under the rule fixed before the send.\n   355\t  - **What it fixed:** no part left unlisted and no refusal on the motivating topics (the control left parts out on 6 topics); every\n   356\t    refusal control kept.\n   357\t  - **What it broke:** it lists an event's own outcomes, and the source the answer is read from, as not judged (9 of 137 entries,\n   358\t    against 1 of 71).\n   359\t  - **The bar itself:** run against itself, the unchanged request already breaks the \"+1\" bar on 5 marks (`unlisted-parts/RESULT-A2.md`,\n   360\t    `control-vs-control.txt`).\n   361\t- **Arm A3 (D584):** A2 plus one closed-set sentence that removes, for an event only, an entry that merely restates one of its outcomes\n   362\t  (D409, D397). It was built at $0 through council rounds 78 to 93 (`unlisted-parts/DESIGN-A3.md` v11).\n   363\t  - The three arms (control, A2, A3) are sent on the same 28 topics.\n   364\t  - They are read with the existing reading and a pre-registered diagnostic one.\n   365\t  - A lead stays provisional until a trace review classes every failure above the control.\n   366\t\n   367\t- **A3 and the edge (D585, D586):** A3 is negative under its fixed rule.\n   368\t  - Two of its failing checks were measurement errors (`unlisted-parts/RESULT-A3.md`).\n   369\t  - Its real side effect: on another event it lists the Ruled-out rung's own named decision as not judged.\n   370\t  - Tuning of the not-judged list's edge stops (D391). A2 stays an unaccepted candidate.\n   371\t- **A fresh comparison of A2 (D587 to D589):** no stored topic set is held out. So the frozen first step ran on the unread week of\n   372\t  10-13 (383 articles), starting from the 10-06 week's library (`poc/data/clean-fresh-a2-2026-11-16/`).\n   373\t  - **The run:** complete, $3.45, 5 topics opened.\n   374\t  - **The populations:** population (a) has all 5. Population (b), classed blind, has 3 different matters, under the minimum of 5,\n   375\t    so the comparison gives no verdict (D589).\n   376\t  - **The council's choice (round 102):** send and read the 5 topics as registered, then close the comparison. Pooling the corpus's\n   377\t    last week was refused.\n   378\t\n   379\t- **The fresh reading (D590):** the frozen step on 5 fresh topics misses lines 2, 3 and 5 and meets line 4. A2 is better or equal,\n   380\t  with no verdict; the comparison is closed (`unlisted-parts/RESULT-FRESH-A2.md`).\n   381\t- **The due-day mark's split (D590):** Codex first readers fail D on 133 company figures with code's day, Claude on none. A D-only\n   382\t  diagnostic held all 12 class items in both families, so it is noted as a reader discrepancy and the brief is unchanged\n   383\t  (`fresh-a2/d-diagnostic/RESULT.md`).\n   384\t\n   385\t- **Ruled-out rungs that catch a postponement (D591):** in 296 frozen-step event answers there are 37 company delays on deadline\n   386\t  questions and 1 authority case (Taiwan p3). No decision settles whether \"not by the due day\" rules an event out. The step and the\n   387\t  form are unchanged, both readings are recorded, and the 38 answers are listed beside gate counts as candidates affected. The\n   388\t  question is on Alex's page (`fresh-a2/postponement/BOUNDARY-CASES.md`).\n   389\t\n   390\t- **The final-answer test's control line (D592):** an unchanged re-send stays at 4 comparable controls of 8, and delivering three\n   391\t  facts reaches at most 7. It is not pursued for the line's sake (`stage-b-controls/DESIGN-SHORTFALL.md`).\n   392\t- **The live store's operating contract (D593):** version 9 is agreed after nine council rounds for a $0 proof build on test stores\n   393\t  (`live-service/OPERATING-CONTRACT.md`). Live operation is not authorized. P1, the exception to AGENTS §9 for the product's own\n   394\t  readers, is only proposed.\n   395\t\n   396\t- **The live store's proof build (D594 to D597; nothing deployed, no service restarted):**\n   397\t  - **Slice 1:** one owner for every upper date bound. A future date is refused, and the served product store's half-processed\n   398\t    2026-08-29 is no longer returned.\n   399\t  - **Slice 2:** one pinned read transaction per API request and per MCP call, and MCP connections per call.\n   400\t  - **Slice 3:** search ranks and embeds only what a request may see.\n   401\t  - **Slice 4a:** the writer's WAL store, its stops and its orderly end.\n   402\t  - **Slice 4b (D598, corrected in D599 and D600):** one writer per store by an operating-system lock, preflight's one locked copy, the\n   403\t    snapshot route, every reader opening a store by its own path, and the writer leaving WAL mode on every exit. The\n   404\t    filesystem-full proof was run separately.\n   405\t  - The suite passes (341), and so do the new system's folders (190).\n   406\t\n   407\t**The live-store contract's proofs are all built at $0 on test stores (D594 to D603):**\n   408\t\n   409\t- the resolver;\n   410\t- pinned reads, through one opener that names the store on failure;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg --files docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop | rg 'proof-v108|frozen-v108' | head -40; rg -n 'v74i|poc-v108' docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/design-v78-fields.md | tail -21 | cut -c1-420; nl -ba src/hivemind/jev.py | sed -n '80,118p'; nl -ba docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | sed -n '407,439p'; nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '3499,3515p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/DECISION-PAGE-2026-11-16.md | sed -n '248,285p'; rg -n 'health|Alert|Monitor|def .*status' scripts/hivemind_api.py scripts/hivemind_mcp.py docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/launch_comparison.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg --files docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop | rg 'proof-v108|frozen-v108' | head -40; rg -n 'v74i|poc-v108' docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/design-v78-fields.md | tail -21 | cut -c1-420; nl -ba src/hivemind/jev.py | sed -n '80,118p'; nl -ba docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | sed -n '407,439p'; nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '3499,3515p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/DECISION-PAGE-2026-11-16.md | sed -n '248,285p'; rg -n 'health|Alert|Monitor|def .*status' scripts/hivemind_api.py scripts/hivemind_mcp.py docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/launch_comparison.py\"","aggregated_output":"docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/predictions-r9-frozen-v108.sha256\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/e2e-funnel-r9-frozen-v108.txt\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/predictions-r9-frozen-v108.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-a-mixed11.txt\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-collapse-r1.txt\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-c-noise10.txt\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-collapse-r2.txt\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-v108-b-supporting29.txt\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/question-recall-r9-frozen-v108.txt\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/score-r9-frozen-v108-d3.txt\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/score-r9-frozen-v108-d2.txt\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/score-r9-frozen-v108-d1.txt\n350:**v74i / poc-v108（22:06；Alex：\"收窄那三句，直接测\"）：** v74h 的复核三句收窄（删\"具体后果\"；\"有名字的价格、租金、交货期或订单在变\"，泛泛的\"需求仍强、产品仍受欢迎\"不算；只限\"新披露的\"数字，文中当作早已存在的交易带金额也是现成安排）。预测（发送前）：杂音 ≤ 89（不高于现默认 v74d），核心 ≥ 65，辅助 ≥ 90。没应验说明什么：杂音没降 → 多出来的不只是这三句，再逐条对；核心掉 → 收窄碰到了北京 / 四芯片 / 微软积压那几类，读原始答案。\n352:**v74i 结果（`proof-v108-*`，`sends/poc-v108-*.json`；三组 50 篇，每篇 3 次，一轮）：**\n354:| | v94 存档 | v74d 现默认 | v74h 兜底 | **v74i 三句收窄** | 预测 |\n362:v74i 对现默认三项都好：核心 +11（四芯片取消 0 → 3、北京拒绝 0 → 2、年度 AI 资本开支 0 → 2 这三件一直漏的都回来）、辅助 +30、杂音 −8。仍是一轮 3 次；核心和辅助的差距远大于抽样波动，杂音 −8 在波动之内（说\"不比现默认多\"）。\n364:**Alex（22:15）：\"那致癌案（债务兜底那篇）的核心事实不就退步了\"**：兜底那篇（2.6 万字，T8）三次发送写出的条数差很多（v74i [17, 6, 16]，v74h [13, 4, 7]，v74g [9, 3, 8]），写得少的那几次只记中段的兜底计划、跳过开头的市场判断（核心）和后面的预测；核心\"市场估计仍明显偏低\"的有无跟着条数摆。$0 普查（六个版本的存档答案）：最少一次不到最多一次一半的比例，5 千字以下 17%、5 千–1 万 26%、1–2 万 39%、2 万以上 50%。假设：低推理强度下长文章的通读不完整。**poc-v109**：v74i 不改一字，推理强度 low → medium，输出上限都到 16,000。预测：2 万字以上那篇的最少/最多比 ≥ 0.7，核心\"市场估计偏低\"≥ 2/3；三组要收 ≥ v74i 的 187，杂音不高于 v74i 的 81 + 10。没应验说明什么：仍\n366:**v74j / poc-v113（22:38；Codex 第三轮首推）：** v74i 加代码切段（约 2,500 字一段，[S1]…，原文每行不变）和复核最后一句逐段再走一遍，把通过检验但还没写的补上，推理仍 low。预测：兜底那篇最少/最多 ≥ 0.6、核心市场估计偏低≥ 8/9；三组要收 ≥ 195，杂音 ≤ 95。\n368:**poc-v114（v74k：v74i 的文字 + v74f 的严格挂题，中推理）：** 假设：推理\"中\"让通读完整（兜底那篇核心 9/9），严格挂题挡住总收入题收容的杂音。预测：要收 ≥ 200，杂音 ≤ 90。\n372:1. **兜底那篇的机制**：同一版本三次发送写出的条数差很多（v74i [17, 6, 16]），写得少的几次整段跳过开头的市场判断和后面的预测。各发 9 次：低推理\"市场估计仍明显偏低\"7/9、年度资本开支 3/9、开始为租约兜底 7/9、Sharon 48.8 亿 7/9；中推理 9/9、6/9、9/9、9/9。第一轮的 1/3 一部分是抽样，一部分是低推理通读不全。\n374:3. **推理档位**（v74i 文字不变；三组 50 篇各 3 次）：\n378:| low（poc-v108） | 70 | 112 | 81 |\n    80\t\n    81\t\n    82\tdef request_for(setting, state, questions):\n    83\t    \"\"\"The complete Jev request used both for dispatch and in-flight identity.\"\"\"\n    84\t    return {'model': setting.model, 'state': state, 'questions': questions}\n    85\t\n    86\t\n    87\tdef ask(archive, cfg, setting, state, questions, purpose, *, transport=None):\n    88\t    \"\"\"One Jev request, archived; returns model.Answer whose data is the `answers` map.\"\"\"\n    89\t    request = request_for(setting, state, questions)\n    90\t    request_json, sha = model.request_identity(request)\n    91\t    prompt_chars = len(request_json)\n    92\t    hit = archive.lookup(sha)\n    93\t    if hit:\n    94\t        call_id, answer_json, _, input_tokens, output_tokens = hit\n    95\t        return model.Answer(json.loads(answer_json), call_id, sha, True, prompt_chars, input_tokens or 0, output_tokens or 0, 0.0)\n    96\t    started = time.time()\n    97\t    response = (transport or globals()['transport'])(request)\n    98\t    seconds = round(time.time() - started, 2)\n    99\t    answers = response.get('answers') if isinstance(response, dict) else None\n   100\t    problems = validate(answers, questions)\n   101\t    usage = response.get('usage') or {} if isinstance(response, dict) else {}\n   102\t    input_tokens, output_tokens = int(usage.get('input_tokens') or 0), int(usage.get('output_tokens') or 0)\n   103\t    price_in, _ = model.PRICES.get(setting.model, (0.0, 0.0))\n   104\t    cost = round(input_tokens / 1e6 * price_in, 6)\n   105\t    call_id = archive.record(purpose=purpose, config_version=cfg.version, config_checksum=cfg.checksum, model=setting.model,\n   106\t                             request_sha256=sha if not problems else sha + ':schema:' + uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], request_json=request_json,\n   107\t                             response_json=json.dumps(response, ensure_ascii=False)[:200000], answer_json=json.dumps(answers, ensure_ascii=False) if answers is not None else None,\n   108\t                             prompt_chars=prompt_chars, input_tokens=input_tokens, output_tokens=output_tokens, cost_usd=cost,\n   109\t                             seconds=seconds, created_at=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n   110\t    if problems:\n   111\t        raise model.SchemaError('; '.join(problems[:5]))\n   112\t    return model.Answer(answers, call_id, sha, False, prompt_chars, input_tokens, output_tokens, cost)\n   407\t**The live-store contract's proofs are all built at $0 on test stores (D594 to D603):**\n   408\t\n   409\t- the resolver;\n   410\t- pinned reads, through one opener that names the store on failure;\n   411\t- visible-only search;\n   412\t- the writer's WAL store, stops, lock and end;\n   413\t- preflight's locked copy and the snapshot route;\n   414\t- serving while the built writer runs (proof 10);\n   415\t- the page's day reaching the Idea call (2f);\n   416\t- the crash, disk and busy proofs.\n   417\t\n   418\tThe suite passes (346), and so do the new system's folders (192). Nothing is deployed or restarted. P1 (the AGENTS §9 exception for\n   419\tthe product's own readers) stays only proposed, and the running service picks up the new behaviour only on a restart, which is\n   420\tAlex's.\n   421\t\n   422\t**This session's investigations, all at $0, closed with evidence (D604 to D612):**\n   423\t\n   424\t- line 5's fresh misses (D605);\n   425\t- the postponement repair, with D606's provisional reading reversed (D607);\n   426\t- the shared fiscal-year note (D608);\n   427\t- delivery of the company's own figures on the carried fortnight (D609, D610: 5 bearing statements undelivered on 3 questions, none\n   428\t  predicted to move an answer by a blind second reader);\n   429\t- a same-news comparison from established libraries (D611: underpowered, and no unread week left).\n   430\t\n   431\tThe council's reversible decisions on Alex's page are recorded in D606 and D607.\n   432\t\n   433\t**The merge test (D678–D680, 2026-11-19): closed; the registered test did not pass.** The old system opens questions, clean Step 1 reads\n   434\tand files under them, and the frozen judge answers. It ran on 70 articles × old-2 and old-3, with a hybrid arm and a control arm, for\n   435\t$2.13 ([result](research/2026-11-19-merge-council/RESULT.md)).\n   436\t- **Held:**\n   437\t  - delivery: the decisive statements reached the judge on 4/4 primary questions in both draws;\n   438\t  - talks stayed talks;\n   439\t  - both blind readers supported all 4 hybrid answers;\n  3499\t## D335 · 2026-10-30 · Each adopted thesis offers only its own two endpoints; two-rung cards show their own Yes/No\n  3500\t\n  3501\t- Alex's Idea returned `502: SchemaError: $.composite.v10.kind: 'driver' not in ['excluded']`; he asked for the root fix and then said \"改\". [Design and evidence](research/2026-10-30-idea-endpoint-choice/design.md).\n  3502\t- Mechanism: D290's array answer offered positions 1–5 to every thesis, while the binder re-checked each entry against that thesis's two endpoints (D282's per-thesis enum, kept in v5/v6). The model wrote a thesis's current-state position (its own account: \"I used v10's `judged.position` value of `2`\"). Census: 2 of 12 stored v7 answers refused, both this cause; all 35 in-range entries agree with their own reasons.\n  3503\t- `poc-v33-idea` / `idea-summary-v8` (prompt text identical to v7) sends one item shape per candidate, pinned to its ID and its two endpoint positions; the binder checks the answer against that same schema and then only uniqueness, non-empty text, the 100% total and the unclear-claim rule. v3–v7 keep their binders. `model.check_schema` now reports the closest `anyOf` option's errors.\n  3504\t- Second defect on the same path: the frontend scored two-rung theses Yes/No by position; 11 of 55 served two-rung theses list No first, so v14's \"Yes\" rendered as \"No\" in the white pill used for negative states. A Yes/No ladder now shows each rung's own label, Yes on the upper lane; the composite value is unchanged.\n  3505\t- Result: the ten valid stored v7 answers bind to identical plans; four Python mutants and one UI mutant fail their tests; the Idea (33) and UI (57) suites pass on the committed tree. The two refused requests re-sent under v8, three draws each: 6/6 valid, 29/29 entries on an endpoint agreeing with their reasons ($0.00578; two model-account probes $0.00105). Alex's Idea through the restarted service: 200, six adopted theses, 75% confidence.\n  3506\t\n  3507\t## D336 · 2026-10-30 · A yes/no ladder with named outcomes shows its outcome once\n  3508\t\n  3509\t- Alex, after the browser check showed v49's state as \"No No restriction adopted\": \"修，然后 merge main\".\n  3510\t- Mechanism: the state chip and the chart's spoken text join the score and the rung label. A two-rung ladder's score is Yes/No; when the ladder names its outcomes (06-views allows named outcomes for yes/no theme theses), the label repeats it. Census: 1 of 55 two-rung theses in the served ledger (v49: Restriction adopted / No restriction adopted) and 1 in the 2026-10-27 snapshot (Permission granted / Permission not granted).\n  3511\t- `stateWords` in `poc/ui/src/model/thesis.js` owns what a state shows: a two-rung ladder shows its own outcome once; five-rung ladders keep score and label. `badgeHtml` and `stateText` read it. Tone, lanes, the score table and the composite still use the Yes/No score.\n  3512\t- Result: the D336 UI test fails on the old composition (\"No No restriction adopted\"); 58 UI tests, lint, format and the 20 standing UI mutation checks pass. In headless Chrome, with the cache disabled, v49 shows \"No restriction adopted\" and v14 \"Yes\".\n  3513\t\n  3514\t## Decisions recorded in the `main` checkout on 2026-10-27 and never committed (numbered at the 2026-11-03 cleanup)\n  3515\t\n   248\t### 6. Running the new system live\n   249\t\n   250\t**Where it stands now (D594 to D603):** the design was resumed under D439, agreed, built and tested on test copies at no cost. Nothing\n   251\tis running live and nothing has been restarted.\n   252\t\n   253\t**What the tests show:**\n   254\t\n   255\t- While the new system writes a day, the website and the agent tools only ever show whole finished days.\n   256\t- On a brand-new database's first day, they say \"not ready yet\" instead of showing a half-done day (open defect 10 is fixed).\n   257\t- Only one writer can work on a database at a time.\n   258\t- A copy for checking is taken safely, and a crash or a full disk loses nothing that was already finished.\n   259\t\n   260\t**Example:** the test re-ran six months of one draw while asking the website for the library about 170 times. Every answer was a\n   261\twhole finished day, never part of one.\n   262\t\n   263\t**Three choices are yours:**\n   264\t\n   265\t1. **How live data is read.** Today's working rule never opens a running database directly, only a copy (AGENTS §9). The product's\n   266\t   own readers would need an exception (P1). This is proposed, not decided.\n   267\t2. **Restarting the running service.** It picks up the new behaviour only on a restart. Example: a date after the last finished day\n   268\t   would then be refused instead of answered from a half-done day.\n   269\t3. **When to adopt.** Adopting the new system at all still comes after the quality gates.\n   270\t\n   271\t**One small gap remains your choice:** if the page cannot reach the service, it quietly keeps the copy built into the page, as\n   272\tspecified. A \"collected snapshot\" note is a possible change.\n   273\t\n   274\t## What the council decided in the meantime, reversibly (D606, D607; each reversed on your word)\n   275\t\n   276\t- **The next product test** starts from a library built from real earlier material. Tests from empty stay as separate diagnostics.\n   277\t- **Your six lines** stay the gate, with their accounting unchanged.\n   278\t- **A company's formal decision that a dated event will not happen by its date** rules the event out. Example: \"NVIDIA will not ship\n   279\t  Vera Rubin in 2026\" answers \"will it ship by 2026-12-31?\" as ruled out. An authority's proceeding that goes on is still waiting.\n   280\t  This is the readers' majority view and my earlier lean; your ruling replaces it.\n   281\t- **The two product directions (D520, D571)** stay as the running product has them.\n   282\t- **Reading a live database directly (P1)** is not taken. The copy rule stays.\n   283\t\n   284\t## What is in force meanwhile\n   285\t\nscripts/hivemind_api.py:96:    def _send(self, status, payload):\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v12.md | sed -n '49,76p;97,108p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/design-v78-fields.md | sed -n '347,363p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/views/round.py | sed -n '95,157p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/replay.py | sed -n '48,92p'; rg -n 'D665|July 20|07-20' docs/DECISIONS-log.md | tail -12 | cut -c1-315; nl -ba scripts/hivemind_api.py | sed -n '255,273p'; nl -ba scripts/hivemind_mcp.py | sed -n '18,28p'; nl -ba poc/ui/src/idea/idea.js | rg -n '/ideas|function read' \"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v12.md | sed -n '49,76p;97,108p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/design-v78-fields.md | sed -n '347,363p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/views/round.py | sed -n '95,157p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/replay.py | sed -n '48,92p'; rg -n 'D665|July 20|07-20' docs/DECISIONS-log.md | tail -12 | cut -c1-315; nl -ba scripts/hivemind_api.py | sed -n '255,273p'; nl -ba scripts/hivemind_mcp.py | sed -n '18,28p'; nl -ba poc/ui/src/idea/idea.js | rg -n '/ideas|function read' \"","aggregated_output":"    49\t\n    50\t1. **The population.** The clean selection rule's articles from 07-20 to 09-20: 1,619 articles (by week: 185, 164, 62, 114, 109, 265, 218, 229,\n    51\t   273). The warm-up from 07-01 to 07-19 has 357 articles.\n    52\t2. **What counts as a read** (the closed set, frozen before any hit is read). The article's id or its text sha appears in any of:\n    53\t   - a run's trace, archive or ledger (either system);\n    54\t   - a probe;\n    55\t   - a gold or reference;\n    56\t   - a reader packet, answer or tally;\n    57\t   - a design, result or log document;\n    58\t   - a report;\n    59\t   - a test fixture, mock or UI-check data file.\n    60\t\n    61\t   **Not reads:**\n    62\t   - **documented corpus storage, by content:**\n    63\t     - `corpus-builds.json`, frozen before any hit is read, lists the documented corpus builds: the current source, `items-window.sqlite`,\n    64\t       `items-window-tags2-2026-10-24.sqlite`, the page store, and any other build the decision log or `data-manifest.md` records as a corpus.\n    65\t       Each comes with its record and its set of input ids.\n    66\t     - A table is exempt only when it is a **verified raw copy** of a listed build: the same rows, by `input_id` and `content_sha256`. That\n    67\t       covers renamed copies.\n    68\t     - Any other such table (a probe's or fixture's selection) is searched like everything else.\n    69\t     - The exemption covers stored rows only. Whatever a probe, run or fixture actually used, even from a whole-corpus copy, is a read\n    70\t       through its trace, packet or fixture text.\n    71\t     - Every other table in the same file, and every other file, is searched;\n    72\t   - the search index built over the whole corpus;\n    73\t   - this comparison's own files.\n    74\t\n    75\t   Git-ignored files are searched.\n    76\t3. **Where it is searched:**\n    97\t   - **Proof through the real entry points:** both launchers run dry with fake answers over the whole span on the copy. Each records the\n    98\t     ordered ids it actually processes and their text sha. The two must be equal in order. Controls:\n    99\t     - an excluded article appears in neither;\n   100\t     - a kept article appears in both.\n   101\t\n   102\t### 1.3 Blind matter census (articles only; frozen before any send)\n   103\t\n   104\t1. **Sample (D668).** Every kept article in the scored window 2026-08-31 to 09-20, read in batches of about 40 per session. Each family merges across every batch and week before reconciling. The warm-up is 07-01 to 08-30, unfiltered: the exclusion filter applies to the scored window only. Read with week reading A1's\n   105\t   brief (`../2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/brief-A1.md`), unchanged except for the file names.\n   106\t2. **Readers.** Codex (memories off, closed, D661) and Claude (closed command line), apart. Nine weeks × 2 families, in fresh sessions.\n   107\t3. **Merge.** One matter is one bet. Two entries are one matter only when the same outcome settles both and their answers cannot move apart.\n   108\t   Another year of a figure is another matter.\n   347\t3. 现成安排那行加的\"不包括客户、供应商、伙伴自己的收入、产能、订单、合同额\"，加上\"没日期不等于旧\"：早就有的带金额交易进来了（AMD 与 Meta 的交易、Alphabet 类似的租用、AMD 去年起的兜底）。应限定为\"新披露的\"。\n   348\t同一轮也去掉了一些（英特尔多年领先 59% −5、Valar 反应堆 −3、梅赛德斯部署 −3）。修法：三句各收窄到标准原话；没建，等 Alex。\n   349\t\n   350\t**v74i / poc-v108（22:06；Alex：\"收窄那三句，直接测\"）：** v74h 的复核三句收窄（删\"具体后果\"；\"有名字的价格、租金、交货期或订单在变\"，泛泛的\"需求仍强、产品仍受欢迎\"不算；只限\"新披露的\"数字，文中当作早已存在的交易带金额也是现成安排）。预测（发送前）：杂音 ≤ 89（不高于现默认 v74d），核心 ≥ 65，辅助 ≥ 90。没应验说明什么：杂音没降 → 多出来的不只是这三句，再逐条对；核心掉 → 收窄碰到了北京 / 四芯片 / 微软积压那几类，读原始答案。\n   351\t\n   352\t**v74i 结果（`proof-v108-*`，`sends/poc-v108-*.json`；三组 50 篇，每篇 3 次，一轮）：**\n   353\t\n   354\t| | v94 存档 | v74d 现默认 | v74h 兜底 | **v74i 三句收窄** | 预测 |\n   355\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n   356\t| 核心出现 | 60 | 59 | 68 | **70** | ≥ 65 ✓ |\n   357\t| 辅助出现 | 72 | 87 | 95 | **117** | ≥ 90 ✓ |\n   358\t| 核心三次全没到 | — | 3 | 0 | **0** | — |\n   359\t| 杂音 | 95 | 89 | 100 | **81** | ≤ 89 ✓ |\n   360\t| 杂音扣长引文 | 71 | 56 | 64 | **54** | — |\n   361\t\n   362\tv74i 对现默认三项都好：核心 +11（四芯片取消 0 → 3、北京拒绝 0 → 2、年度 AI 资本开支 0 → 2 这三件一直漏的都回来）、辅助 +30、杂音 −8。仍是一轮 3 次；核心和辅助的差距远大于抽样波动，杂音 −8 在波动之内（说\"不比现默认多\"）。\n   363\t\n    95\t\n    96\t\n    97\tdef run(conn, archive, cfg, universe, item, seq, *, resume_from=None, transport=None, log=print, extractor=None, matching_workers=1):\n    98\t    result = RoundResult(item['input_id'])\n    99\t    if resume_from in ('judged', 'handed_over'):       # written already; judging is the day's step\n   100\t        dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'handed_over', 'ok', 'resumed')\n   101\t        conn.commit()\n   102\t        return result\n   103\t    objects = [o['value'] for o in item.get('object_identifiers') or [] if universe.has(o['value'])]\n   104\t    shown = extraction.shown_views(conn, cfg, item, objects)\n   105\t    # extraction (or its stored handover on resume)\n   106\t    handover = None\n   107\t    if resume_from and resume_from != 'extracted':\n   108\t        row = conn.execute('select handover_json from handovers where input_id=? order by id desc limit 1', (item['input_id'],)).fetchone()\n   109\t        if row:\n   110\t            saved = vocabulary.extraction_answer(json.loads(row['handover_json']))          # a handover saved by a Chinese version reads in the canonical vocabulary\n   111\t            handover = extraction.Handover(saved['evidence'], saved['candidates'], saved['dropped'], 0, '', True, 0.0, saved.get('new_groups') or [])\n   112\t    if handover is None:\n   113\t        try:\n   114\t            handover = (extractor or extraction.extract)(archive, cfg, item, item['text'], shown, universe, transport=transport)\n   115\t        except Exception as error:\n   116\t            return _fail(conn, item, seq, result, 'extracted', 'extraction_failed', 'extraction: ' + repr(error), type(error).__name__)\n   117\t        result.cost += handover.cost_usd\n   118\t        result.cached_calls += int(handover.cached)\n   119\t        store.insert(conn, 'handovers', input_id=item['input_id'], seq=seq,\n   120\t                     handover_json=json.dumps({'evidence': handover.evidence, 'candidates': handover.candidates, 'dropped': handover.dropped, 'new_groups': handover.new_groups}, ensure_ascii=False))\n   121\t        dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'extracted', 'ok', f'{len(handover.evidence)} evidence, {len(handover.candidates)} candidates, {len(handover.dropped)} dropped')\n   122\t        conn.commit()\n   123\t    result.evidence, result.candidates, result.dropped = len(handover.evidence), len(handover.candidates), len(handover.dropped)\n   124\t    if not handover.evidence and not handover.candidates:\n   125\t        dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'handed_over', 'ok', 'nothing to match')\n   126\t        conn.commit()\n   127\t        return result\n   128\t    # first matching call: the candidates and the evidence linked straight to existing views\n   129\t    lists = matching.build_lists(conn, handover, shown, cfg.search_top_n)\n   130\t    checked = _match(conn, archive, cfg, universe, item, seq, result, handover.candidates, handover.evidence, lists, shown, transport=transport, workers=matching_workers)\n   131\t    if checked is None:\n   132\t        return result\n   133\t    # second call: evidence linked to candidates that attached to an existing view, compared under that view\n   134\t    second_pass = {}\n   135\t    pending = []\n   136\t    for e in handover.evidence:\n   137\t        for link in e['links']:\n   138\t            outcome = checked.outcomes.get(link)\n   139\t            if outcome and outcome[0] == 'merge':\n   140\t                pending.append((e, outcome[1]))\n   141\t    if pending:\n   142\t        lists2 = matching.Lists({}, {(e['id'], view_id): matching.rank_evidence(conn, view_id, e['one_line'], cfg.search_top_n) for e, view_id in pending})\n   143\t        evidence2, seen = [], set()\n   144\t        for e, view_id in pending:\n   145\t            if e['id'] not in seen:\n   146\t                evidence2.append(dict(e, links=[v for x, v in pending if x['id'] == e['id']]))\n   147\t                seen.add(e['id'])\n   148\t        checked2 = _match(conn, archive, cfg, universe, item, seq, result, [], evidence2, lists2, [], extra_views=sorted({v for _, v in pending}),\n   149\t                          call_offset=2, transport=transport, workers=matching_workers)\n   150\t        if checked2 is None:\n   151\t            return result\n   152\t        second_pass = checked2.evidence\n   153\t    dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'matched', 'ok', f'{len(checked.outcomes)} candidates placed')\n   154\t    # write, and record what changed in the same commit (a resume at 'judged' reads it)\n   155\t    try:\n   156\t        written = writing.write(conn, universe, seq, item, handover, checked, second_pass)\n   157\t    except Exception as error:\n    48\t        day += datetime.timedelta(days=1)\n    49\t\n    50\t\n    51\tdef run(*, testdb_path, views_path, archive, cfg, universe, from_day, until_day, day0=None, spend_cap_usd=None,\n    52\t        transport=None, log=print, only_objects=None, max_items_per_day=None, day_runner=None):\n    53\t    items_db = testdb.open_db(testdb_path)\n    54\t    conn = store.open_db(views_path)\n    55\t    refuse_unfinished_parallel(conn)\n    56\t    last_done = store.last_completed_day(conn)\n    57\t    start = from_day\n    58\t    if last_done and from_day <= last_done:\n    59\t        next_day = (datetime.date.fromisoformat(last_done) + datetime.timedelta(days=1)).isoformat()\n    60\t        if next_day > until_day:\n    61\t            raise BackdatingError(f'views database already completed {last_done}; nothing to run before it')\n    62\t        log(f'resuming after the last completed day {last_done}')\n    63\t        start = next_day\n    64\t    last_written = conn.execute('select max(publication_day) from processing_steps where sequence_no > 0').fetchone()[0]\n    65\t    if last_written and start < last_written:\n    66\t        raise BackdatingError(f'views database already holds rounds of {last_written}; a replay cannot start before it (D31)')\n    67\t    totals = {'items': 0, 'extracted': 0, 'skipped': 0, 'merged': 0, 'not_processed': 0, 'returned': 0, 'failed': 0,\n    68\t              'evidence': 0, 'new_views': 0, 'judged': 0, 'changed': 0, 'closed': 0}\n    69\t    calls_before, cost_before, *_ = archive.totals()\n    70\t    for day in calendar_days(start, until_day):\n    71\t        day_stats = {k: 0 for k in totals}\n    72\t        day_cost_before = archive.totals()[1]\n    73\t        processed = 0\n    74\t        to_run = []\n    75\t        for item in testdb.feed(items_db, day, day):\n    76\t            if item['publication_day'] > day:\n    77\t                raise LookAheadError(f'{item[\"input_id\"]} is dated {item[\"publication_day\"]}, after replay day {day}')\n    78\t            if only_objects and not any(o['value'] in only_objects for o in item['object_identifiers']):\n    79\t                continue\n    80\t            if max_items_per_day and processed >= max_items_per_day:\n    81\t                break\n    82\t            day_stats['items'] += 1\n    83\t            route = dispatch.route(conn, item, universe)\n    84\t            if route.kind != 'extract':\n    85\t                day_stats[route.kind] += 1\n    86\t                if route.kind == 'skipped':\n    87\t                    processed += 1      # written by an earlier run of this day: a restart keeps the day's item limit\n    88\t                if route.kind == 'merged':\n    89\t                    dispatch.mark(conn, item, 0, 'merged', 'ok', route.reason)\n    90\t                    conn.commit()\n    91\t                continue\n    92\t            processed += 1\n9479:     - D613's \"unread\" was a Step 1 census; this is the full census D665 asks for.\n9480:  3. **The company's own figures** (D505's list) count in N, as D665 says. Their subgroup is flagged blind at the census and printed beside\n9632:    - Codex refuses. D665 and D667 make the reviewed instruments a gate before the first send.\n9633:    - The Claude reviewer accepts under D665 (it freezes the rule, not the code that applies it), provided the rule leaves the code nothing to\n9663:  - **The criteria:** D665's verdict (a practical lead, with the hard checks) on the frozen ruler of this comparison (D667–D673), which does not\n10034:    week. Neither the council (D665–D667) nor Claude computed it (AGENTS §7.2); two days and about $145 measured a knowable result.\n10231:      the constraint that sets that ceiling. Otherwise the strongest opening fix is tested on final answers against D665's line:\n10253:  - D665's lead needs 5 net gains and at least twice as many wins as losses, which a gross count does not show.\n10258:  - then one opening change is tested on final answers against old: three paired runs, blind readers, the frozen 32 matters, D665's\n10274:## D688 · 2026-11-20 · Under D687 (council M): no credible path to a D665 lead through opening changes alone; to Alex, keep old and pause the hybrid's release line\n10296:  - The census found no credible path to a D665 lead through opening changes alone. Five gains with zero losses would pass on paper,\n10314:  - the release bar (D665) is unchanged;\n   255\t\n   256\tdef main():\n   257\t    global ALIASES, CFG, SEMANTIC\n   258\t    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n   259\t    parser.add_argument('--views', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828', 'views.sqlite'))\n   260\t    parser.add_argument('--items', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite'), help='the items database, for source titles in the idea card')\n   261\t    parser.add_argument('--index', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'service-english', 'search-index.sqlite'))\n   262\t    parser.add_argument('--archive', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'service-english', 'idea-archive.sqlite'), help='where idea model calls are archived for replay')\n   263\t    parser.add_argument('--config', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'config', 'poc-v118-idea.json'), help='the config whose idea settings name the mapping and final assessment models and prompts')\n   264\t    parser.add_argument('--universe', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'universe.json'))\n   265\t    parser.add_argument('--host', default='127.0.0.1')\n   266\t    parser.add_argument('--port', type=int, default=8788)\n   267\t    parser.add_argument('--lexical', action='store_true', help='no embedding at all (no network): search ranks by the trigram index and says mode lexical')\n   268\t    args = parser.parse_args()\n   269\t    PATHS.update(views=args.views, items=args.items, index=args.index, archive=args.archive)\n   270\t    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(args.archive)), exist_ok=True)\n   271\t    ALIASES = search.object_aliases(args.universe)\n   272\t    CFG = config.load(args.config) if args.config and os.path.exists(args.config) else None\n   273\t    SEMANTIC = not args.lexical\n    18\tfrom hivemind import bundle, search as search_module, service  # noqa: E402\n    19\tfrom hivemind.views import store  # noqa: E402\n    20\t\n    21\tparser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    22\tparser.add_argument('--views', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828', 'views.sqlite'))\n    23\tparser.add_argument('--index', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'service-english', 'search-index.sqlite'))\n    24\tparser.add_argument('--universe', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'universe.json'))\n    25\tparser.add_argument('--items', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite'))\n    26\tparser.add_argument('--lexical', action='store_true', help='no embedding at all (no network): search ranks by the trigram index and says mode lexical')\n    27\tparser.add_argument('--transport', choices=['stdio', 'streamable-http'], default='stdio', help='stdio for a local agent; streamable-http to serve /mcp over HTTP (Docker)')\n    28\tparser.add_argument('--host', default='127.0.0.1')\n1:     1\t/** The Idea card: the user's sentence read by the service (POST /ideas, docs/poc/idea-card.md, D112).\n26:    26\texport async function readIdea(api, text, { signal, asOf, onProgress = () => {} } = {}) {\n28:    28\t    const response = await fetch(`${api}/ideas`, {\n46:    46\texport async function readIdeaEvents(response, onProgress) {\n222:   222\texport async function readBundles(api, ids, asOf, { signal } = {}) {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^## D(665|668|672|676|677)'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; rg -n '\"'^## |''^'\"\\\\|.*prod' docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/idea-planner/RESULT.md | head -25; nl -ba docs/poc/pipeline-plan.md | head -17; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/launch_comparison.py | sed -n '61,85p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '302,334p'; rg -n 'def open|return_to|human_review' src/hivemind/dispatch.py src/hivemind/views/store.py | head -24; nl -ba poc/corpus/scripts/freeze_nvda_window.sh | head -34\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^## D(665|668|672|676|677)'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; rg -n '\"'^## |''^'\"\\\\|.*prod' docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/idea-planner/RESULT.md | head -25; nl -ba docs/poc/pipeline-plan.md | head -17; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/launch_comparison.py | sed -n '61,85p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '302,334p'; rg -n 'def open|return_to|human_review' src/hivemind/dispatch.py src/hivemind/views/store.py | head -24; nl -ba poc/corpus/scripts/freeze_nvda_window.sh | head -34\"","aggregated_output":"9398:## D665 · 2026-11-17 · Council (D664, Alex's \"run your council to determine\"): the six lines stop blocking release; one product comparison against the running pipeline decides readiness, its verdict written before the first send (council consensus)\n9519:## D668 · 2026-11-17 · Under D667 (council): the old replays are all reads; the scored window is 08-31 to 09-20; every kept article in it is read for the census\n9618:## D672 · 2026-11-17 · Alex's \"开始跑\" with the stage-0 freeze review: the slice goes ahead; the scorer and cards are built during the run against a rule frozen to the last choice\n10007:## D676 · 2026-11-19 · The release comparison: the new system loses for two known mechanisms; keep the old system; the outcome was computable before the run (council consensus)\n10042:## D677 · 2026-11-19 · The release comparison's goal loop is closed; the old system stays; no paid work continues (council consensus, D439/D544)\n32:## What this means\n     1\t# POC pipeline: the implementation of the design\n     2\t\n     3\tUpdated November 5, 2026. This is the working implementation overview: what each stage does in code and where it is specified. The PRDs own what each module must do, [decisions](../DECISIONS.md) own what is decided, and the [current state](../CURRENT_STATE.md) owns open defects and the next task. The original plan and the run history up to October 25 are preserved in the [historical snapshot](pipeline-plan-history-2026-10-25.zh.md); the original fifteen-task plan is `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-23-nvda-poc.md`.\n     4\t\n     5\t## What runs\n     6\t\n     7\tThe replay default is `poc/config/poc-v118.json` (D370, D374): the frozen v108 extraction, matching and judging settings without seeded questions, a separate coverage-start report reading or the unused sampling setting. Existing article-created questions remain context. An earnings release can still enter as a source item. This configuration is not yet accepted end to end.\n     8\t\n     9\t| Stage | What it does | Code | Specified in |\n    10\t|---|---|---|---|\n    11\t| Dispatch | Each item in order: three questions, a sequence number, a processing record; items before coverage start are not dispatched | `dispatch.py` | PRD 04 |\n    12\t| Extraction | One call per item reads the whole item with the questions open at the start of its day and their takes lines, and files each statement under the questions it bears on; a statement no question takes is dropped as no home (D209, D264); extraction v74i at low reasoning (D274) | `extraction.py`, `placement.py` (the takes lines and the links rule) | PRD 05 and the extraction standard |\n    13\t| Matching and writing | Jev asks each candidate's relation to the listed theses and each evidence piece's relation to its thesis's pieces (D169); the collision judge decides when a candidate collides with an open question (D190); themes are written first | `views/jev_matching.py`, `views/matching.py`, `jev.py`, `views/writing.py`, `views/groups.py` | PRD 06 |\n    14\t| Judging | Once at the end of each day, the open questions whose evidence changed, dependencies first (D63); judging-v7 reads the evidence in view (D198, D263) | `views/round.py`, `views/judging.py` | PRD 06 |\n    15\t| Pull mode | At the end of each day, every question whose due day has come closes at the rung it stands on; one never judged closes with \"no data to verify\"; nothing is re-judged (D356) | `pull.py` | PRD 08 |\n    16\t| Replay | Items advance by day with a future-input guard; a run cannot start before a completed day; the parallel day prepares extraction requests early and re-checks each at its turn (D181–D183) | `replay.py`, `parallel_day.py`, `scripts/replay.py` | D159, D183 |\n    17\t\n    61\t    root.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    62\t    ledger = root / 'ledgers' / f'{label}.json'\n    63\t    ledger.parent.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n    64\t    if not ledger.exists():\n    65\t        subprocess.run([sys.executable, BUDGET_REPLAY, '--init-ledger', ledger, '--ceiling', str(float(guard))], check=True, cwd=ROOT)\n    66\t    elif float(json.loads(ledger.read_text())['ceiling']) != float(guard):\n    67\t        raise SystemExit(f'refused: the existing ledger {ledger} has ceiling {json.loads(ledger.read_text())[\"ceiling\"]}, not {guard}')\n    68\t    argv = ['caffeinate', '-i', '-s', sys.executable, str(RUN_FRESH), 'clean' if kind == 'new' else 'prod', '--root', str(root), '--label', label,\n    69\t            '--ledger', str(ledger), '--manifest', str(DATA / 'manifest-2026-07-01-09-20.json'), '--until-day', until_day,\n    70\t            '--items', str(DATA / 'items-comparison.sqlite')]\n    71\t    if kind == 'new':\n    72\t        argv += ['--limits', str(DATA / 'comparison-limits.json'), '--ladder-variant', 'astra-frozen', '--judge-end-day', until_day,\n    73\t                 '--passes', '3']\n    74\t    if redo:\n    75\t        if len(redo) != 4 or redo[0] != '--redo' or redo[2] != '--redo-reason' or not redo[3].strip():\n    76\t            raise SystemExit('a redo is: --redo <component> --redo-reason <text>')\n    77\t        argv += list(redo)\n    78\t    log = open(root / f'{label}.launcher.log', 'a')\n    79\t    process = subprocess.Popen(argv, cwd=ROOT, stdout=log, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, start_new_session=True,\n    80\t                               env=dict(os.environ, PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE='1'))\n    81\t    (root / f'{label}.pid').write_text(f'{process.pid}\\n')\n    82\t    print(f'{label} ({kind}) launched: pid {process.pid}, ledger {ledger} (guard ${guard}), until {until_day}')\n    83\t\n    84\t\n    85\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   302\t\n   303\t    def is_theme(view_id):\n   304\t        return store.view(conn, view_id)['object_kind'] == 'theme'\n   305\t\n   306\t    pending = [v for v in topological(conn, list(changed_views) + queued_by_ledger(conn, seq)) if eligible(v)]\n   307\t    done, results = set(), []\n   308\t    while pending:\n   309\t        ready = [v for v in pending if upstream(conn, v).isdisjoint(set(pending) - {v})] or pending[:1]\n   310\t        level = [v for v in ready if is_theme(v)] or ready\n   311\t        prompts = {v: build_prompt(conn, v, version) for v in level}\n   312\t\n   313\t        def ask(view_id, note=''):\n   314\t            system, user = prompts[view_id]\n   315\t            return model.call(archive, cfg, cfg.rejudging, system, user + note, schema, 'judgement', 'judge', transport=transport)\n   316\t\n   317\t        with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=JUDGE_WORKERS) as pool_:\n   318\t            answers = dict(zip(level, pool_.map(ask, level)))\n   319\t        for view_id in level:\n   320\t            answer = answers[view_id]\n   321\t            errors = check_answer(conn, view_id, answer.data, prompts[view_id][1])\n   322\t            if errors:\n   323\t                archive.retire(answer.call_id)                 # a refused answer never answers the same request again (a resume re-samples)\n   324\t                answer = ask(view_id, retry_note(errors))\n   325\t                errors = check_answer(conn, view_id, answer.data, prompts[view_id][1])\n   326\t                if errors:\n   327\t                    archive.retire(answer.call_id)\n   328\t                    raise JudgementRefused(f'{view_id}: ' + '; '.join(errors))\n   329\t            result = _record(conn, cfg, view_id, seq, item, answer)\n   330\t            done.add(view_id)\n   331\t            results.append(result)\n   332\t            if result['changed']:\n   333\t                for dependant in queued_by_change(conn, view_id):\n   334\t                    if dependant not in done and dependant not in pending and eligible(dependant):\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:55:def open_db(path):\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:167:def open_views_with_key(conn, object_id, measure, scope_key, period_start, period_end, basis='n/a', unit='n/a', event_type=None):\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:201:def open_views(conn):\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:219:def open_read_only(path):\n     1\t#!/bin/zsh\n     2\t# Freeze the NVDA window database for the three-month run (2026-10-27): whole-page text from every raw HTML, assemble the\n     3\t# corpus for 2026-07-01..2026-10-27, relabel into a new dated database, drop the GDELT listings (harvested for six July days\n     4\t# only, so they would make those days heavier than the rest; Google News RSS is the one listing source the whole window\n     5\t# shares), then the clean checks. Nothing here touches a database a run has used.\n     6\tset -eu\n     7\texport HIVEMIND_WINDOW_START=2026-07-01\n     8\texport HIVEMIND_WINDOW_END=2026-10-27\n     9\tcd /Users/lchingen/hivemind\n    10\tS=poc/corpus/scripts; L=poc/corpus/logs\n    11\tOUT=poc/data/items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite\n    12\ttest ! -e $OUT\n    13\techo \"$(date '+%H:%M:%S') freeze start\" >> $L/backfill.log\n    14\tpython3 $S/regenerate_text.py >> $L/backfill-freeze.log 2>&1\n    15\tpython3 $S/assemble.py >> $L/backfill-assemble.log 2>&1\n    16\tpython3 $S/relabel.py --in poc/corpus/items.sqlite --out $OUT >> $L/backfill-freeze.log 2>&1\n    17\tpython3 - \"$OUT\" <<'PY'\n    18\timport sqlite3, sys\n    19\tconn = sqlite3.connect(sys.argv[1])\n    20\tn = conn.execute(\"select count(*) from items where channel='GDELT listing'\").fetchone()[0]\n    21\tconn.execute(\"delete from items where channel='GDELT listing'\"); conn.commit(); conn.execute('vacuum')\n    22\tprint('GDELT listings dropped from the frozen database:', n)\n    23\tPY\n    24\tpython3 /Users/lchingen/hivemind-admission-v12-2026-10-26/docs/research/2026-10-27-nvda-3m/check_corpus.py --db $OUT --from 2026-07-01 --until 2026-10-27 > poc/reports/items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.check.md 2>&1 || true\n    25\tpython3 $S/review.py >> $L/backfill-review.log 2>&1 || true\n    26\techo \"$(date '+%H:%M:%S') freeze done\" >> $L/backfill.log\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"agent_message","text":"**v118 is ready for historical replay. A daily production test still needs a news feed and a way to publish each finished day.** The clearest sign is that all three 82-day replays finished, while the page and agent tools still default to the August 28 library built by v34. [RUN-LOG.md:32](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-LOG.md:32) · [CURRENT_STATE.md:128](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/CURRENT_STATE.md:128)\n\n### From article to analyst\n\n- **Supply and start.** The corpus tools gather news, filings and company releases from sources including Google News, SEC EDGAR and NVIDIA, then label and clean them into an items database. An operator starts `scripts/replay.py` with explicit dates. The daily loop and dispatch checks are built. A live feed and automatic daily start are missing, and human-review handling is deferred. [corpus-plan.md:9](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/poc/corpus-plan.md:9) · [corpus README.md:6](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/corpus/README.md:6) · [replay.py:51](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/replay.py:51) · [00-system.md:149](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/00-system.md:149)\n- **Read, match, write, judge.** `extraction.py` uses the day’s starting library to propose questions and file quoted evidence, with Luna v74i at low reasoning. `views/jev_matching.py` uses Jev 1.14.0 to match questions and evidence, with Luna collision-v2 at low reasoning for close cases. `views/writing.py` writes SQLite records. At day end, `views/judging.py` uses Luna judging-v7 at medium reasoning to reassess changed questions. `pull.py` closes due questions at their current answer without another call. All are built. Earnings releases enter through the ordinary article path. [pipeline-plan.md:7](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/poc/pipeline-plan.md:7) · [poc-v118.json:6](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/config/poc-v118.json:6) · [jev.py:82](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/jev.py:82)\n- **Serve and explore.** The built page, HTTP API and MCP expose dated questions, evidence and answer history. Search can use `text-embedding-3-small` or lexical mode. HTTP `POST /ideas` calls `idea.py` for two Luna discovery calls with reasoning off, then one low-reasoning call to select and weight theses. The page keeps its embedded snapshot if the API is unavailable. [service.md:17](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/poc/service.md:17) · [hivemind_api.py:186](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/hivemind_api.py:186) · [hivemind_mcp.py:92](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/hivemind_mcp.py:92) · [search.py:24](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/search.py:24) · [poc-v118-idea.json:86](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/config/poc-v118-idea.json:86) · [bootstrap.js:254](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:254)\n\n### Measured performance\n\n- **Frozen reference.** The inherited v74i prompt recorded 187 helpful and 81 unhelpful appearances across 50 articles sent three times. For unseeded v118, the July 1–14 diagnostic found one settled agreement out of seven graded questions in each of three draws, or two each if disputed matches count. Every eligible answer agreed. The full frozen judgement score requires preset questions. [Extraction results:352](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/design-v78-fields.md:352) · [July census:21](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/CENSUS-FULL-RESULT.md:21) · [score_judgement.py:38](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/score_judgement.py:38)\n- **Release comparison.** v118 gave a supported answer to 10 of 32 matters in at least two of three draws, under both readings of disputed cases. The matters came from August 31–September 20. The comparison remained diagnostic after the sixth draw was stopped. [RUN-PLAN-v12.md:102](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v12.md:102) · [RUN-LOG.md:124](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-LOG.md:124)\n- **Operations.** Each July 1–September 20 NVIDIA draw extracted 1,884 articles in about 2h45m. They opened 47, 43 and 49 questions. Archived tokens price to **$7.40, $6.72 and $6.85**, about **$0.08–$0.09 per replay day**. Judgement checks refused 1, 4 and 2 answers respectively. All recovered, with zero terminal failures. Live delivery latency, a second company and v118 beyond 82 days remain unverified in the records reviewed. [Run logs: draw 1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/replay.log:83) · [draw 2](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/replay.log:83) · [draw 3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-3/prod/replay.log:83) · [Token rates](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:32)\n\n### Production-test blockers, ranked\n\n1. **Missing — daily supply and start.** Engineering must connect the feed and schedule. Alex chooses the sources, tester access and acceptable freshness. [00-system.md:18](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/00-system.md:18) · [replay.py:51](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/replay.py:51)\n2. **Partial — publish finished days.** Snapshot tooling and readers exist. Engineering must wire the finished v118 ledger and its matching articles into all surfaces. Alex authorizes the pilot service. [snapshot_store.py:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/snapshot_store.py:1) · [README.md:103](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/README.md:103)\n3. **Partial — spend and monitoring.** Research has pre-call guards and monitoring. The default cap can overshoot. Engineering must wire spend, stale-data and failed-day alerts into the pilot. Alex sets the ceiling. [README.md:170](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/README.md:170) · [RUN-PLAN-v12.md:309](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v12.md:309)\n\n**NOT READY — shortest path:** Wire those three pieces, then run one private seven-day NVIDIA pilot from a library built by v118. Verify that the page, API, MCP and an Idea show the same completed day, and that a failed run leaves the last good copy available and raises an alert. Historical usage implies about $0.60 for seven replay days. I propose a $5 model ceiling with room for growth and Idea calls. Feed and hosting costs are unpriced. [D690](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10360)"}}
